PVD("malaysia_ndp_2016-2020",{"docs":["","Malaysia NDP 2016 20"],"s":{"1":[[1,"227","4","Downstream Oil and Gas Refining Expansion","Strategy E3: Enabling growth in the oil and gas subsector in downstream oil and gas refining, introducing third party access regulation to allow new entrants into the gas business and implementing clean fuels in the transport sector;",""],[1,"227","4","Third-Party Access Regulation for Gas Market Entry","Strategy E3: Enabling growth in the oil and gas subsector in downstream oil and gas refining, introducing third party access regulation to allow new entrants into the gas business and implementing clean fuels in the transport sector;",""],[1,"228","6","Refinery and Petrochemical Integrated Development (RAPID)","The Refinery and Petrochemical Integrated Development (RAPID) within PIPC is a major development that will add 300,000 bpd of oil refining capacity in Malaysia during the Eleventh Plan.",""],[1,"228","6","Supporting Infrastructure for RAPID","The Government will provide support to construct essential infrastructure such as roads, drainage, and utilities for this development.",""],[1,"228","6","Additional PIPC Investment Mobilisation","Another investment in PIPC will be secured by the Johor Petroleum Development Corporation during the Eleventh Plan to complement existing investments by DIALOG-Vopak and PETRONAS.",""],[1,"228","7","Gas Supply Market Liberalization through Amended Gas Supply Act","Third party gas players will be able to utilise gas supply infrastructure through the enforcement of the amended Gas Supply Act, 1993 (Act 501) in 2016.",""],[1,"254","9","Oil and Gas Hub Development and Upstream Capability Strengthening","Develop Malaysia as an oil and gas hub in the Asia Pacific region through strengthening upstream capability, and improve collaboration between industry and higher learning institutions",""],[1,"255","1","Oil and Gas Services Industry Development Programme","The development of the oil and gas services industry (OGSI) will be enhanced further towards Malaysia's aspiration of becoming an oil and gas services hub in Asia Pacific.",""],[1,"255","1","Industry Centre of Excellence Establishment","The establishment of Industry Centre of Excellence (ICoE) will foster stronger collaboration between industry and institutions of higher learning in identifying technology needs, enhancing manpower development, and promoting local technologies overseas.",""]],"2":[[1,"278","1","Public Service Delivery Reform","An important part of addressing these challenges requires adapting to new models of service delivery that are better suited to today's technologies, norms and citizen needs.",""],[1,"278","1","Public Sector Modernization and Efficiency Reform","This will also require the public sector to be leaner, facilitative, more efficient, more productive, more skilled, more open, more innovative, and less bureaucratic, in order to better deliver for the rakyat and for Malaysia.",""],[1,"279","1","Digital and Online Government Services Expansion","expanding digital and online government services for the rakyat.",""],[1,"279","2","Public Service Delivery Improvement Programme","Service delivery will be further enhanced and executed with speed and accuracy through innovative and creative approaches while upholding integrity.",""],[1,"279","2","Public Sector Institutional Rationalisation and Rightsizing","It covers the rationalising of public sector institutions, rightsizing of the public service, and introducing exit policy for non-performers, as well as enhancing talent management and competency building.",""],[1,"282","1","Whole-of-Government Service Delivery Approach","During the Tenth Plan, the Government embarked on efforts to adopt a whole-of- government approach in delivering services.",""],[1,"284","9","1MOCC Integrated Government Customer Service Centre","1MOCC provides a seamless approach to customer service, offers low call rates for the public, and enables cost savings through a centralised, efficient and accurate communication system.",""],[1,"284","10","Citizen Engagement for Public Service Delivery Improvement","Transparency and efficiency of public service delivery can be enhanced through more effective engagements with citizens to understand their preferences and needs, as well as through better coordination or data sharing among and within agencies.",""],[1,"284","10","Public Awareness and Service Channel Information Campaign","There is also room for improvement in public perception and public awareness of available services and delivery channels.",""],[1,"287","10","Comprehensive Institutional and Agency Audit","Conducting a comprehensive audit across institutions and agencies",""],[1,"288","1","Citizen-Centric Public Service Reform","In the Eleventh Plan, the Government will become more citizen- centric and focus on enhancing productivity and efficiency of the public service.",""],[1,"288","2","Public Sector Service Delivery Innovation Initiative","The public sector will introduce several creative and innovative approaches to enhance the quality of its delivery system.",""],[1,"288","2","Citizen-Centric Public Service Reform","The focus will be on creating a more citizen-centric government to enhance the efficiency and productivity of the public service.",""],[1,"288","3","Participatory Governance and Service Delivery Reform","The Government will introduce several transformative changes as shown in Exhibit 9-2.",""],[1,"288","4","Whole-of-Government Service Delivery Reform","The Government will shift away from the traditional approach of agency-based service delivery towards a whole-of-government approach based on services and information that adopts the perspective of the rakyat and puts them at the centre.",""],[1,"290","1","Strengthening of MAMPU for Service Delivery Modernisation","the role of the Malaysian Administrative Modernisation and Management Planning Unit (MAMPU) will be strengthened to spearhead the implementation of initiatives to enhance service delivery.",""],[1,"290","2","Reduction of Public Service Bureaucracy and Non-Core Services","Strategy A1: Reducing public service bureaucracy and non- core services.",""],[1,"290","3","Frontline Service Delivery Process Improvement","Key initiatives include improving work processes in the frontline, enhancing trade facilitation mechanisms, adopting green practices, and introducing alternative service delivery mechanisms;",""],[1,"290","3","Alternative Service Delivery Mechanisms","Key initiatives include improving work processes in the frontline, enhancing trade facilitation mechanisms, adopting green practices, and introducing alternative service delivery mechanisms;",""],[1,"290","5","Expansion of Online Services and Community Transformation Centres","This will involve measures to increase and encourage the use of online services and Urban, Rural, and Mobile Community Transformation Centres, as well as to enhance citizen engagement in co-creating service solutions;",""],[1,"290","7","Review and Streamline Bureaucratic Procedures","Work processes and procedures will be reviewed to identify and eliminate unnecessary bureaucratic processes such as approvals for licences and permits as well as rules and regulations, which are not in line with current needs.",""],[1,"290","9","Privatisation and Outsourcing of Non-Core Government Services","The Government will systematically reduce ownership and control of selected non-core services through privatisation and outsourcing.",""],[1,"293","2","Community Engagement Framework for Public Sector Co-creation","A community engagement framework will be established to enable the co-creation2 of public sector solutions where frontline agencies gather feedback through crowdsourcing3 platforms.",""],[1,"294","1","Government Institution Rationalisation","Efforts to transform the public service will be continued through the rationalisation of government institutions.",""],[1,"294","2","Public Sector Institutional Realignment and Streamlining","Strategy B1: Realigning public sector institutions and reducing overlapping roles to streamline functions, manpower and funding to better align with changes in the economic structure;",""],[1,"294","6","Public Sector Rationalisation and Institutional Review","Public sector institutions will be rationalised in line with changes in the structure of the economy and national demographics.",""],[1,"303","1","Whole-of-Government Public Service Transformation","In the Eleventh Plan, the government will become more citizen-centric and focus on enhancing productivity of the public service through a whole-of-government approach supported by a lean and agile structure, competent talent, effective delivery of projects, and efficient services of the local authority.",""],[1,"303","1","Modernized Public Service Delivery Models","Ministries and agencies will adapt to new models of service delivery better suited to today's technologies, norms, and expectations of the rakyat.",""],[1,"303","1","Public Service Innovation and Process Simplification","Public service will be comprehensively transformed, rigid structures and redundant processes will be removed; innovation and openness will be encouraged; and responsiveness and pace of delivery will be accelerated.",""]],"3":[[1,"279","2","Public Service Talent Management and Competency Building","It covers the rationalising of public sector institutions, rightsizing of the public service, and introducing exit policy for non-performers, as well as enhancing talent management and competency building.",""],[1,"284","10","Public Awareness and Service Channel Information Campaign","There is also room for improvement in public perception and public awareness of available services and delivery channels.",""],[1,"284","10","Public Service Talent Management Reform","Talent management in the public service can be enhanced with more flexible working arrangements, a performance-based reward system as well as more relevant and outcome-focused training opportunities.",""],[1,"294","3","Public Service Restructuring and Productivity Reform","Rightsizing the public service for better productivity and capabilities through restructuring and delayering, multi-skilling in the public service, extending self- regulation, as well as introducing new practices and productivity- based KPIs;",""],[1,"294","4","Public Service Exit Policy for Underperformers","Introducing exit policy for underperformers to create greater accountability and improve overall performance within the public service.",""],[1,"295","1","Public Service Restructuring and Empowerment Reform","The public service will be restructured with a focus on better capabilities and greater productivity.",""],[1,"295","2","Public Service Upskilling and Reskilling for Multi-skilling","The Government will undertake and intensify the upskilling and reskilling of the support group in the public service to become multi- skilled.",""],[1,"295","3","Progressive Shift to Self-Regulation and Co-Regulation","the Government will progressively move towards self-regulation or co-regulation where it is suitable, such as in telecommunications, education, and consumer- related areas.",""],[1,"295","5","Public Sector Productivity Enhancement","public sector institutions will leverage guidelines and practices from the Malaysia Productivity Corporation (MPC) on productivity enhancements, and yardsticks for productivity measurement will be embedded into the KPIs of ministries and agencies.",""],[1,"295","6","Public Sector Exit Policy for Underperformers","an exit policy for underperformers will be introduced.",""],[1,"296","1","Public Sector Talent Management and Leadership Strengthening","The public sector will strengthen its talent management, capabilities, and leadership to enable quality improvement in service delivery.",""],[1,"296","2","Contractual Appointment of Top Talent in Critical Fields","Appointment on a contractual basis to secure top talent in critical fields with flexible pay structures and outcome- based KPIs;",""],[1,"296","4","Ministry Talent Management Customization","Empowering ministries to customise talent management through a bottom-up approach in talent development and performance evaluation;",""],[1,"296","5","Public Sector Training Upgrading Initiative","Strategy C4: Upgrading public sector training to improve relevance and impact with a focus on leadership skills and functional specialisation.",""],[1,"296","7","Contractual Appointment and Flexible Pay Reform for Specialized Public Sector Talent","Appointments to appropriate positions will be on a contractual basis to attract and retain talent in specialised and critical fields.",""],[1,"296","9","Public Service Work-Life Balance Flexibility Measures","The Government will improve existing work arrangements for better work-life balance by providing greater flexibility in the public service.",""],[1,"296","10","Flexible Work Arrangement Scheme","Flexible work arrangement schemes, which will allow working from home, flexible working time and compressed working hours4 .",""],[1,"296","11","Part-Time Worker Scheme for Public Service Employees","Part-time worker scheme that will retain expertise and minimise new recruitment.",""],[1,"296","12","Compressed Working Hours for Public Servants","Compressed working hours will allow public servants to work a 40-hour work week in less than five work days.",""],[1,"297","1","Bottom-Up Talent Development Programme Governance Reform","A bottom-up approach will be institutionalised to reduce centralised management of talent development programmes.",""],[1,"297","2","Decentralized Public Sector Performance Evaluation and Incentive Reform","Public sector institutions will be empowered to customise performance evaluation based on the roles and functions of the agency, in addition to the standard appraisal system.",""],[1,"297","5","Public Sector Leadership Capacity Enhancement","The capacity and capabilities of the National Institute of Public Administration (INTAN) and Razak School of Government (RSOG) in developing public sector leaders will be enhanced.",""],[1,"297","7","Public Sector Training Policy Review and Revision","Public sector training policies will be reviewed and revised to focus on outcomes that will benefit both the individual and their organisation.",""],[1,"297","7","Public Sector Capability Building and Multi-Skilling Programme","more capability building will also be provided to encourage multi-skilling, as well as more targeted training opportunities in new and specialised fields relevant for the new economy, such as data science, forensic economics and accounting, green auditing, and intellectual property evaluation.",""],[1,"297","9","Public Sector Training Institute Streamlining","The role of public sector training institutes will be streamlined to focus on areas of specialisation and to better support relevant functional roles.",""]],"5":[[1,"290","6","Integrity and Anti-Corruption Strengthening Measures","Continuous efforts will be undertaken to uphold integrity, eradicate corruption, implement outcome-based budgeting (OBB), and instil noble values among public servants.",""],[1,"293","4","Integrity and Anti-Corruption Efforts","Continuous efforts to uphold integrity and eradicate corruption will be undertaken.",""],[1,"293","5","Government Procurement Transparency Portal","Publishing government procurements through MyProcurement portal to enhance transparency;",""],[1,"293","7","Review of the Malaysian Anti-Corruption Commission Act","Reviewing the Malaysian Anti-Corruption Commission Act to further boost efforts to eradicate corruption;",""],[1,"293","8","Certified Integrity Officer Participation in Project Implementation","Ensuring the participation of Certified Integrity Officers (CelO) throughout the whole process of project implementation;",""],[1,"293","9","Corporate Integrity Pledge Implementation with Private Sector","Focusing on further implementation of the Corporate Integrity Pledge (CIP) with the private sector in executing corruption prevention initiatives;",""],[1,"293","15","Public Service Values and Ethics Strengthening Initiative","the public service will intensify efforts to instil noble values among public servants.","Public Service Department (PSD)"]],"6":[[1,"279","2","Public Sector Project Management and Implementation Strengthening","The emphasis is also on improving project management and implementation by public sector institutions, as well as capitalising on local authority with greater empowerment, more stakeholder engagement, and stronger business or community partnerships.",""],[1,"284","10","Public Sector Project Implementation Strengthening","Project implementation by the public sector can also be improved with greater engagement with relevant stakeholders, stronger monitoring, as well as enhanced planning and execution capabilities.",""],[1,"287","11","Public Sector Comparator Establishment","Establishing a public sector comparator (PSC)",""],[1,"298","1","Public Sector Project Execution Capability Strengthening","The Eleventh Plan will place emphasis on efficient and effective project management and implementation to ensure the completion of projects within the stipulated time, quality and cost requirements.",""],[1,"298","1","Project Management and Implementation Improvements","Improvements in project management and implementation will be undertaken at all stages of planning, implementation, monitoring, and evaluation.",""],[1,"298","2","Project Planning Strengthening","Strategy D1: Strengthening project planning at all levels and stages, including stakeholder engagement, resource allocation and project selection;",""],[1,"298","3","Pre-approved Plans and Project Management Efficiency Reform","Strategy D2: Enhancing implementation efficiency through pre- approved plans (PAP) for construction, competent contractors and consultants, as well as effective project management;",""],[1,"298","7","Stakeholder Engagement Requirement for Project Approval","Stakeholder engagement is crucial for the successful implementation of projects and will be made a prerequisite for project approval.",""],[1,"298","10","Shadow Ceiling for Rolling Plan Project Expenditure","The rolling plan approach, which was introduced in the previous Plan will be enhanced through the introduction of a shadow ceiling.",""],[1,"298","11","Creativity Index for Project Prioritization","During the Eleventh Plan, the Creativity Index (CI) will be introduced to assist ministries and agencies to assess the potential impact and prioritise proposed projects.",""],[1,"298","11","Public Sector Comparator for Project Evaluation","steps will be undertaken to establish a public sector comparator (PSC) as part of the project evaluation and selection process.",""],[1,"298","12","Project Brief Enhancement in the Project Monitoring System","The Project Brief in the Project Monitoring System (SPPII) will be enhanced to include comprehensive data for effective project analysis,",""],[1,"299","2","Use of Pre-approved Plans for Government Building Construction","Increasing the use of pre-approved plans for construction of government buildings",""],[1,"299","3","Standardized Public Building Design Package","The PAP, which consist of a complete set of architectural, structural, mechanical, and electrical design drawings, but without the site-related design components like earthworks and foundations, will be used to expedite the construction of Government buildings and facilities such as schools, health clinics, fire stations, police stations, government offices, and quarters.","Public Works Department"],[1,"299","4","Competent Contractors and Consultants Appointment Measure","Ensuring appointment of competent contractors and consultants",""],[1,"299","5","Contractor Training and Rating Programme","The Government will encourage contractors undertaking projects to undergo the Construction Industry Development Board's training and development programmes to enhance their competency and capability.",""],[1,"299","8","Technical Agency Process Review and Skills Upgrading","Reviewing work processes and systems as well as upgrading technical skills and competencies of personnel in technical agencies to enhance their roles in the management and implementation of government projects;",""],[1,"299","9","Dedicated Project Teams for Project Supervision and Monitoring","Establishing dedicated project teams in ministries and agencies to enhance supervision and monitoring of projects to ensure timely completion;",""],[1,"299","10","Capacity Building for Policy Planning and Development Divisions","Enhancing the capabilities of the policy planning and development divisions in ministries and agencies to ensure cost effective and timely implementation of projects;",""],[1,"299","11","Integrated Public Project Management Training Programme","Creating a pool of project management personnel through the Certificate in Integrated Public Project Management training programme conducted by INTAN;","INTAN"],[1,"299","12","Centralised Programme and Project Coordination and Implementation","Strengthening the centralised coordination and implementation of programmes and projects to ensure that citizens benefit from implementation outputs and outcomes;",""],[1,"299","13","Inter-Ministerial Resource Sharing for Project Cost Reduction","Sharing of resources between ministries and agencies to reduce project cost.",""]],"7":[[1,"24","5","Macroeconomic Stability and Fiscal Management Measures","Malaysia's economic fundamentals will be strengthened to achieve sustainable growth by ensuring stable prices and exchange rates, and an adequate level of savings as a source of investible resources.",""],[1,"39","1","Monetary and Fiscal Stability Policy Package","Monetary and fiscal policies will be implemented to ensure stable prices, exchange rates, and interest rates.",""],[1,"39","1","Tax Base Strengthening and Development Allocation Reform","The Federal Government will balance its fiscal position by 2020 by strengthening the tax base and improving the decision-making process of development allocation for proposed programmes or projects.",""],[1,"60","5","Accommodative Monetary Policy and Administrative Price Stability Measures","Accommodative monetary policy and administrative measures will continue to ensure price stability.",""]],"8":[[1,"95","2","Bumiputera High-Skills Training and Certified Professionals Programme","Strategy E1: Empowering Bumiputera human capital by expanding high-skills training and certified professionals programmes;",""],[1,"95","6","Integrated Bumiputera Programme Delivery Database","Strengthening delivery effectiveness of Bumiputera-oriented programmes by setting up an integrated database comprising Bumiputera socio-economic status, simplifying Government procedures to reduce the cost of doing business and ensuring collaboration across all relevant agencies and the private sector to deliver programmes effectively.",""],[1,"95","7","Expansion of Employment Insertion and Skills Programmes for Bumiputera","Successful employment insertion programmes such as the Program Peneraju Skil under YPPB will be expanded to improve skills of the Bumiputera.",""],[1,"95","7","Industry-Training Collaboration Incentive Scheme","Industry players in high impact sectors will play a prominent role through collaboration with training institutions in tailoring their modules to industry needs.",""],[1,"98","5","Bumiputera Economic Empowerment Coordination and Monitoring System","A comprehensive approach will be implemented through the creation of realistic and practical KPIs as well as an integrated database that comprises statistics on Bumiputera socio-economic status.",""],[1,"98","5","Strengthening of Bumiputera Economic Development Units","The roles and functions of Bumiputera-based EDOs will be reviewed and Unit Pemerkasaan Ekonomi Bumiputera (UPEB) in each ministry and agency will be strengthened through appropriate redeployment of human capital and resource allocation.",""],[1,"98","5","Government Procedure Simplification for Bumiputera Entrepreneurs","Government procedures will also be simplified to reduce the cost of doing business to enable Bumiputera entrepreneurs to be more competitive.",""],[1,"98","5","BEC Multi-Stakeholder Collaboration Mechanism","Public agencies, GLCs and GLICs, Bumiputera non-governmental organisations as well as relevant business associations will collaborate in a symbiotic relationship to develop BEC.",""]],"9":[[1,"300","1","Local Authority Capacity and Capability Building","The Eleventh Plan aims to improve the delivery of services at the local level by building the capacity and capabilities of the local authorities.",""],[1,"300","2","Local Authority Accountability and Capability Assessment","Strategy E1: Empowering and improving accountability of local authorities through better assessment of their capabilities and expectations of the local communities;",""],[1,"300","3","Local Authority Service Delivery Strengthening","Strategy E2: Strengthening service delivery by local authorities through greater collaboration with federal and state governments, and streamlining of rules and processes that can enhance local authority responsiveness;",""],[1,"300","6","Local Authority Accountability and Enforcement Strengthening","Strategy E1 Empowering and improving accountability of local authorities Strengthening enforcement at the local level",""],[1,"300","7","Strengthened Regulatory Enforcement Coordination","Enforcement will be strengthened through greater collaboration with relevant agencies such as the police, immigration and district offices to ensure compliance to regulations.",""],[1,"300","7","Local Authority Revenue Collection Efficiency Improvement","Efficiency of revenue collection by local authorities will also be enhanced.",""],[1,"300","7","Review of Enforcement By-laws and Procedures","In addition, by-laws, guidelines, and standard operating procedures will be reviewed to streamline enforcement activities.",""],[1,"300","11","Local Authority Capability and Capacity Ranking System","Local authorities will be ranked according to their capability and capacity in delivering services.",""],[1,"301","4","Local Authority Service Delivery Improvement","Efforts will be continued to enhance the delivery of local authority services through improvement in work systems and processes.",""]],"10":[[1,"169","9","National Crisis and Disaster Management Centre","National crisis and disaster management centre to enhance capacity for disaster preparedness and response",""],[1,"170","4","Comprehensive Disaster Risk Management Approach","A comprehensive disaster risk management approach will be put in place to respond to the increased frequency and intensity of climate- related disasters, with an important reorientation from a cost to an investment for the future.",""],[1,"172","7","National Crisis and Disaster Management Centre","The institutional framework will be strengthened with the establishment of a national crisis and disaster management centre, national climate change centre, national committee on sustainable waste management, and national chemical management board through the restructuring and deployment of talent from existing agencies.",""],[1,"172","7","National Climate Change Centre","The institutional framework will be strengthened with the establishment of a national crisis and disaster management centre, national climate change centre, national committee on sustainable waste management, and national chemical management board through the restructuring and deployment of talent from existing agencies.",""],[1,"172","7","National Committee on Sustainable Waste Management","The institutional framework will be strengthened with the establishment of a national crisis and disaster management centre, national climate change centre, national committee on sustainable waste management, and national chemical management board through the restructuring and deployment of talent from existing agencies.",""],[1,"172","7","National Chemical Management Board","The institutional framework will be strengthened with the establishment of a national crisis and disaster management centre, national climate change centre, national committee on sustainable waste management, and national chemical management board through the restructuring and deployment of talent from existing agencies.",""],[1,"172","7","Inter-Ministerial and Federal-State Coordination for Green Growth","Coordination and collaboration among relevant ministries and agencies, particularly at the federal and state levels, will also be strengthened to achieve green growth and better resource management.",""],[1,"184","1","Comprehensive Disaster Risk Management Framework","Planning and preparing for natural disasters, identifying which areas and communities are at risk and providing the right tools in case such situations occur will be important in preparing a comprehensive disaster risk management (DRM) framework.",""],[1,"184","3","Disaster Risk Management Policy and Institutional Framework","Strengthening disaster risk management by establishing DRM policy and institutional framework, improving disaster detection and response capacity, incorporating DRM into development plans and creating community awareness;",""],[1,"184","3","Mainstreaming DRM into Development Plans","Strengthening disaster risk management by establishing DRM policy and institutional framework, improving disaster detection and response capacity, incorporating DRM into development plans and creating community awareness;",""],[1,"184","5","National Climate Change Adaptation Plan Development","Enhancing climate change adaptation by developing a national adaptation plan, and strengthening resilience of infrastructure, natural buffers including water and agriculture sector as well as creating awareness on health impact.",""],[1,"184","7","National Disaster Risk Management Policy and Legislative Reform","The Government will strengthen the policy, regulatory and institutional framework of DRM under the National Security Council (Majlis Keselamatan Negara, MKN).",""],[1,"184","7","National DRM Policy and Related Legislation Development","A comprehensive national DRM policy and its related legislation will be formulated, and relevant standard operating procedures will be revised.",""],[1,"184","7","National Crisis and Disaster Management Centre","Concurrently, a national crisis and disaster management centre will be established as the main training centre in Malaysia to conduct training programmes and drills.",""],[1,"184","7","Multi-Stakeholder Disaster Risk Management Engagement Platform","It will also act as a platform for greater engagement with stakeholders such as DRM related agencies, the private sector, academia, civil society organisations and the rakyat.",""],[1,"184","7","Coordinated and Integrated Disaster Management Approach","MKN will play a critical role in ensuring a more coordinated, integrated and interconnected approach to managing disasters.",""],[1,"185","1","Disaster Risk Management Coordination and Collaboration Strengthening","the Government will continue to strengthen coordination and collaboration among disaster- related agencies at the federal, state and district levels, including on issues regarding deployment of resources and assets to ensure faster response.",""],[1,"185","3","Disaster Risk Management Reorientation and Climate-Responsive Development Planning","DRM will be reoriented from a cost to an investment and as a prerequisite for cities and infrastructure.",""],[1,"187","2","Climate Change Adaptation Measures","Climate change adaptation measures will be enhanced to minimise the impact of increasingly frequent and severe extreme weather events.",""],[1,"187","3","National Climate Change Adaptation Plan","NRE will develop a national climate change adaptation plan to provide a coherent framework as well as coordinate and synergise adaptation efforts across relevant ministries and agencies.","NRE"]],"11":[[1,"236","1","SME Strengthening Programme","Small and medium enterprises (SMEs) will continue to be strengthened to increase their share in terms of Gross Domestic Product (GDP) and exports.",""],[1,"245","10","SME Masterplan Implementation and Coordination Strengthening","The role of SME Corporation Malaysia (SME Corp.) was also strengthened and the coordination mechanism steamlined to enable the Master Plan to be implemented effectively.",""],[1,"264","1","Resilient and Sustainable SME Development","The Eleventh Plan will focus on developing resilient and sustainable SMEs to achieve inclusive and balanced growth.",""],[1,"264","8","SME Development Support in Sabah and Sarawak","Strategy E6: Developing SMEs in Sabah and Sarawak by strengthening infrastructure, encouraging market expansion through e-commerce, reducing the cost of doing business, and increasing outreach of government assistance.",""],[1,"265","1","SME Proposal Preparation Advisory Support","For better access to financing, SMEs are encouraged to engage industry experts when preparing proposals, particularly for technology and innovation activities.",""],[1,"265","1","SME Investment Partner Financing Programme","The SME Investment Partner (SIP) programme will also introduce new ways of financing for early stage companies by combining equity and loan financing features and providing up to 100% margin of financing.",""],[1,"265","1","SME Resource Pooling and Bulk Purchasing Initiative","SMEs will be encouraged to pool resources, utilise shared services, and purchase inputs, raw materials and services in bulk to reduce cost.",""],[1,"265","4","Infrastructure Development for SMEs in Sabah and Sarawak","Infrastructure development in Sabah and Sarawak will be given priority to enable SMEs to expand their businesses.",""],[1,"265","4","SME Digital Market Expansion and Alternative Financing Support","In addition, SMEs will be encouraged to expand their markets by adopting e-commerce, cloud computing, and crowdsourcing for financing.",""],[1,"265","4","Business Regulation Review and SME Assistance Expansion","Regulations will be reviewed to reduce the cost of doing business and increase the outreach of government assistance to allow businesses to enable and unleash the potential of SMEs in Sabah and Sarawak.",""],[1,"267","3","Access to Financing and Assistance Strengthening","Access to financing and assistance will be strengthened through continuous engagement with private financial institutions, venture capitalists, and angel investors to widen financial options, reduce",""],[1,"269","27","Performance-Based Incentives for Social Enterprises","Performance-based incentives to encourage social enterprises",""]],"12":[[1,"24","5","Private Consumption and Investment Promotion","The Government will also promote private consumption, as well as private investment in agriculture, manufacturing, and services to spearhead economic growth, and increase exports by improving product competitiveness, promoting services exports, and diversifying markets.",""],[1,"28","1","Private and Public Investment Expansion","Malaysia will continue to boost private investment and undertake public investment during the Eleventh Plan",""],[1,"48","5","Performance-Based Incentives for Knowledge-Intensive Economic Activities","Providing performance-based incentives for high-income and knowledge-intensive economic activities",""],[1,"48","5","Financing Access Support for Knowledge-Intensive Industries","Improving access to financing for knowledge-intensive industries",""],[1,"48","6","Facilitation Fund Tipping Point Financing","Providing tipping point financing through the Facilitation Fund",""],[1,"53","1","Domestic and Foreign Direct Investment Promotion","Both domestic direct investment (DDI) and FDI will be promoted.",""],[1,"53","2","Private Investment Facilitation and Regulatory Reform","The Government will take on more of a regulatory and facilitative role in increasing private investment through targeted strategies such as improving access to financing and improving regulations to be more business-friendly.",""],[1,"53","3","Business Cost Reduction through Infrastructure Provision and Regulatory Review","Reducing the cost of doing business through increased provision of basic infrastructure and facilities, and reviewing bureaucratic regulations",""],[1,"53","10","Innovative Financing for Knowledge-Intensive Industries","Improving access to financing for knowledge-intensive industries by considering innovative financing options",""],[1,"53","11","Facilitation Fund for Strategic Investment Projects","Providing tipping point financing through the Facilitation Fund to bridge the viability gap in financing for strategic investment projects",""],[1,"59","12","Reinvestment Incentives for Targeted Foreign Direct Investment","In order to reduce the deficit in the primary income account, the Government will encourage re-investment of earnings from targeted FDI as well as provide a comprehensive and conducive ecosystem for new investments.",""]],"13":[[1,"266","1","Innovation Promotion at Enterprise and Societal Levels","Efforts to promote innovation will be undertaken at the enterprise and societal levels.",""],[1,"266","1","Relational Capital Strengthening for Innovation Coordination","Focus will be on strengthening relational capital to foster stronger linkages, collaboration, and trust among stakeholders.",""],[1,"266","3","Research Management Agency and 1Dana Portal Expansion","Strengthening the governance mechanism by creating a research management agency (RMA) and expanding the 1Dana Portal;",""],[1,"266","4","Streamlined Public Sector Funding for R&D, Commercialisation and Innovation","Enhancing demand-driven research by streamlining public sector funding for research, development, commercialisation and innovation (R&D&C&I);",""],[1,"266","5","Industry-Academia Technology Transfer Collaboration","Strengthening industry-academia collaboration through intermediaries by encouraging local and international collaborations for technology transfer, including strategic alliances between MNCs and SMEs;",""],[1,"266","6","Private Financing Framework for R&D, Commercialisation and Innovation","Strategy F4: Promoting private financing of research, development, commercialisation and innovation by increasing access to private sources of financing, and developing a framework for risk mitigation and management of crowdfunding activities.",""],[1,"266","8","Restructuring of the RMA for Public R&D&C&I Governance","An existing agency will be restructured to become the RMA to strengthen the institutional mechanism to manage public R&D&C&I initiatives to increase return on investment.",""],[1,"266","9","1Dana R&D&C&I Centralised Registry Expansion","The 1Dana portal, established in 2014, will be expanded to serve as a centralised registry for R&D&C&I-related information to encourage sharing of resources.",""],[1,"267","1","Public Sector R&D&C&I Funding Streamlining","Public sector funding for R&D&C&I will be streamlined to ensure better returns.",""],[1,"267","1","Research Proposal Clearing House","The RMA will act as a clearing house for research proposals to coordinate and reduce duplication of proposals and increase collaboration for implementation.",""],[1,"267","1","Applied and Demand-Driven Research Funding","Funding will be channelled into fundamental research for experimental and knowledge creation; applied research to solve national issues and to develop new industries; and demand-driven research to solve problems, improve processes and create new value in industries.",""],[1,"267","2","Public-Private Research Collaboration Platforms","Local and international collaboration between Government, industry, and academia will be further encouraged through platforms such as Public Private Research Network (PPRN), Steinbeis, SIRIM-Fraunhofer, and PlaTCOM.",""],[1,"267","2","Industry-Research Technology Adoption Support","These platforms will serve as intermediaries to assist in connecting industries with the relevant research entities to provide solutions on companies' specific problems and support technology adoption.",""],[1,"267","2","Strategic Alliances for Research Commercialisation","This collaboration, which includes strategic alliances between MNCs and SMEs, will increase commercialisation of research findings and accelerate sharing of knowledge and innovative ideas.",""],[1,"267","4","R&D&C&I Project Financing Expansion","dependency on Government resources and increase the financing of R&D&C&I projects.",""],[1,"267","4","Technology Park Malaysia Angel Chapter Expansion","This includes the expansion of the Technology Park Malaysia Angel Chapter",""],[1,"267","4","Early-Stage SME Financing Programme","and early stage financing for SMEs through the SIP programme.",""],[1,"267","5","Equity Crowdfunding Framework Development","equity crowdfunding will be explored to widen the range of fundraising and investment products, as well as improve market access to a broader spectrum of issuers and investors.",""],[1,"267","5","SME and Start-up Crowdfunding Financing Support","Crowdfunding is envisioned to provide financing opportunities for SMEs, start-ups, and innovative businesses seeking liquidity in a more efficient and transparent manner.",""],[1,"267","5","Innovation Risk Mitigation and Management Framework","The enabling environment for innovation will be further strengthened by providing a clear framework for risk mitigation and management.",""],[1,"268","5","Enhanced Innovation Ecosystem Collaboration","In the enhanced innovation ecosystem, there will be greater collaboration and integration across industry, academia, and communities.",""],[1,"268","5","Industry-Aligned Research and Private Sector R&D Partnership","Research will be closely aligned with industry demand, and the private sector will be active partners in the R&D&C&I process by contributing funds, expertise, and other resources.",""],[1,"268","6","Stakeholder Collaboration Strengthening Initiative","The Eleventh Plan will focus on strengthening relational capital by improving collaboration among all stakeholders.",""],[1,"268","6","Enterprise-Level Innovation Support Initiative","At the enterprise level, initiatives will enhance demand-driven research, improve collaboration between researchers and industries,",""],[1,"269","1","Private Investment in R&D&C&I Promotion","and encourage private investment in R&D&C&I.",""],[1,"269","6","Industry-Research Partnership Strengthening","Better partnerships between industry and researchers, with industry helping to shape research to ensure relevance to business and contribute ideas, infrastructure, tools, and expertise",""]],"15":[[1,"256","3","Manufacturing Sector Growth and Revitalization Strategies","To this end, five strategies have been identified to grow and energise the manufacturing sector, as shown in Exhibit 8-10.",""],[1,"256","12","Catalytic Subsector Pioneer Incentive Scheme","Incentivise pioneers in catalytic subsectors to promote development of frontier products",""],[1,"256","13","Automation Promotion to Reduce Reliance on Unskilled Foreign Workers","Promote automation to reduce reliance on unskilled foreign workers",""],[1,"256","18","Intellectual Property Registration, Sharing and Protection Promotion","Promoting IP registration, sharing and protection",""],[1,"256","19","Targeted and Performance-Based Incentives with Exit Policy","Introducing targeted and performance-based incentives with exit policy",""],[1,"256","24","Life Cycle Assessment Adoption","Adopting life cycle assessment",""],[1,"257","2","Automation Productivity Enhancement Strategy","Strategy B2: Enhancing productivity through automation supported by developmental and performance-based financial assistance and collaboration with industry;",""],[1,"257","3","Innovation-Led Growth and Sustainable Production Promotion","Stimulating innovation-led growth by engaging with intermediaries to increase R&D and innovation activities as well as implementing sustainable consumption and production practices;",""],[1,"257","9","Automation and Workforce Productivity Enhancement Measures","Measures to increase productivity will be undertaken by increasing automation and enhancing workforce skills development.",""],[1,"257","9","Financial Assistance for Automation and Technology Adoption","Greater automation and technology utilisation will be encouraged through developmental and performance-based financial assistance to reduce the high dependence on unskilled foreign workers.",""],[1,"257","9","Expansion of Levy System and Cap on Unskilled Foreign Workers","The current levy system will be expanded and a cap on employment of unskilled foreign workers will also be introduced.",""],[1,"257","10","Manufacturing R&D and Innovation Support","Manufacturers will be encouraged to undertake R&D and innovation activities to improve their products and processes by leveraging existing research institutions through intermediaries.",""],[1,"257","10","Strategic Technology and Innovation Alliances","Strategic alliances with developed economies will be increased, especially in the field of technology, innovation and R&D, to strengthen capabilities in producing high-value products.",""],[1,"258","1","Manufacturing Innovation Intermediaries and R&D Collaboration Platforms","These intermediaries will engage the right experts to solve manufacturing problems and strengthen collaboration between manufacturers and research institutions.",""],[1,"258","2","Sustainable Manufacturing and Life Cycle Assessment Promotion","Sustainable consumption and production practices will be promoted in manufacturing processes, particularly by adopting life cycle assessment to optimise raw materials usage.",""],[1,"258","2","Manufacturing Sector Compliance Streamlining","The manufacturing sector development will also be streamlined to ensure compliance with multilateral environmental commitments and other international environmental standards in order to overcome non-tariff barriers.",""]],"16":[[1,"237","1","Private Investment, Innovation, and Export Ecosystem Improvement","The ecosystem to stimulate private investment, innovation, and exports will be further improved.",""],[1,"251","5","Export Services Internationalisation Support Programme","Strategy A3: Stepping up internationalisation by assisting firms to export services through better access to funding, upskilling, and market intelligence;",""],[1,"253","1","Services Sector Guarantee Scheme","Among the initiatives to strengthen the capabilities of services firms to export are: a dedicated Services Sector Guarantee Scheme;",""],[1,"253","1","Services Export Fund Enhancement","an improved Services Export Fund (SEF) to provide assistance to services firms to expand overseas;",""],[1,"253","1","Franchise Development Programme Improvement","the franchise development programme will be improved",""],[1,"253","1","Market Harmonisation Efforts","efforts will be taken to further harmonise markets.",""],[1,"253","3","Promotion of Tradeable High-Value Industries","Industries such as Islamic finance, ICT, oil and gas services, private healthcare, private higher education, ecotourism, the halal industry, and professional services will be further promoted.",""],[1,"254","13","Professional Services Outsourcing Promotion and Capacity Building","Promote Malaysia as an outsourcing centre for professional services to increase exports through capacity building",""],[1,"255","5","Promotion of Malaysia as an Outsourcing Centre for Professional Services","Malaysia will continue to be promoted as an outsourcing centre for professional services to increase exports in knowledge-intensive activities, such as oil and gas, aviation maintenance, repair and overhaul (MRO), and construction.",""],[1,"255","5","Capability Building and Industry Consolidation for Professional Services Firms","Professional services firms will also be encouraged to build capability and scale in niche areas through industry consolidation, partnerships with larger corporations or form multi disciplinary consortia when bidding for projects, either domestically or internationally.",""],[1,"255","5","Use of FTAs and MRAs to Support Internationalisation","Professional services firms will also be encouraged to use Free Trade Agreements (FTAs) and Mutual Recognition Agreements (MRAs) to facilitate internationalisation of the industry.",""],[1,"255","5","Reduction of Non-Tariff Barriers Through Government Negotiations","Non-tariff barriers in targeted markets will be reduced through proactive government-to-government negotiations.",""],[1,"256","16","National Export Promotion Council","Intensifying export promotion via National Export Council",""],[1,"257","5","Targeted Exporter Support and Internationalisation Strategy","Ramping up internationalisation by providing targeted support to exporters, leveraging the AEC and FTAs as well as encouraging smart partnerships between SMEs and MNCs.",""],[1,"258","5","Export Market Access and Distribution Support","The Malaysia External Trade Development Corporation (MATRADE) and related agencies will strengthen their capability to assist export-ready companies across all sectors to penetrate a wider export market and strengthen product distribution.",""],[1,"258","5","Mid-Tier Companies Development Programme Intensification","The Mid-Tier Companies Development Programme will be further intensified to accelerate export growth by mid-tier companies (companies with average annual revenues of RM20 million to RM500 million) by providing targeted market intelligence, building export capabilities, and matchmaking mid-tier companies with suitable business partners abroad.",""],[1,"258","5","National Export Council","the newly established National Export Council will address gaps and challenges in the export supply chain.",""],[1,"258","6","Export and Investment Promotion through AEC and FTAs","The AEC and FTAs will be leveraged to further ramp up exports and investments.",""],[1,"258","6","Intra-ASEAN Industry Linkage Promotion","MATRADE will promote greater intra-ASEAN industry linkages to strengthen supply chain and production networks to maximise opportunities in ASEAN and other markets.",""],[1,"258","6","FTA Utilisation for Market Access and Investment Protection","To facilitate market access and protect investment, companies will be encouraged to utilise provisions in FTAs when venturing abroad.",""]],"17":[[1,"253","4","Halal Industry Institutional and Regulatory Reform","Institutional and regulatory reforms will be undertaken to increase the efficiency and effectiveness of relevant agencies governing the halal industry.",""],[1,"253","4","Halal Certification and Auditing Coordination Enhancement","A business-friendly ecosystem and greater collaboration between agencies related to halal certification and auditing processes will be enhanced.",""],[1,"253","4","Preferential Public Procurement for Halal Products and Services","special preference in public sector procurement for halal-certified products and services will be promoted to support the growth of the industry.",""],[1,"253","5","Alignment of Halal Standards with International Standards","Malaysian halal standards will be linked to international standards to enhance global acceptance.",""],[1,"253","5","Halal Certification Incentive Scheme","Local industry players will be incentivised to obtain halal certifications to increase the halal offerings in the domestic market and position Malaysia as a global halal hub.",""],[1,"253","5","Regional Halal Distribution Centre and E-Trading Platform","the halal services industry will be further intensified through the development of a regional distribution centre that is equipped with an e-trading platform to link local halal suppliers to the global supply chain.",""],[1,"253","5","Halal Industry Innovation and R&D Support","Growth in the industry will be catalysed through innovation and R&D.",""],[1,"253","5","Alternative Halal Ingredients Industry Development","the alternative ingredients industry will be further developed to produce halal ingredients thereby strengthening Malaysia's role in the global trade of halal ingredients.",""],[1,"254","5","Halal Standards International Alignment and Alternative Ingredients Industry Promotion","Develop halal industry by linking Malaysian halal standards to international standards and promote the alternative ingredients industry",""]],"18":[[1,"93","1","Regional Economic Corridor Development","Regional economic corridors will continue to spur economic growth to address inter- and intra-regional imbalances and increase inclusivity.",""],[1,"93","3","Strategic Review of Regional Economic Corridor Master Plans","Strategy D1: Strategic review of regional economic corridor master plans by revisiting regional economic corridor priorities and industry focus;",""],[1,"93","4","Regional Economic Corridor Investment Facilitation","Accelerating investment in regional economic corridors by enhancing facilitation for investors, improving connectivity and mobility as well as intensifying research, development and commercialisation.",""],[1,"93","7","Regional Economic Corridor Investment and Infrastructure Acceleration","Efforts will be undertaken to accelerate investment, improve infrastructure and review of regional economic corridor master plans in order to realise investment of RM236 billion and create 470,000 jobs by 2020.",""],[1,"93","8","Regional Economic Corridor Development Programmes and Projects","A number of long term, high impact programmes and projects are currently underway, and will continue to be implemented in the coming years.",""],[1,"93","8","Iskandar Malaysia Creative Cluster Development","Priority sectors include the creative cluster in Iskandar Malaysia;",""],[1,"93","8","Northern Corridor Automotive and Aeronautics Industry Development","automotive and aeronautics industries in NCER;",""],[1,"93","8","East Coast Petrochemical Industry Development","petrochemical industries in the existing industrial parks in ECER;",""],[1,"93","8","Sabah Tourism and Palm Oil Downstream Processing Development","tourism and palm oil downstream processing in SDC;",""],[1,"93","8","Sarawak Energy-Intensive Industry Development","energy-intensive industries including aluminium, steel and glass in SCORE.",""],[1,"94","3","Regional Economic Corridor Investor Facilitation Mechanism","Regional economic corridor authorities will facilitate investors in obtaining approvals across multiple agencies, solving land issues and related matters to ensure committed investments are realised.",""],[1,"94","3","Expanded Investor Facilitation for Operating Businesses","Expansion of this investor facilitation model will also ensure that authorities continue to facilitate investors once their businesses are in operation, to address implementation challenges and encourage reinvestment in the future.",""],[1,"94","4","Regional Transportation Network Improvement","Transportation networks will be improved to enhance connectivity and mobility in regional economic corridors.",""],[1,"94","4","Road and Highway Construction and Upgrading","This includes the construction and upgrading of roads and highways such as the Pan Borneo Highway to link SCORE and SDC; Central Spine Road and Kota Bharu-Kuala Krai Highway to increase connectivity in ECER.",""],[1,"94","4","Mukah Airport Completion and Smart City Development","The completion of Mukah Airport is expected to accelerate development in Mukah and the surrounding areas within SCORE, with Mukah to be developed as a smart city as well as one of the growth nodes in SCORE.",""],[1,"94","5","Government-Industry-Academia R&D and Commercialisation Collaboration","Collaboration between government, industry and academia will be strengthened to intensify research, development and commercialisation (R&D&C) activities in economic clusters to ensure industrial sustainability.",""]],"19":[[1,"39","1","Export Competitiveness and Market Diversification Initiative","Exports will be increased by improving product competitiveness, promoting exports of services, and diversifying markets, thus maintaining a surplus in the external account.",""],[1,"53","14","Wholesale and Retail Subsector Modernisation and Supply Chain Efficiency Enhancement","The wholesale and retail subsector will continue to be the main contributor, expanding by 5.8% per annum, supported by strategies to modernise the subsector as well as enhance the efficiency and effectiveness of the supply chain.",""],[1,"53","15","Manufacturing Sector Productivity and Upgrading Programme","The performance of the manufacturing sector will be enhanced through a shift towards the production of more complex and diverse products and improving productivity by adopting greater automation and upgrading skills.",""],[1,"59","1","National Export Council","the formation of the National Export Council (NEC) will further stimulate export growth by facilitating cross-ministry policy coordination and implementation.",""],[1,"59","7","Export Growth Acceleration Strategies","During the Eleventh Plan, several strategies will be introduced to spur export growth to improve Malaysia's trade balance.",""],[1,"59","7","SME Export Contribution Enhancement","Efforts will also be undertaken to enhance SME contribution to exports to 25% by 2020 from 19% in 2015.",""],[1,"59","7","National Export Strategy Implementation","The NEC will enhance the contribution of exports to the economy, where several key strategies to spur export growth will be implemented as follows:",""],[1,"59","8","Export Ecosystem Improvement through Infrastructure Upgrading and Bureaucratic Simplification","Improving the export ecosystem by upgrading infrastructure and reducing bureaucratic requirements",""],[1,"59","9","Value Chain Upgrading through New Technology Investment","Moving up the value chain by encouraging companies to invest in new technologies to participate at the higher end of the global supply chain",""]],"20":[[1,"95","5","Bumiputera Entrepreneur Financing Programmes","intensifying entrepreneur financing programmes",""],[1,"95","5","Integrated Development Programmes for Bumiputera Enterprises","enhancing development-oriented and integrated programmes for Bumiputera enterprises",""],[1,"95","5","Bumiputera Mindset Change Programme","enhancing mindset change programmes",""],[1,"95","5","Community and Social Enterprise Institutionalisation","institutionalising community- and social-based enterprises",""],[1,"95","5","Private Sector Participation Incentives","providing incentives to encourage private sector and industry participation",""],[1,"95","5","Business Collaboration and Marketing Platform","establishing platform for business collaboration and marketing opportunities",""],[1,"97","2","Micro Business Financing Support","AIM and TEKUN Nasional will continue to provide financing to micro businesses.",""],[1,"97","2","SME Support for High Value-Added Industries","PUNB, SME Corp and MARA will assist SMEs in high value added industries with the potential to grow and move to the next stage of the business cycle where Bumiputera participation is still low.",""],[1,"97","3","Entrepreneur Financing Programme Intensification","Entrepreneur financing programmes will be intensified to support the implementation of an effective and integrated entrepreneur development programme.",""],[1,"97","3","Second Chance Support Policy for Bumiputera Entrepreneurs","A second chance policy will also be introduced to assist potential Bumiputera entrepreneurs to resume their business activities.",""],[1,"97","3","Waqf and Islamic Finance Support for Bumiputera Entrepreneurship","In addition, the waqf fund, as well as Islamic banking and financing will be utilised to create more Bumiputera entrepreneurs in strategic subsectors, particularly in the halal industry.",""],[1,"97","4","Government Procurement and Contract Restructuring","Government procurement and contracts will be restructured to minimise rent-seeking and spurious-front activities.",""],[1,"97","4","Graduation and Exit Policy for Government Support","It will include the introduction of an appropriate graduation and exit policy to reduce continuous dependence on the Government.",""],[1,"97","4","Smart Partnerships Between R&D Centres and Bumiputera SMEs","In addition, smart partnerships will be developed between R&D centres and Bumiputera SMEs to ensure creation of innovative products and services.",""],[1,"97","4","Soft Loan for R&D to Support SME Standards Compliance","A soft loan for R&D will be provided to enable Bumiputera SMEs to comply with international standards and certifications.",""],[1,"97","4","Vendor Development Programme Continuation","Other high impact programmes such as the Vendor Development Programme and Groom Big will be continued.",""],[1,"97","4","Carve-out Policy for Large Contracts","The carve-out policy on contracts worth RM500 million and above will continue to be implemented.",""],[1,"97","4","Outsourced Work Allocation to Bumiputera Entrepreneurs","In addition, outsourced work will continue to be given to Bumiputera entrepreneurs.",""],[1,"97","5","Bumiputera Business Chambers Streamlining and Rebranding","The Bumiputera Business Chambers will be streamlined and rebranded towards creation of a genuine entity that will champion the supply chain \"farm-to-table\" network of Bumiputera entrepreneurs.",""],[1,"97","5","Bumiputera Entrepreneur Consortium Development","A pool of high potential Bumiputera entrepreneurs among industry champions will be identified to form consortiums along the supply chain network, thus providing a supportive business ecosystem.",""],[1,"97","5","Special Funding and Market Access Support for Bumiputera Consortiums","Special provisions including funding and easier access to market will strengthen these consortiums.",""],[1,"98","1","Bumiputera Entrepreneur Mindset Change Measures","appropriate measures will be introduced to bring about a mindset change to reduce dependency on Government assistance as well as eliminate rent-seeking and spurious-front activities.",""],[1,"98","2","Bumiputera Enterprise Consolidation and Cooperative Development Initiative","This initiative will involve the merging of small Bumiputera enterprises as well as the amalgamation of agriculture smallholdings to benefit from economies of scale.",""],[1,"98","3","Bumiputera Entrepreneurship Incentive Support","Financial and non-financial incentives will be continued to encourage private sector and industry to contribute to Bumiputera entrepreneurship development.",""],[1,"98","4","Bridging Programme for Bumiputera Entrepreneurs","A Bridging Programme will be introduced to pool credible Bumiputera entrepreneurs to elevate them to the next level.",""],[1,"98","4","Bumiputera Entrepreneur Collaboration Strengthening","The Bumiputera entrepreneurial development agencies will strengthen collaboration among them to develop successful and competitive entrepreneurs.",""],[1,"98","4","Business Development Voucher Programme","a Business Development Voucher Programme will be introduced to provide matching grants to assist entrepreneurs to modernise their facilities, explore new markets and improve their business processes.",""],[1,"98","4","International Distribution Centre","An International Distribution Centre will also be established and managed by the private sector or a cooperative movement to gain access to foreign markets to ensure business viability.",""]],"21":[[1,"29","7","Micro-Entrepreneurship and Traditional Industry Development","Focus on developing micro- entrepreneurship and economic activities in low-value, traditional industries",""],[1,"29","11","Community and Social Enterprise Support for the B40 Community","Fostering community and social-based enterprises in the B40 community, in addition to individual enterprises",""],[1,"68","8","Holistic Support Programmes for Micro-Enterprises","Providing holistic support programmes for micro-enterprises",""],[1,"68","23","Incubator Expansion for Entrepreneurship and Employment","Extending the incubator concept to increase entrepreneurship and employment opportunities",""],[1,"71","10","Mobile Community Transformation Centre Programmes","The Mobile CTCs also provide a platform for the government to channel assistance directly to the target groups, including micro-credit facilities.",""],[1,"73","2","Entrepreneurship Development Programmes for Vulnerable Groups","the East Coast Economic Region (ECER) developed a range of entrepreneurship development programmes to broaden the abilities of target groups such as women, youth and unemployed to participate in the economy",""],[1,"73","5","Suri@Home Home-Based Business Programme","Suri@Home Programme creates home-based business opportunities for housewives and single mothers to supplement household incomes.",""],[1,"73","13","Bumiputera Entrepreneur Development Funding","Unit Peneraju Agenda Bumiputera (TERAJU) has allocated RM100 million for entrepreneur development, including RM1.5 million for a fishmeal and surimi processing enterprise and RM16.1 million Facilitation Fund allocated to 4 local companies enabling them to provide support services to Petroliam Nasional Berhad (PETRONAS) and Bintulu Port",""],[1,"88","4","Youth Entrepreneurship Development Programmes","Integrated entrepreneurship development programmes including financial and investment literacy will be made more accessible to youth to create a larger pool of successful young entrepreneurs",""],[1,"88","5","Integrated Youth Entrepreneurship Development Strategic Plan","Towards this end, the related agencies will formulate a strategic plan to develop dynamic and effective entrepreneurs among youth in a more integrated manner.",""]],"22":[[1,"262","1","Construction Industry Transformation Programme","The Government will introduce the Construction Industry Transformation Programme (CITP), 2016-2020, to propel the industry forward and meet market demand.",""],[1,"262","5","Sustainable Construction Legislation Development","developing legislation that supports sustainable construction activities",""],[1,"263","1","Construction Industry Productivity Enhancement Programme","A number of initiatives will be introduced to drive productivity, including expediting the adoption of the IBS by the industry through the revision of the public procurement policy and Uniform Building by-Laws 1984 and improving existing regulations to ease construction-related business processes.",""],[1,"263","1","Expansion of Construction Productivity Reforms to Local Authorities","This effort, which started with Kuala Lumpur City Hall, will be expanded to other local authorities.",""],[1,"263","1","BIM Common Platform on Pay-Per-Use Basis","The use of ICT will be enhanced by providing a common platform to use BIM on a pay-per-use basis.",""],[1,"263","2","Sustainable Construction Regulatory and Standards Package","This will include inculcating green practices in the construction value chain and developing legislation that supports sustainable construction activities.",""],[1,"263","2","Sustainable Waste Management Compliance Requirement","mandating compliance to sustainable waste management practices through EMS ISO 14001 certification",""],[1,"263","2","Building Rating and Infrastructure Standards Enhancement","enhancing the current rating systems for buildings and developing new standards for infrastructure to promote sustainability",""],[1,"263","2","Construction HSE Awareness and Accountability Initiative","enhancing the awareness and accountability of health, safety and environment (HSE), where HSE good practices will be made obligatory",""],[1,"263","2","Construction Workers Amenities Standards Upgrade","The minimum level of construction workers' amenities will be raised in the code of practice and further mandated within standard contracts.",""]],"23":[[1,"103","2","Social Cohesion and National Unity Platforms","Platforms for interaction between and among different social groups will be enhanced to foster social cohesion and national unity, while more programmes to inculcate ethics and moral values will be implemented at schools and institutions of higher education.",""],[1,"103","2","School and Higher Education Values Education Programmes","more programmes to inculcate ethics and moral values will be implemented at schools and institutions of higher education.",""],[1,"110","3","National Blueprint for Social Cohesion and National Unity","The NUCC is mandated to formulate a national blueprint for social cohesion and national unity which will be completed in 2015.",""],[1,"114","3","Social Cohesion and Unity Programme Strengthening","Social cohesion and unity programmes will be strengthened to promote an understanding of diversity through interactions and shared experiences such as community-based volunteerism activities.",""],[1,"122","2","Programmes and Platforms for Inter-Community Interaction","During the Eleventh Plan, the Government will therefore focus on enhancing programmes and platforms for greater interaction, engagement, and collaboration among Malaysians.",""],[1,"122","3","Stakeholder Collaboration for Moral and Ethical Society","During the Eleventh Plan, the Government will therefore intensify collaboration with all stakeholders, particularly community-based and religious institutions, to foster a shared sense of responsibility for building a more moral and ethical society.",""],[1,"122","5","Social Integration and Ethics Promotion Strategy","This will not only involve creating more shared experiences-from volunteerism to arts, culture and heritage-that will deepen Malaysians' understanding and appreciation of diversity, but also enhance how ethics and morality are incorporated in the education system;",""],[1,"122","6","Stakeholder Engagement and Public Awareness for Social Responsibility","This will be achieved by building an awareness of the role every stakeholder - government, private sector, communities, and individuals - has to play in building a tolerant and caring society.",""],[1,"123","1","Streamlining and Expansion of Social Integration and Unity Programmes","The Eleventh Plan will streamline existing social integration and unity programmes to reduce redundancy and improve impact.",""],[1,"123","1","Social Integration and Unity Programmes in Educational Institutions","The Government will also increase the number of social integration and unity programmes in educational institutions, from schools to universities.",""],[1,"123","1","MySilang Career Programmes for Higher Education Students","a total of 5,000 students from institutions of higher education will be sent for MySilang Career Programmes to enhance their acceptance and tolerance of Malaysians with varying backgrounds, through shared interactions and exposure.",""],[1,"123","2","Neighbourhood Unity Promotion Programmes","RT will also be encouraged to organise and implement programmes to promote unity in their respective neighbourhoods.",""],[1,"123","2","J-NITA Multi-ethnic Female Teams","Under RT, more than 400 multi-ethnic female teams will be established through the J-NITA programme.",""],[1,"123","2","Social Integration Platforms through Community Programmes","Programmes such as KOSPEN, urban farming, and Bomba Sukarela will also serve as additional platforms to promote social integration.",""],[1,"123","4","Strengthening Research and Training Institutions for National Unity Programmes","The capabilities and capacity of various research and training institutions will be enhanced to improve national planning, monitoring and implementation of unity, and ethnic relations programmes.",""],[1,"123","4","Strengthening the Institute of Ethnic Studies and the National Integration Research and Training Institute","The Institute of Ethnic Studies and the National Integration Research and Training Institute will also be strengthened.",""],[1,"123","5","School Curriculum Enhancement for Ethics and Spirituality","The formal schooling curriculum, from preschool through to higher education will therefore also be enhanced to achieve the desired outcome.",""],[1,"123","5","Public Campaigns to Promote Civic-Mindedness Among Youth","More public campaigns will be conducted by relevant agencies to instil values of civic mindedness among youth.",""],[1,"123","6","Community Ethics and Values Promotion Programmes","at the community level, the Government will collaborate with NGOs to promote ethical and moral values through specially targeted programmes and awareness campaigns.",""],[1,"123","6","Community Leadership Role-Modelling Initiative","Professional and community leaders will be encouraged to role model the desired behaviours of a caring society.",""],[1,"123","6","Religious Institution Values Promotion Programmes","Religious institutions are also expected to play a bigger role in fostering these values by conducting their own programmes.",""],[1,"125","1","Social Cohesion and National Unity Programme","The Eleventh Plan therefore aims to improve wellbeing through six focus areas: enabling universal access to quality healthcare; providing adequate and quality affordable housing; creating safer living environments; improving road safety and emergency services; fostering social cohesion and national unity; and increasing mass participation in sports.",""]],"24":[[1,"87","1","Community Empowerment and Inclusiveness Strategies","During the Eleventh Plan, efforts will focus on empowering the community to enhance inclusiveness by addressing the needs of the community, including family, youth, women, children, the elderly and PWD.",""],[1,"87","2","Family Institution Strengthening Strategy","Strategy B1: Strengthening the family institution by enhancing parenting skills and family values, as well as improving counselling services and the family support system;",""],[1,"87","8","Family Wellbeing Strengthening Initiatives","Strengthening families as the core of communities is a priority for this Eleventh Plan, with initiatives aimed at helping families to cope in a rapidly changing environment.",""],[1,"87","9","Pre-Marriage and Marriage Enrichment Programmes","Pre-marriage and marriage enrichment programmes will be promoted across all communities, to inculcate family values, parenting skills and effective communication to strengthen the marriage institution and family resilience.",""],[1,"87","9","Community-Led Family Education and Knowledge Enrichment Campaigns","NGOs, community-based organisations (CBOs) and private organisations will be encouraged to conduct these programmes.",""],[1,"87","9","Financial Management and Healthy Lifestyle Promotion for Young Married Couples","In addition, prudent financial management and healthy lifestyle will be promoted among young married couples.",""],[1,"87","9","Family Education Promotion Through Social and Mass Media","Social and mass media will be utilised to promote family education and knowledge enrichment programmes.",""],[1,"88","1","Family Counselling and Support Services Strengthening","Counselling services to family members in need, particularly those experiencing shock, emotional stress and financial difficulties will be strengthened by engaging experts and relevant NGOs.",""],[1,"88","1","Family Support System and Facilities Improvement","The existing family support system and facilities will also be improved through collaboration between the Government, community, NGOs and the private sector.",""],[1,"88","1","Integrated Community Centres Development","Integrated community centres will be established to house taska, respite care for the elderly, and transit centre for children and students, as well as other facilities such as rehabilitation centres, kafe@TEEN and Klinik Nur Sejahtera.",""]],"25":[[1,"70","11","Child Protection and Wellbeing Strengthening","Under the Tenth Plan, the protection and wellbeing of children continued to be strengthened.",""],[1,"70","12","Nur Alert Missing Child Information System","Meanwhile, a multimedia messaging service (MMS) and short messaging service (SMS) system called Nur Alert, established in 2010, continued to disseminate and seek information and feedback on missing children below 12 years old.",""],[1,"89","2","Child Protection Enhancement Measures","Efforts to protect the needs and interests of children will be enhanced to address issues of abuse and neglect.",""],[1,"89","3","Expansion of Childcare and Child Protection Units","The number of Childcare and Child Protection Units will be increased to improve the protection of children against abuse, abandonment and neglect.",""],[1,"89","3","Child Protection Advocacy Campaign","Advocacy efforts will be intensified through social media.",""],[1,"89","3","Review of the Child Act 2001","The Child Act, 2001, will also be reviewed to safeguard the needs and protection of children.",""],[1,"89","3","Strengthening Preventive and Rehabilitative Programmes for Children","Preventive and rehabilitative programmes for children in need will be strengthened by increasing the participation of family and community.",""],[1,"89","4","Community Childcare Centre Establishment","Communities will be encouraged to set up childcare centres to provide facilities for learning and recreational activities to prevent children from getting involved in undesirable social activities.",""],[1,"89","4","ECCE Child Minder Training Programme","Child minders in ECCE will be trained in collaboration with NGOs and relevant universities to enhance the quality of service and outcomes for the children under their care.",""],[1,"89","4","Special Needs Childcare Centre Expansion","More childcare centres for children with special needs, such as Down's Syndrome and learning, hearing or physical disabilities, will be established in partnership with NGOs and the private sector.",""],[1,"89","4","Technical and Vocational Education Access for Welfare Institution Youth","Children aged 13 to 18 in welfare institutions will be provided with opportunities to pursue technical and vocational education and training.",""],[1,"313","4","Child Health, Childcare, and Social Support Services","Children are given the best possible start to life with quality healthcare and childcare facilities as well as other social support systems regardless of who they are and where they come from.",""],[1,"313","4","Child Protection and Safety Measures","Our children are safe and protected at all times.",""]],"26":[[1,"87","7","Accessible Physical Environment for Persons with Disabilities","Empowering persons with disabilities by creating a friendly physical environment for PWD",""],[1,"87","7","Disability Training and Skills Development Programme","expanding training and skills development to increase employability",""],[1,"90","4","PWD-Friendly Environment Enhancement","The focus of the Eleventh Plan will continue to provide a more conducive and PWD-friendly environment for active, productive and independent living.",""],[1,"90","5","Strengthened Enforcement of Universal Access Building By-Laws","the enforcement of the Uniform Building By-Laws for Universal Access 1984 will be strengthened to ensure compliance to universal design and creating a disabled-friendly physical environment.",""],[1,"90","5","Upgrade of Existing Government Buildings for Universal Access","Existing Government buildings will also be upgraded in compliance with the By-Laws.",""],[1,"90","6","Community-Based Independent Living Centres for Persons with Disabilities","community-based Independent Living Centres will be established with the participation of NGOs.",""],[1,"90","7","Productive Persons with Disabilities Empowerment Programmes","During the Plan, more programmes will be implemented to empower productive PWD.",""],[1,"90","7","Basic Education, Skills Training, and Entrepreneurship Support for Persons with Disabilities","More accessibility to basic education and skills training will be provided, including entrepreneurship, to build relevant skills among PWD such that they are employable by the private sector and the government, in line with the target to employ at least 1% PWD among civil servants.",""],[1,"90","7","Disability Training and Research Centre of Excellence Upgrade","the Pusat Latihan Perindustrian dan Pemulihan will be upgraded as the centre of excellence (CoE) for disability training and research.",""]],"27":[[1,"89","5","Elderly Quality of Life Enhancement Initiative","During the Plan, concerted efforts will be undertaken to enhance the quality of life of the elderly.",""],[1,"89","6","Elderly-Friendly Infrastructure and Care Services Expansion","Initiatives to improve the support environment for the elderly include providing elderly-friendly infrastructure and improving care services.",""],[1,"89","6","Elderly Day Care Centre Expansion","More day care centres for the elderly will be established in collaboration with NGOs to enable them to live with family members who are working.",""],[1,"89","6","Elderly Care Centres and Home Help Services Expansion","In addition, elderly care centres and Home Help services will also be expanded.",""],[1,"89","6","Elderly Care Awareness Programme","Awareness programmes on elderly care will be strengthened to shift the elderly community to action in adopting active and healthy lifestyles.",""],[1,"90","2","Institute of Gerontology Capacity Enhancement","The capacity of the Institute of Gerontology, Universiti Putra Malaysia will be enhanced to conduct more research to support active ageing.",""],[1,"90","2","University of the Third Age Programme Expansion","The University of the Third Age (U3A) Programme will be expanded to provide opportunities for the elderly to continuously learn and acquire knowledge and skills in collaboration with universities, community colleges and Pusat Aktiviti Warga Emas.",""],[1,"90","2","NGO Self-Help Learning Programme Support","NGOs will also be encouraged to implement self-help based learning programmes.",""],[1,"90","3","National Volunteerism Awareness Campaign for Retired Professionals","A national campaign to promote social awareness on volunteerism among retired professionals will be launched to encourage the elderly to participate in community-based activities.",""],[1,"90","3","Community Development Volunteer Recruitment Support","CBOs and NGOs will be encouraged to attract more retired professionals to participate in voluntary community development programmes.",""]],"28":[[1,"32","3","Whole-Society Social Services Delivery Approach","will be actively engaged in addressing social issues through a whole- society approach in the provision of social services.",""],[1,"32","4","Community Participation in Social Service Delivery","At the societal level, communities will be encouraged to provide input into social service delivery mechanisms, while a social financing model will be developed to assist communities to fund new initiatives.",""],[1,"32","4","Social Financing Model for Community Initiatives","while a social financing model will be developed to assist communities to fund new initiatives.",""],[1,"32","11","Community Feedback-Based Social Services Delivery Streamlining","Focus on streamlining social services delivery by incorporating feedback from the community in line with the \"whole-society approach\"",""],[1,"32","12","Social Financing Model and Outcome-Based Funding","Delivery supported by a Social Financing Model and outcome- based funding to provide communities with avenues to invest in innovative initiatives",""],[1,"267","7","Whole-Society Collaboration for Social Services Delivery","Strategy F5: Strengthening collaboration through a whole- society approach by encouraging broader participation across Government, residents, non-governmental organisations (NGOs), organisational and community leaders for social services delivery;",""],[1,"267","8","Social Financing Model for Social Service Delivery","Strategy F6: Developing a social financing model to promote investments from the private sector, foundations, and individuals in delivering social services;",""],[1,"267","10","Whole-Society Social Services Delivery Approach","the design and delivery of social services will shift from a top-down, government-centric approach to a whole-society approach.",""],[1,"268","1","Social Services Delivery Coordination Task Force","A task force comprising representatives from relevant ministries, private sector, NGOs and Community-based Organisations (CBOs) will be established to coordinate social services delivery.","relevant ministries"],[1,"268","1","Replication of Successful Community-Based Programmes","Through this task force, successful community-based programmes will be replicated",""],[1,"268","1","NGO and CBO Capacity-Building Support","the Government will also be able to assist in improving the professionalism and capabilities of NGOs and CBOs.",""],[1,"268","2","Social Financing Model for Public-Private Partnership Programmes","a social financing model for public-private partnership programmes will be introduced to promote investments from the private sector, foundations, and individuals in delivering social services.",""],[1,"268","5","Whole-Society Social Service Engagement","Communities will be actively engaged in addressing social issues through a whole-society approach in the provision of social services.",""],[1,"269","1","Community Participation in Social Service Delivery","communities will be encouraged to provide input into social services delivery mechanisms",""],[1,"269","1","Social Financing Model for Community Initiatives","a social financing model will be developed to assist communities to fund new initiatives.",""],[1,"269","9","Social Financing and Outcome-Based Funding Mechanism","Delivery supported by a social financing model and outcome- based funding to provide communities with avenue to invest in innovative initiatives",""],[1,"291","5","Alternative Service Delivery Mechanism for Welfare Services","The Government will leverage the capacity and geographical presence of NGOs and other community-based organisations (CBOs) as an alternative service delivery (ASD) mechanism to deliver selected services.",""],[1,"315","7","Citizen Co-creation and Public Service Delivery Partnership","Local governments demonstrate strong leadership by engaging the rakyat in the decision-making process to achieve the best outcomes.",""],[1,"315","7","Civil Society Participation and Service Co-Delivery Expansion","Civil society is empowered to champion social causes and its role and capabilities are expanded to actively participate in the co-creation and delivery of public services.",""]],"29":[[1,"270","3","Strategic Review of Corridor Development Master Plans","Strategy G2: Strengthening corridors to fuel regional development through a strategic review of corridor development master plans, accelerate investment in regional economic corridors, improve infrastructure, as well as enhance talent and skill development.",""],[1,"270","3","Investment Acceleration in Regional Economic Corridors","Strategy G2: Strengthening corridors to fuel regional development through a strategic review of corridor development master plans, accelerate investment in regional economic corridors, improve infrastructure, as well as enhance talent and skill development.",""],[1,"270","3","Regional Infrastructure Improvement Programme","Strategy G2: Strengthening corridors to fuel regional development through a strategic review of corridor development master plans, accelerate investment in regional economic corridors, improve infrastructure, as well as enhance talent and skill development.",""],[1,"274","1","Regional Economic Corridors Development","regional economic corridors will continue to be a key enabler to ensure a more balanced geographic development across Malaysia.",""],[1,"274","2","Regional Economic Corridor Development Enhancement","Regional economic corridor development will be enhanced through a strategic review of the corridor development master plans and increased investment, improved infrastructure as well as talent and skill development across the five corridors to ensure that local communities continue to benefit from the investment and resulting economic growth in these areas.",""]],"30":[[1,"65","1","Regional Growth Acceleration Initiative","Specific strategies include ... accelerating regional growth;",""],[1,"72","2","Regional Economic Corridor Community Benefit Initiatives","A number of initiatives were implemented across the regional economic corridors to enable local communities to benefit from the development taking place in the region.",""],[1,"72","9","Iskandar Malaysia Housing, Transport, Skills, and Entrepreneur Development Initiative","Housing, transportation linkages, skills training, and entrepreneur development continued to be a priority in Iskandar Malaysia",""],[1,"72","14","Northern Corridor Economic Region Skills Training and Social Inclusion Initiatives","Initiatives in the Northern Corridor Economic Region (NCER) focused on skills training for increased employability, welfare, and social inclusion programmes",""],[1,"73","3","Empower ECER Entrepreneurship Skills Training Programme","Empower ECER Programme trained 4,050 participants in entrepreneurship skills, with an 83% success rate, while 7,045 participants are currently undergoing training",""],[1,"73","7","Skills Training Programmes for Local Communities in the Sabah Development Corridor","Initiatives to increase opportunities for local communities in the Sabah Development Corridor (SDC) focused on skills training programmes",""]],"31":[[1,"91","8","Rural Road Construction and Upgrading Programme","New roads will be constructed and existing roads including ex-logging roads will be upgraded to improve connectivity, particularly in Sabah and Sarawak as well as Orang Asli settlements in Peninsular Malaysia.",""],[1,"91","9","Rural Water Supply Expansion Programme","The Rural Water Supply programme, to supply clean and treated water directly to each household, will be expanded and this will involve connecting households to the meter stands of the reticulation systems.",""],[1,"91","9","Alternative Rural Water Supply Systems","In addition, alternative systems such as gravity feed, tube wells and rain water harvesting will be used in remote and isolated areas.",""],[1,"91","10","Rural Off-Grid Electricity Supply Programme","The Rural Electricity Supply programme will continue to focus on off- grid generation for remote and isolated areas.",""],[1,"92","1","Rural Alternative Electrification System Sustainability","ensure sustainability of the rural alternative electrification system.",""]],"32":[[1,"72","17","Ecotourism Training for Orang Asli","Social inclusion initiatives include ecotourism training for Orang Asli in the Belum- Temenggor tropical rainforest area to create additional streams of income",""],[1,"82","9","Rural Entrepreneurship Promotion Programme","To encourage rural entrepreneurship, an appropriate socio-economic environment will be established to facilitate local activities.",""],[1,"82","9","Entrepreneurial Orientation Programme","The entrepreneurial orientation programme focused on stimulating local entrepreneurial talent and growth of indigenous companies will be introduced.",""],[1,"83","1","Rural Youth Financing and Entrepreneurship Support","Initiatives to enhance access to financing and entrepreneurship training, as well as the provision of advisory services, and business premises will be increased.",""],[1,"83","2","Community- and Social-Based Enterprise Development on Cooperative Model","A systematic approach will be introduced to develop community- and social-based enterprises on the cooperative model to carry out activities such as childcare services or crèches, tuition centres, and orphanages for B40 households in urban areas.",""],[1,"83","3","Cooperative-Based Community Enterprise Support","In rural areas, B40 households especially the Orang Asli in Peninsular Malaysia and those living in the rural and remote areas in Sabah and Sarawak, will be encouraged to establish cooperative-based community enterprises including through provision of initial funding by Suruhanjaya Koperasi Malaysia (SKM).","Suruhanjaya Koperasi Malaysia (SKM)"],[1,"83","3","Rural Community Enterprise Capability and Market Access Support","Government-linked companies (GLCs) and GLICs will collaborate with the relevant local, regional, and corridor authorities to develop capabilities and provide business opportunities for these community enterprises.","Government-linked companies (GLCs) | GLICs | relevant local, regional, and corridor authorities"],[1,"83","3","Youth Participation in Rural Enterprise Programmes","Youth in the rural area will be encouraged to participate in enterprises and dedicated programmes designed to induce the involvement of local community.",""],[1,"83","4","Private Sector Incentives for B40 Area Investment","The private sector, especially multinational corporations (MNCs) and large local companies, will be incentivised to locate their business operations in urban and rural areas with majority B40 households to provide better job opportunities for their local communities, especially high paying jobs.",""],[1,"83","4","Rural Investment Support and Local Workforce Incentives","Investment in rural areas will leverage on local natural resources.",""],[1,"83","4","Tax Incentives for Local Hiring and Training","Existing incentives such as double deduction and tax relief will be provided to encourage the MNCs and large local companies to employ and train the local workforce.",""],[1,"83","4","Basic Infrastructure and Facilities for Business Support","Basic infrastructure and facilities will also be provided to support these businesses and reduce the cost of doing business.",""],[1,"83","5","Rural Development Centre Service Provision","banking, postal, and marketing services will be provided in rural development centres, especially in Orang Asli settlements in Peninsular Malaysia and majority B40 households population in Sabah and Sarawak.",""],[1,"91","3","Private Investment Promotion in Rural Areas","Encouraging more private investment in rural areas by providing a more conducive business environment;",""],[1,"91","5","Mobile Community Transformation Centre Programme Expansion","Strategy C4: Expanding access to basic services by expanding the mobile community transformation centre programme,",""],[1,"91","5","Rural Banking Services Expansion","and extending banking services to rural areas;",""],[1,"92","2","Rural Investment Promotion and Business Facilitation","Efforts will be implemented in collaboration with regional economic corridor authorities to provide a more conducive business environment to attract higher value added investment to rural areas.",""],[1,"92","2","Inter-Ministerial Infrastructure and Support Services Coordination","Collaboration among relevant ministries and agencies will be strengthened to provide appropriate infrastructure, logistics and support services to facilitate private sector investment.",""],[1,"92","2","RTCs One-Stop Business Facilitation Enhancement","The role of RTCs as a one-stop business facilitation centre will be enhanced to increase the ease of doing business, including providing information on potential areas for investment.",""],[1,"92","3","Rural-Urban Connectivity and Mobility Improvement","The linkage between rural and urban areas will be strengthened by improving connectivity and mobility to foster greater economic integration.",""],[1,"92","3","Integrated Transport System and Bus Route Optimization","The transportation system will be integrated to provide better connectivity and more cost-effective routes for buses will be identified to increase mobility.",""],[1,"92","4","Strengthening UTC, RTC and Mini-RTC Rural-Urban Linkages","The role of UTCs, RTCs and mini-RTCs as conduits of rural-urban linkages will be strengthened by leveraging ICT.",""],[1,"92","4","Rural Service Use Promotion for Ecotourism Support","Measures will also be undertaken to encourage rural dwellers to use these centres to provide supporting services, particularly for those in the ecotourism industry.",""],[1,"92","5","Mobile Community Transformation Centre Programme Expansion","Expanding the Mobile Community Transformation Centre programme",""],[1,"92","6","Mobile CTC Service Expansion Programme","The Mobile CTC programme which brings basic government services to rural communities, especially in remote areas, will be expanded with the participation of more government and private agencies.",""],[1,"92","7","Rural Banking Services Expansion Programme","Implementation of the rural banking services programme will be expanded to increase accessibility to financial services for the rural community.",""]],"33":[[1,"339","23","Pahang-to-Selangor Raw Water Transfer Tunnel","Construction of a water tunnel to transfer raw water from Pahang to Selangor to address water shortages in the Klang Valley",""]],"34":[[1,"224","1","Non-Revenue Water Reduction Initiative","the Government remains committed to tackling the long-standing issue of non-revenue water, currently at a national average of 36.6%.",""],[1,"224","4","Non-Revenue Water Reduction Programme","Strategy D3: Increasing efficiency and productivity of water and sewerage services through implementation of the Non- Revenue Water Reduction Programme",""],[1,"225","4","Holistic Non-Revenue Water Reduction Programme","During the Eleventh Plan, NRW will be reduced from 36.6% in 2013 to 25%, as shown in Exhibit 7-15, with the implementation of a holistic NRW reduction programme.",""],[1,"225","4","District Metering Zone Development and Network Rehabilitation","One of the initiatives is to develop comprehensive district metering zones, which also include meter and pipe replacement programmes, and pressure control management.",""],[1,"225","4","Illegal Water Tapping Enforcement","Enforcement on illegal tapping will also be given priority.",""],[1,"225","4","Trained Worker Requirement for Pipe Works","Regulations to require contractors to only use trained workers in pipe works will be enforced.",""],[1,"226","5","Water Demand Management Master Plan","The Ministry of Energy, Green Technology and Water (KeTTHA) will develop a master plan on water demand management, which will enable better demand management and provide tools to forecast water demand.","The Ministry of Energy, Green Technology and Water (KeTTHA)"],[1,"226","5","Alternative Water Use and Tariff Revision Measures","Priority will be given to reduce the use of treated water for non-potable uses by using alternative water sources such as rain water harvesting, storm water, and treated waste water.",""],[1,"226","5","Water Conservation Awareness and Education Programmes","In addition, communications, awareness and education programmes will be intensified to promote the efficient and prudent use of water.",""]],"35":[[1,"27","6","Water and Sewerage Network Expansion","Expansion and investment in new water and sewerage networks and treatment capacity will continue.",""],[1,"27","6","Energy Security Improvement Measures","Emphasis will also be placed on improving the security and reliability of the energy sector by addressing both supply-side and demand-side measures.",""],[1,"77","4","Clean and Treated Water Supply Expansion","additional houses will be supplied with clean and treated water",""],[1,"91","2","Rural Basic Infrastructure Expansion and Planning Streamlining","Strategy C1: Extending provision of rural basic infrastructure by streamlining rural infrastructure planning and increasing the provision of road, water and electricity supply;",""]],"36":[[1,"170","4","Multi-purpose Flood Mitigation Exploration","In addition, flood mitigation approaches with multifunctional purposes will be explored to attract investments in value-generating economic activities.",""],[1,"184","4","Flood Mitigation Investment and Forecasting Strengthening","Improving flood mitigation by generating new investments from flood mitigation projects, enhancing long-term planning and strengthening flood forecasting and warning systems;",""],[1,"185","5","Flood Mitigation Improvement through Innovative Solutions","Flood mitigation efforts will be further improved through innovative solutions taking into account the intensity and frequency of extreme weather events.",""],[1,"185","6","Multi-purpose Flood Mitigation Infrastructure","The Department of Irrigation and Drainage Malaysia (DID) will use alternative and new technologies, including multifunctional mechanisms, to mitigate floods and encourage investment.","Department of Irrigation and Drainage Malaysia (DID)"],[1,"185","7","Floodplain and High-Risk Area Flood Mitigation Reorientation","The approach to addressing flood mitigation in floodplains and high risk areas will be reoriented, including generating new economic activities, and improving the financial viability of such investments.",""],[1,"185","7","Flood-Resilient Building and Infrastructure Design Standards","Developments in such areas, especially construction of buildings and infrastructure, will be based on appropriate design and technology to adapt to floods and extreme weather.",""],[1,"185","8","Long-term Flood Mitigation Solutions","the DID and relevant agencies will strengthen long-term flood mitigation solutions through implementation of Integrated Water Resource Management, Integrated River Basin Management and Integrated Flood Management.","DID"],[1,"185","8","Integrated Structural and Non-Structural Flood Protection Measures","This includes the implementation of integrated solutions using a combination of structural components - such as retention ponds, diversion and river improvement works, and non-structural components - such as flood maps, flood warning system, and flood proofing as well as awareness and education programmes.",""],[1,"185","8","Review of Existing Flood Mitigation Measures","DID will also review existing flood mitigation measures such as bunds and flood levees to cope with higher flood levels.","DID"],[1,"187","1","Flood Forecasting and Warning System Upgrade","The Government will upgrade the current flood forecasting and warning system to allow a longer lead time in numerical weather prediction, raising from current three days lead time to seven days, and flood warnings from current six hours to two days lead time.",""],[1,"188","1","Climate-Resilient Infrastructure Planning","In energy-related infrastructure, due consideration will be given to climate change and environment at the planning, evaluation and implementation stages.",""],[1,"188","1","Alternative Water Source Diversification","Alternative sources of water such as recycled water, ground water, lakes and reservoirs will be explored to increase the diversity of supply and resilience against potential climate change impacts.",""]],"37":[[1,"191","6","Water Services Industry Restructuring","Continuing efforts to restructure the water services industry",""],[1,"193","2","Water and Sewerage Network and Treatment Capacity Investment","In water and sewerage, Malaysia will continue to invest in new networks and treatment plant capacity.",""],[1,"193","2","Non-Revenue Water Reduction Programme","Focus will also be given to a holistic non-revenue water reduction programme and improving the performance of the sewerage system.",""],[1,"193","2","Sewerage System Performance Improvement","Focus will also be given to a holistic non-revenue water reduction programme and improving the performance of the sewerage system.",""],[1,"193","2","Water Services Industry Licensing Regime Migration","Efforts to expedite migration towards a new licensing regime under the Water Services Industry Act, 2006 (WSIA), will also be undertaken to ensure the sustainability of the water services industry.",""],[1,"201","2","Sewerage Service Capacity Expansion","In addition, construction of seven regional and centralised treatment plants including the Pantai 2 Sewage Treatment Plant (STP) in FT Kuala Lumpur and Langat STP in Selangor commenced.",""],[1,"204","12","Water Network and Treatment Plant Capacity Expansion","Expanding network and treatment plant capacity through infrastructure investment and use of efficient technology",""],[1,"204","14","Water Services Regulatory Framework Strengthening","Strengthening the regulatory framework of the water services industry",""],[1,"206","4","Rural Water and Sewerage Network Expansion","In these sectors, expanding network reach especially in rural areas, improving the reliability and efficiency of services, and enhancing the financial sustainability of the sector, are main areas of focus.",""],[1,"206","4","Clean Water, Sewerage, and Non-Revenue Water Reduction Targets","By 2020, the Government aims to provide 99% of the population with clean and treated water, 80% with connected sewerage services and reduce non-revenue water to 25%.",""],[1,"224","1","Water Services Industry Reform and Coverage Expansion","The Government remains committed to expanding coverage and improving the quality of the water services industry nationwide.",""],[1,"224","1","Water Services Industry Act Implementation","To achieve these objectives, the Water Services Industry Act (WSIA) was introduced in 2006.",""],[1,"224","2","Water Tariff System Strengthening and Joint Billing Reform","Raising the financial sustainability of the water services industry by strengthening the tariff system and implementing joint billing for water and sewerage;",""],[1,"224","3","Rural Water and Sewerage Infrastructure Expansion","Strategy D2: Expanding network and treatment plant capacity through infrastructure investment and use of efficient technology, through developing new treatment plants, increasing clean and treated water coverage and expanding connected water and sewerage services in rural areas;",""],[1,"224","5","Water Services Regulatory Framework Strengthening","Strategy D4: Strengthening the regulatory framework of the water services industry with the National Sewerage Master Plan, a water demand management master plan and promotion of waste to wealth initiatives.",""],[1,"224","7","Water Treatment and Distribution Capital Financing via PAAB","Capital expenditure for water treatment and distribution will be financed through the Perbadanan Aset Air Berhad (PAAB) to reduce the amount of financial support required from the Government.",""],[1,"224","7","New Water Tariff Setting Mechanism for Full Cost Recovery","The viability of this arrangement will need to be tied to a new tariff setting mechanism that promotes full cost recovery.",""],[1,"224","9","Joint Water and Sewerage Billing System","To this end, a joint billing exercise between water and sewerage services will be implemented based on a volumetric formula for sewerage tariffs.",""],[1,"225","1","Construction and Upgrading of Water Treatment Plants","The Government will ensure water supply sustainability, especially in stressed areas, by constructing new treatment plants or upgrading existing ones.",""],[1,"225","2","Rural Alternative Water Supply Expansion","Alternative water supply systems such as rain water harvesting, tube wells, and gravity feed systems will be expanded in rural areas - particularly in Kelantan, Pahang, Sabah, and Sarawak.",""],[1,"225","2","Expansion of Connected Water Supply Coverage","Efforts to expand connected water supply coverage in these states will continue, supplemented by these alternative systems.",""],[1,"225","6","Water Services Sustainability Policy","A comprehensive policy will be prepared for implementing agencies, industry players, and relevant stakeholders to guide the water services industry towards sustainability.",""]],"38":[[1,"287","13","National Single Window for Trade Facilitation","U-Customs providing a national single window for trade facilitation",""],[1,"290","3","Trade Facilitation Mechanism Enhancement","Key initiatives include improving work processes in the frontline, enhancing trade facilitation mechanisms, adopting green practices, and introducing alternative service delivery mechanisms;",""],[1,"291","2","National Single Window Implementation through u-Customs","The commitment to provide a National Single Window (NSW) for trade facilitation will be realised with the implementation of a ubiquitous customs system, u-Customs.","Royal Malaysian Customs Department | permit issuing agencies | other government agencies | traders"]],"39":[[1,"79","3","Healthcare Access Expansion","increasing access to healthcare services",""],[1,"84","3","Private and NGO Healthcare Facility Provision in Urban Areas","The Government will encourage the participation of private healthcare service providers and non-governmental organisations (NGOs) in the provision of specific healthcare facilities such as dialysis, rehabilitation and medical testing lab centres in urban areas.",""],[1,"84","4","Rural Community Clinic Expansion","In rural areas, more community clinics will be built to increase access to basic healthcare services.",""],[1,"84","4","Specialist Outreach and Mobile Health Services","Frequency of visits by medical specialists in non-specialist district hospitals, mobile clinics, and flying doctors will also be increased while local health volunteer programmes will be strengthened.",""],[1,"84","4","Community Health and Nutrition Support Programmes","Other health programmes such as food baskets, community feeding, and immunisation programmes will be continued.",""],[1,"84","4","Family Health Awareness and Education Campaigns","In addition, awareness and education programmes on family health such as nutrition, family planning, and healthy living will be intensified.",""],[1,"103","2","Healthcare Delivery Improvement for Underserved Populations","Improvements in healthcare will focus on addressing underserved populations, improving health system delivery to enhance efficiency and effectiveness, and intensifying collaboration with the private sector and NGOs.",""],[1,"114","3","Universal Healthcare Access Expansion","Under the Eleventh Plan, the Government will accelerate efforts to achieve universal access to quality healthcare by targeting underserved areas, and increasing capacity of both facilities and healthcare personnel.",""],[1,"115","1","Universal Access to Quality Healthcare","the Government remains committed to achieving universal access to quality healthcare during the Eleventh Plan by continuing efforts to improve the fundamentals of the health system.",""],[1,"115","2","Targeted Support for Underserved Communities","Specific initiatives include the expansion of mobile healthcare, the improvement of primary healthcare teams, and domiciliary healthcare programmes;",""],[1,"115","4","Healthcare Facility Expansion and Workforce Capacity Enhancement","Initiatives include developing new facilities, upgrading existing facilities, as well as enhancing healthcare personnel capacity and capabilities;",""],[1,"115","6","Expansion of Quality Healthcare Access in Underserved Areas","Access to quality healthcare, particularly in underserved urban and rural areas and communities will be expanded.",""],[1,"115","7","Expanded Domiciliary Healthcare and Family Caregiver Training Programme","Domiciliary healthcare programmes will be expanded to include care programmes for patients who require long-term nursing upon early discharge, such as stroke patients.",""],[1,"116","5","Healthcare Facility Upgrading and Expansion","Existing healthcare facilities and assets will be upgraded, while the development of new facilities will take into account functionality, cost- effectiveness, and the needs of local communities.",""],[1,"116","5","Private Sector Healthcare Facility Partnership","the private sector will be encouraged to collaborate and set up more healthcare facilities that cater to the needs of low- and middle-income households.",""],[1,"116","5","Health Workforce Distribution and Capability Building","The number and distribution of health specialists and skilled personnel will also be improved by reviewing policies, incentives, and capability building programmes.",""],[1,"116","5","Rural and Remote Health Personnel Incentive Packages","Incentive packages will be reviewed to attract health personnel to serve in rural and remote areas.",""],[1,"125","1","Universal Access to Quality Healthcare","The Eleventh Plan therefore aims to improve wellbeing through six focus areas: enabling universal access to quality healthcare; providing adequate and quality affordable housing; creating safer living environments; improving road safety and emergency services; fostering social cohesion and national unity; and increasing mass participation in sports.",""]],"40":[[1,"254","10","Healthcare Travel Promotion and Accreditation Initiative","Grow healthcare travel through international accreditation, increased insurance coverage, and leverage regional referral network",""],[1,"255","2","Healthcare Travel Services Promotion","In further promoting the healthcare travel services industry, focus will be given to attract healthcare travellers to seek treatment in areas such as oncology, cardiology, orthopaedic, reproductive help, and dental treatment.",""],[1,"255","2","Traditional and Complementary Medicine Industry Development","the traditional and complementary medicine industry will be further developed with an aim to become a regional referral centre and hub.",""],[1,"255","2","Healthcare Accreditation and Insurance Portability Support","International accreditation, increased insurance coverage and portability, and regional referral network will be fully leveraged to ensure Malaysia attracts higher in-patient mix and revenue-per-patient in the identified areas.",""]],"41":[[1,"313","3","Healthcare Digitalisation and Virtual Monitoring","Personalised healthcare with virtual monitoring and digitised records will be the norm.",""]],"42":[[1,"58","2","Affordable Housing Initiatives","Demand for affordable housing by the low-income group will also remain favourable, which will be supported by several Government initiatives, such as Program Perumahan Rakyat 1Malaysia (PR1MA), Rumah Idaman Rakyat and Rumah Mesra Rakyat 1Malaysia.",""],[1,"79","3","Affordable Housing Expansion","increasing the provision of affordable housing",""],[1,"84","1","Affordable Housing Support for B40 Households","The Government will continue to ensure that affordable homes are available to B40 households.",""],[1,"84","1","Special Interest Housing Loans for B40 Households","Special interest rate loans, with a 10-year moratorium on sale of the property, will be provided to B40 households to enable them to own houses.",""],[1,"84","1","Affordable Housing Schemes by PR1MA and Syarikat Perumahan Negara Berhad","Affordable housing schemes by Perbadanan PR1MA Malaysia and Syarikat Perumahan Negara Berhad will be continued.",""],[1,"84","1","Housing Rental Assistance","Housing rental assistance will also be made available to eligible households.",""],[1,"84","1","State Affordable Housing Quota Encouragement","state governments will be encouraged to set an adequate quota for affordable housing.",""],[1,"84","2","Low-Cost Housing Refurbishment Campaign","Existing low-cost flats and houses will be refurbished as part of a holistic campaign to improve the living conditions of the community.",""],[1,"84","2","Program Bantuan Rumah Integrated Settlements","the Government will continue to provide housing with basic amenities through the construction of integrated settlements under Program Bantuan Rumah (PBR).",""],[1,"84","2","Program Perumahan Rakyat for Poor Urban Households","The Program Perumahan Rakyat (PPR) will be continued for poor households in urban areas.",""],[1,"103","2","Housing Support for Low-Income Households","Housing support will be maintained for the poor, low- and middle-income households, including youth and young married couples.",""],[1,"114","3","Affordable Housing Programme Expansion","Access to quality affordable housing will be further enhanced by expanding and strengthening existing programmes for poor, low- and middle-income households, and providing more avenues for youth homeownership.",""],[1,"117","1","Affordable Housing Support for Low- and Middle-Income Households","The Government will therefore continue to provide affordable housing for the poor, low- and middle-income households, with differing levels of support based on need.",""],[1,"117","2","Affordable Housing Programmes for Targeted Groups","This strategy will be delivered through the continuation of programmes for poor, low- and middle-income households, the introduction of targeted programmes for youth and young married couples, as well as the facilitation of greater private sector participation;",""],[1,"117","5","Targeted Housing Programmes for Urban and Rural Households","The Government will continue to play a major role in meeting the housing needs for targeted groups in urban and rural areas by continuing successful, existing programmes.",""],[1,"117","5","Housing Financing Scheme Enhancement","In addition, financing schemes such as the My First Home Scheme, Youth Housing Scheme and MyHome will be enhanced to improve access and affordability for low- and middle-income households.",""],[1,"117","6","Transit Housing for Youth and Young Married Couples","Transit houses will be built for youth and young married couples in urban areas, including those proposed under the 1Malaysia Youth City programme.",""],[1,"125","1","Affordable Housing Provision","The Eleventh Plan therefore aims to improve wellbeing through six focus areas: enabling universal access to quality healthcare; providing adequate and quality affordable housing; creating safer living environments; improving road safety and emergency services; fostering social cohesion and national unity; and increasing mass participation in sports.",""]],"43":[[1,"117","3","Integrated Public Housing Database","Measures under this strategy include the development of an integrated database to match supply and demand",""],[1,"117","3","Public Housing Land Bank Establishment","the establishment of a land bank for future development projects",""],[1,"117","4","Enhanced Regulatory Framework for Environment-Friendly Facilities","This will be achieved through an enhanced regulatory framework and collaboration among community and NGOs.",""],[1,"118","1","Integrated Affordable Housing Planning Database","an integrated database accessible to all relevant stakeholders will be established to ensure housing supply matches demand according to locality, price, and target groups",""],[1,"118","1","Affordable Housing Land Bank Establishment","a land bank will be established for the development of affordable housing, particularly in urban areas",""],[1,"118","1","Waqf and Baitulmal Land Mobilization for Affordable Housing","Collaboration between the National Housing Department with state Islamic religious councils could be leveraged to unlock potential waqf and baitulmal land","National Housing Department | state Islamic religious councils"],[1,"118","2","Sustainable Affordable Housing Development Standards","The Government will encourage all new affordable housing developments to adopt sustainable practices, and provide liveable and environment-friendly facilities and infrastructure for the rakyat, including PWD and senior citizens.",""],[1,"118","2","Public Housing Rental Rate Review","Public housing rental rates will be reviewed to ensure that sufficient funds are available to cover the cost of management and regular standard maintenance of public housing.",""],[1,"118","3","Community Housing Maintenance Awareness Programme","Awareness programmes among residents to foster a culture of maintenance, cleanliness, and the prevention of vandalism will be enhanced through collaboration among communities and NGOs.",""],[1,"118","3","MyBeautiful Malaysia Cleanliness Promotion Initiative","MyBeautiful Malaysia will continue to promote a comfortable living environment and instil a culture of cleanliness among residents.",""]],"44":[[1,"95","3","Bumiputera Corporate Ownership Expansion Strategy","Strategy E2: Increasing Bumiputera effective control and sustainable corporate ownership by broadening investment strategy to improve equity ownership, increasing GLCs and GLICs divestment of non-core assets and activities to Bumiputera enterpreneurs, as well as introducing new funding mechanisms for financial assets;",""],[1,"95","4","Institutional-Based Asset Ownership Programmes and New Funding Mechanisms","Enlarging the share of Bumiputera wealth ownership by strengthening institutional-based programmes for assets ownership and introducing new funding mechanisms for non- financial assets;",""],[1,"96","1","Corporate Equity Enhancement Programmes","Corporate equity enhancement programmes will be continued to increase Bumiputera equity ownership with effective control such as private equity investments by EKUINAS, SJJB and Program Pembangunan Usahawan Korporat (The Baron).",""],[1,"96","1","Amanah Saham Bumiputera Portfolio Diversification","PNB will further diversify the Amanah Saham Bumiputera (ASB) portfolio of investment into property to maximise returns to unit holders.",""],[1,"96","1","Acquisition of High-Potential Companies and Profitable PLCs","Other Bumiputera agencies and institutions will also be focusing on the acquisition of high potential companies and profitable PLCs.",""],[1,"96","2","Divestment of Profitable Non-Core GLC and GLIC Assets to Bumiputera Entrepreneurs","Divestment of profitable non-core GLCs and GLICs assets and activities to genuine Bumiputera entrepreneurs will continue to be implemented to increase Bumiputera effective direct individual ownership.",""],[1,"96","3","EPF Account 1 Withdrawal for ASB2 Unit Purchase","Bumiputera individual equity ownership will be expanded by allowing withdrawal from Account 1 of the Employee Provident Fund to purchase ASB2 units, which provide competitive long-term returns at minimal risk.",""],[1,"96","3","Crowdfunding-Based Waqf and Private Equity Funding Mechanisms","New funding mechanisms, such as waqf investment fund and private equity for investment will be created through crowd funding to invest in profitable and high potential companies.",""],[1,"96","4","Strengthening Institutional-Based Bumiputera Property Ownership Programmes","Institutional-based programmes including Bumiputera REIT will continue to be strengthened to enhance Bumiputera ownership of large commercial and residential properties in strategic locations.",""],[1,"96","4","Malay Reserve and Waqf Land Development Collaboration","Yayasan Wakaf Malaysia, state Islamic religious councils, and other Bumiputera- based institutions will collaborate to develop Malay reserve and waqf land to unlock value while retaining Bumiputera ownership.",""],[1,"96","5","Bumiputera Unsold Property Purchase Mechanism","A mechanism to enable Bumiputera institutions to purchase unsold Bumiputera lots in new property developments will be introduced.",""],[1,"96","5","Strategic Business Space Acquisition for Bumiputera Entrepreneurs","EDOs such as MARA, TEKUN Nasional and Perbadanan Usahawan Nasional Berhad (PUNB) will continue to acquire strategic business spaces or shop lots to be rented to Bumiputera entrepreneurs.",""],[1,"97","1","Affordable Housing Development for Bumiputera Households","more affordable houses will be developed by utilising funds including a clawback funding mechanism.",""],[1,"97","1","Bumiputera Commercial Property Revolving Fund","Bumiputera Commercial Property Revolving Fund will be established to assist entrepreneurs to acquire commercial properties.",""]],"45":[[1,"129","1","TVET Transformation for Industry Demand","The Government will focus on four areas: improving the efficiency of the labour market to accelerate economic growth, transforming TVET to meet industry demand, strengthening lifelong learning for skills enhancement, and improving the quality of the education system for better student outcomes and institutional excellence.",""],[1,"134","6","Public TVET Programme Rationalisation","One initiative involved the rationalisation of programmes offered by public TVET institutions to avoid duplication as well as enhance specialisation.",""],[1,"146","1","TVET Industry Collaboration and Quality Improvement Strategy","The Government will therefore intensify collaboration with industry to increase intake in TVET, improve the quality of programmes and institutions, and improve the sector's overall branding and profile.",""],[1,"146","2","TVET Governance Strengthening and Qualification Framework Harmonisation","Strengthening the governance of TVET for better management, through the streamlining of the national qualification framework, and harmonising of various rating systems across both private and public TVET institutions;",""],[1,"146","3","TVET Programme Quality and Delivery Enhancement","Strategy B2: Enhancing quality and delivery of TVET programmes to improve graduate employability, by enabling industries to lead curriculum development, eliminating the duplication of programmes and resources, enhancing cost efficiency, and increasing enrolment;",""],[1,"146","6","Single Accreditation System","Establishing a single system for accreditation",""],[1,"146","7","Single TVET Accreditation and Coordination System","The current fragmented TVET sector will be consolidated through the establishment of a single system adopted by both MQA and DSD to facilitate better coordination and monitoring of the TVET sector.",""],[1,"146","10","Unified TVET Rating System","The Government will harmonise the various rating systems across private and public TVET institutions into a single system.",""],[1,"148","6","Industry-TVET Provider Collaboration Across the Value Chain","Industry and TVET providers collaborate across the entire value chain from student recruitment, through to curriculum design, delivery, and job placement;",""],[1,"148","8","System Harmonisation and Streamlining Initiative","Achieving these aspirations will require harmonising and streamlining how the system currently operates to reduce fragmentation across the various public and private stakeholders.",""],[1,"149","8","Institutional Rationalisation and Consolidation of TVET Providers","The Government will prioritise improving existing institutions rather than investing in new ones.",""],[1,"149","8","Shared Facilities and Best-Practice Collaboration for TVET Providers","Public and private TVET providers will be encouraged to share facilities, faculty and best practices, and to deliver their programmes in as cost-efficient a manner as possible.",""],[1,"149","9","Student Development Fund Support for TVET Programmes","The SDF will continue to provide funding for students who pursue TVET programmes that are highly demanded by industry and delivered by TVET institutions with good performance ratings.",""],[1,"149","9","Standardised Public TVET Fee Structure","Fees in public TVET institutions will be standardised based on the type and level of programme.",""]],"46":[[1,"154","2","21st Century School Curriculum Reform","The school curriculum will embed knowledge, skills, and values that are relevant to the 21st century.",""],[1,"154","2","Multilingual Student Proficiency Initiative","Students will be proficient in Bahasa Melayu and English, and be encouraged to learn a third language.",""],[1,"154","2","Higher-Order Thinking Skills Teaching Reform","Teachers will embed HOTS in their lessons to develop critical, creative,and innovative thinkers.",""],[1,"154","2","STEM Education Reinforcement Programme","STEM (science, technology, engineering, and mathematics) education will continue to be reinforced through enquiry-based and hands-on learning opportunities.",""],[1,"154","2","Primary School TIMSS Participation Expansion","Participation in the TIMSS assessment will be extended to primary school students to provide a basis for earlier interventions.",""]],"47":[[1,"154","6","Competency-Based Professional Development Programme for Teachers and School Leaders","A comprehensive, competency-based professional development programme will be rolled out for in-service teachers and school leaders.",""],[1,"154","6","Continuous Enhancement of Teacher Education Lecturer Quality and Pre-Service Curriculum","The quality of ITE lecturers and the pre-service teacher training curriculum will also be continuously enhanced.",""]],"48":[[1,"129","1","Lifelong Learning and Skills Enhancement","The Government will focus on four areas: improving the efficiency of the labour market to accelerate economic growth, transforming TVET to meet industry demand, strengthening lifelong learning for skills enhancement, and improving the quality of the education system for better student outcomes and institutional excellence.",""],[1,"142","7","Lifelong Learning and Continuous Skills Development","The existing workforce will move from a world where learning only happens during one's youth, to one where every person has the opportunity to continuously enrich and develop themselves.",""],[1,"149","9","Employee Upskilling and Reskilling Loan Mechanism Reform","The existing SDF loan mechanism for employee upskilling and reskilling will also be revamped to increase the number of recipients through a cost-sharing arrangement with industry.",""],[1,"150","1","Lifelong Learning Access Expansion and Quality Improvement","The Government will widen access to LLL and raise the quality of existing programmes, with the goal of making LLL a way of life for all Malaysians.",""],[1,"150","2","Industry-Based Training Programme Expansion","Strategy C1: Improving effectiveness of programmes to meet learning needs, by increasing the use of industry-based training programmes, streamlining community-based programmes, and introducing entrepreneurship training in high-value economic sectors;",""],[1,"150","2","Community-Based Programme Streamlining","Strategy C1: Improving effectiveness of programmes to meet learning needs, by increasing the use of industry-based training programmes, streamlining community-based programmes, and introducing entrepreneurship training in high-value economic sectors;",""],[1,"150","2","Entrepreneurship Training in High-Value Sectors","Strategy C1: Improving effectiveness of programmes to meet learning needs, by increasing the use of industry-based training programmes, streamlining community-based programmes, and introducing entrepreneurship training in high-value economic sectors;",""],[1,"150","3","Regulatory and Funding Support for Prior Learning Recognition and HRDF Expansion","Strategy C2: Improving regulatory and funding support to broaden access through the enhancement of existing frameworks for recognising prior learning, and expanded HRDF support for new sectors and target groups.",""],[1,"151","4","Entrepreneurship Training Programme Strengthening","Agencies such as Institut Keusahawanan Negara (INSKEN), Majlis Amanah Rakyat (MARA), and Malaysian Global Innovation and Creativity Centre (MaGIC) will strengthen entrepreneurship related training programmes for high-income economic sectors in collaboration with industry.",""],[1,"151","4","MaGIC Go2Market Business Incubation Programme","MaGIC, through its Go2Market programme in partnership with the Stanford Graduate School of Business will help innovators incubate and set up successful businesses.",""],[1,"151","4","Youth Entrepreneurship Education and Extracurricular Development","Additionally, the Government will nurture an entrepreneurial spirit in youth from an early age, through the formal curriculum in schools, IHEs, TVET institutions, as well as through extracurricular activities.",""],[1,"151","5","Community College Lifelong Learning Curriculum Task Force","A task force headed by the Department of Community College will be formed to enhance LLL curricula, reduce redundancies, and optimise resources at the community level.","Department of Community College"],[1,"151","5","Community-Relevant Programme Portfolio Review","The portfolio of programmes offered by relevant agencies will be reviewed to ensure relevance to the specific needs of the community it serves, with training being delivered in existing facilities.",""],[1,"151","6","Expansion of HRDF Act Coverage","The coverage of the HRDF Act, 2001, will be expanded to include more subsectors under the services and agriculture sectors.",""],[1,"151","6","SME Training Collaboration with SME Corp","HRDF will also collaborate with SME Corp to provide training to SMEs not covered under the HRDF Act.",""],[1,"151","7","Recognition of Prior Learning and Prior Experiential Learning Enhancement","The Recognition of Prior Learning (RPL) programme under the DSD and Accreditation of Prior Experiential Learning (APEL) under the MQA will be enhanced to make it easier for employees to continue their education.",""],[1,"151","7","MyPhD-Industry Enrolment Expansion","In addition, the Government will encourage higher enrolment into the MyPhD-Industry programme.",""],[1,"151","8","Future Workers Training Scheme","The Future Workers Training (FWT) Scheme will be established under the HRDF to promote pre-employment training focusing on emerging technologies.",""]],"49":[[1,"154","7","Expansion of K9 Schools","The K9 school concept, which offers primary and lower secondary education under one roof, will be expanded to improve enrolment, especially among Orang Asli children.",""],[1,"154","7","Integrated Living Skills and Basic Vocational Education Curriculum Enhancement","The K9 school curriculum will also emphasise the teaching and learning of the Integrated Living Skills subject and Basic Vocational Education.",""],[1,"154","7","Special Education Facilities Upgrade","More schools will be equipped with facilities to cater for students with special education needs.",""],[1,"154","7","Expansion of Religious Stream Classes","To cater to rising demand for religious education, the religious stream classes or Kelas Aliran Agama (KAA) will be expanded in primary and secondary schools.",""],[1,"154","7","Registration Expansion of Government-Aided Religious Schools","The number of registered Sekolah Agama Bantuan Kerajaan (SABK) will also be increased, with a target of registering at least 10 private and state religious schools every year over the next five years.",""]],"50":[[1,"138","8","Graduate Employability Tracer Study","The Graduate Employability Tracer Study is an annual survey done by MoE to understand the status of employment for graduates within three to six months of graduation.","MoE"],[1,"142","1","World-Class Talent Development Initiative","The Eleventh Malaysia Plan will produce a fundamental shift in how the system currently operates in order to develop world-class talent that can thrive in a globally competitive economy.",""],[1,"144","8","Industry Centres of Excellence and Academia-Industry Graduate Development Centres","Industry Centres of Excellence (ICoE) and Academia-Industry Graduate Development Centres (AIGDC) in universities will also help address mismatches in the labour market.",""],[1,"145","1","Industry-Relevant Curriculum Development through ICoEs","industry will be used for the development of industry-relevant curricula.",""],[1,"147","2","Graduate Employability Programme Rationalisation","Low-impact programmes that are not in demand by industry and that yield low graduate employability will be eliminated.",""],[1,"147","2","Graduate Tracer Study System Upgrade and Expansion","The existing centralised system for tracer studies for public institutions will be upgraded and expanded to private institutions to enable comparisons of graduate employability.",""],[1,"147","2","Industry Dialogue-Based Programme Validation","more industry engagement in the form of scheduled dialogues will be conducted for continuous programme assessment and validation.",""],[1,"147","2","University Specialisation and Centres of Excellence Initiative","Overlapping programmes among public institutions will be reduced by encouraging them to specialise and create Centres of Excellence in niche areas of expertise in order to optimise resources and produce better student outcomes.",""],[1,"148","8","Industry-Led Graduate Supply Programmes","Furthermore, efforts will be made to encourage industry-led interventions and programmes as they are the stakeholders best placed to ensure that the supply of graduates meet their requirements.",""],[1,"252","1","Graduate Employability Skills and Internship Programme","Initiatives will focus on delivering the skills most critical to industries through existing graduate employability programmes.",""],[1,"252","1","Industry-Higher Education Collaboration and Structured Internship Programme","Greater collaboration between industries and higher education institutions will also be fostered, including the provision of more structured internship programmes.",""],[1,"252","1","Government-SME Co-funded Scholarship Programme","A co-funded scholarship programme between the Government and SMEs will be developed to enable the latter to tap on high-quality talent.",""],[1,"252","2","ICT Professional Regulatory Body","Within the ICT industry, a professional body to govern professional competencies and ethics in ICT will be considered to ensure ICT professionals' competencies are on par with global standards.",""],[1,"252","3","Compulsory and Elective ICT Curriculum Expansion","ICT will be offered as a compulsory subject at the lower secondary level and as an elective at the upper secondary level",""],[1,"253","1","Services Export Upskilling Programme","upskilling programmes to improve service providers' knowledge of international market opportunities, export requirements, and processes.",""],[1,"256","17","Industry-Led Workforce Skills Training","Enhance industry-led training for local workforce skills development",""],[1,"256","23","Frontier Products Workforce Skills Development","Develop workforce skills and capabilities in producing frontier products",""],[1,"264","4","SME Worker Reskilling and Upskilling through Industry Partnerships","Strengthening human capital development within SMEs by reskilling and upskilling workers through industry partnerships;",""],[1,"264","10","TVET Curriculum Strengthening with Industry Input","Curriculum for TVET will be strengthened with greater input from the industry to equip workers in SMEs with the right skill sets.",""],[1,"264","10","Worker Reskilling and Upskilling Initiative","In addition, reskilling and upskilling of workers will be intensified to enable them to fill higher-paying jobs.",""],[1,"264","10","Workforce Entry Standards and Entrepreneurship Promotion","Other measures to strengthen human capital development include ensuring new entrants into the workforce meet industry requirements and creating an entrepreneurial culture in the society.",""]],"51":[[1,"79","1","B40 Upskilling and Job Opportunity Initiative","as upskilling and providing job opportunities to the 2.7 million B40 households, will increase the nation's skilled workforce and reduce inequality passed on to future generations",""],[1,"79","2","School Dropout Reduction Initiative","reducing school dropouts; enhancing accessibility to higher education and skills training; increasing productivity through adoption of modern technology; enhancing adoption of information and communications technology; enhancing integrated entrepreneurship support; developing community- and social-based enterprises; incentivising investment in majority B40 households areas; and increasing wealth ownership through investment programmes;",""],[1,"79","2","Higher Education and Skills Training Access Expansion","enhancing accessibility to higher education and skills training; increasing productivity through adoption of modern technology; enhancing adoption of information and communications technology; enhancing integrated entrepreneurship support; developing community- and social-based enterprises; incentivising investment in majority B40 households areas; and increasing wealth ownership through investment programmes;",""],[1,"79","5","Employer Incentives for Employee Higher Education","employers will be incentivised to encourage their employees to pursue higher education and skill levels.",""],[1,"79","5","Soft Loan Facilities for Further Study","incentives such as soft loan facilities will be provided to employees to further their studies to enable them to secure better paying jobs for more comfortable living.",""],[1,"79","5","Advanced Skills Training Programmes","more programmes in advanced skills training will be provided to enable them to enhance their opportunity to compete for higher paying jobs in technical areas.",""],[1,"81","5","Rural Student Support Facilities","Appropriate facilities such as hostel, transport, and financial aid will continue to be provided to students in rural and remote areas to enable them to complete primary and secondary education.",""],[1,"81","5","K9 School Expansion","The K9 School2 will be expanded to increase student enrolment, particularly among the Orang Asli in Peninsular Malaysia, and those living in the rural and remote areas in Sabah and Sarawak.",""],[1,"81","5","Education Awareness Campaigns for Schoolchildren and Parents","Special awareness programmes on the importance of education will be conducted for schoolchildren and their parents to inspire a mindset change.",""],[1,"81","6","Special Higher Education and Skills Training Access Programmes","Accessibility to higher education and skills training among students from B40 households will be enhanced through special programmes.",""],[1,"81","6","Preferential Entry and Enrolment Quota for Disadvantaged Students","Institutions of higher learning and skills training will be encouraged to provide more places for these students through preferential entry qualification criteria and enrolment quota.",""],[1,"81","6","Financial Aid for Higher Education and Skills Training","This will be complemented with the provision of financial aid.",""],[1,"81","6","Special Access Support for Orang Asli and Rural Students","Special consideration will be given to potential students from Orang Asli communities in Peninsular Malaysia, and those living in rural and remote areas in Sabah and Sarawak.",""],[1,"89","2","Inclusive Education Opportunity Expansion","a range of initiatives to increase education opportunities especially for disadvantaged and disabled children, will be implemented.",""]],"52":[[1,"146","4","TVET Rebranding and Promotion Campaign","This will be achieved through promotional activities highlighting TVET as an attractive career choice.",""],[1,"149","10","Instructor Professional Development Enhancement Programme","Professional development programmes for instructors will be improved by incorporating more industrial training and attachment programmes.",""],[1,"149","10","Centralized Instructor Profile Repository","A centralised repository of instructor profiles will be established to identify competency gaps and enable the development of an effective training roadmap.",""],[1,"149","10","Industry Expert Recruitment Incentive Scheme for TVET Instructors","Besides these, more industry experts including retired industry practitioners will be encouraged to serve as TVET instructors through the provision of attractive remuneration packages.",""],[1,"149","11","TVET Promotion and Career Guidance Campaigns","SkillsMalaysia will drive a series of targeted media campaigns to educate students and families on the attractive career and entrepreneurship opportunities that TVET programmes can offer.",""],[1,"149","11","TVET Student Career Guidance and Success Story Outreach","Such promotional efforts will offer students meaningful career guidance and showcase success stories.",""],[1,"149","11","TVET Skills Competitions Promotion Platform","The MySkills Competition and International Skills Competition for TVET students will also be used as platforms to boost the image of TVET.",""]],"53":[[1,"152","4","Curriculum Soft and Entrepreneurial Skills Integration","embedding soft and entrepreneurial skills in the curriculum",""],[1,"152","4","Industry Collaboration in Programme Design and Delivery","collaborating with industry in the design and delivery of programmes",""],[1,"152","4","Research Quality Enhancement Initiative","enhancing the quality of research",""],[1,"152","4","University Innovation and Industry Solutions Role Strengthening","strengthening the role of IHEs as a conduit for innovation and as solution providers to industry and community",""],[1,"152","4","MOOCs in Niche Areas of Expertise","launching massive open online courses (MOOCs) in niche areas of expertise",""],[1,"152","5","Public University Earned Autonomy Reform","Measures include empowering public universities through earned autonomy within the regulatory framework, linking government funding to performance and encouraging public universities to diversify their funding sources.",""],[1,"155","6","Entrepreneurship Education Integration Across the Curriculum","Entrepreneurial skills will be embedded across the curriculum to instil a \"job creator\" mindset in all graduates.",""],[1,"155","6","University Entrepreneurship Course Enhancement","Public universities will be encouraged to increase the practical component in entrepreneurship courses, introduce entrepreneurship minors in academic programmes, and emphasise entrepreneurship education for students in professional courses such as engineering, pharmacy, and medicine.",""],[1,"155","6","Integrated Graduate Attributes Assessment Reform","Other vital student attributes such as language proficiency, leadership skills, and ethics and spirituality will also be embedded across the curriculum and assessed through an integrated cumulative grade point average.",""],[1,"155","6","Graduate English Proficiency Improvement Requirement","To improve English proficiency among graduates in public universities, students will be required to improve their performance in the Malaysian University English Test (MUET) by at least one band upon graduation.",""],[1,"155","7","Industry-Aligned Higher Education Curriculum Revision","IHEs will periodically and systematically revise their curriculum to keep abreast of changing industry needs.",""],[1,"155","7","Industry-Collaborative New Programme Development","the development of any new programmes will be done in close collaboration with industry.",""],[1,"155","7","Removal of Irrelevant Higher Education Programmes","Programme offerings that are irrelevant to industry will be eliminated.",""],[1,"155","7","Mandatory Extended Industrial Training for Students","Industrial training for students will be made compulsory and its duration will be extended to better prepare them for entry into the workforce.",""],[1,"155","7","Industry Attachment Programme for Teaching Staff","Teaching staff will also be given the opportunity to update their knowledge and skills through industry attachments.",""],[1,"155","7","Recruitment of Industry Practitioners as Faculty","IHEs will also recruit more industry practitioners as faculty members.",""],[1,"156","1","MOOC Launch in Niche Areas of Expertise","The Government will launch MOOCs in niche areas of expertise for Malaysia, make online learning an integral component of all teaching and learning, and support eligible IHEs in establishing the required cyber infrastructure in areas where none exist yet.",""],[1,"156","3","Innovation Ecosystem Development in Strategic Areas","The Government will facilitate the development of innovation ecosystems in selected strategic areas that are critical to the nation's economic growth.",""],[1,"156","3","Industry-Academia-Community Innovation Partnerships","IHEs will be encouraged to partner with industry, government and local communities to incubate, develop, and commercialise ideas and to establish supporting systems such as technology transfer offices and mechanisms for co-utilisation of facilities.",""],[1,"156","3","Private-Public Research Network Investment Platform","The Government will in turn play a catalytic role in securing investments from the private sector through platforms like the Private-Public Research Network.",""],[1,"156","5","International Higher Education Branding and Promotion Initiative","The branding of Malaysian IHEs will be reinforced in strategic markets such as Southeast Asia, Middle East and Central Asia.",""],[1,"156","6","Earned Autonomy for Public Universities","Empowering public universities through earned autonomy within the regulatory framework",""],[1,"156","7","University Governance and Autonomy Reform","The role of MoE will be transformed from that of a tight controller to a regulator and policy-maker by empowering public universities with greater decision rights.","MoE"],[1,"156","8","Public University Funding Formula Reform","The Government will revise the funding formulae for public universities by replacing block grants with performance-linked and per student funding, and implementing performance contracts.",""],[1,"156","8","University Revenue Diversification and Cost Optimisation","Public universities will be encouraged to diversify revenue sources and implement cost optimisation measures.",""],[1,"156","8","PTPTN Reform and Efficiency Enhancement","Reform efforts by Perbadanan Tabung Pendidikan Tinggi Nasional (PTPTN) will be intensified further to address issues of sustainability, equitable disbursement, and operational efficiencies.",""],[1,"156","8","Household Income-Based Education Financing Assessment","All applications and approvals will be evaluated based on household income and the databases of e-Kasih and Bantuan Rakyat 1 Malaysia (BR1M).",""],[1,"156","8","PTPTN Educational Financing Services Expansion","PTPTN will also manage educational financing services for other agencies to increase revenue and lower its own operational cost.",""]],"54":[[1,"14","20","Broadband Coverage Expansion and Digital Terrestrial Television Migration","Increasing broadband coverage and initiating migration to Digital Terrestrial Television (DTT)",""],[1,"27","6","Broadband Expansion and Digital Affordability Initiative","Digital access will be increased through both broadband infrastructure expansion and initiatives to ensure their affordability.",""],[1,"82","4","ICT Adoption Acceleration Initiative","The adoption of ICT will be accelerated to increase access to information on agriculture, business, education and health, and expand business and income earning opportunities to improve wellbeing.",""],[1,"191","5","Broadband Coverage Expansion and Digital Terrestrial Television Migration","Increasing broadband coverage and initiating migration to Digital Terrestrial Television",""],[1,"193","1","National Broadband Initiative Fibre Rollout","Under the National Broadband Initiative, 55,801 km of fibre was rolled out, increasing the broadband penetration to 70.2% of Malaysia's households.",""],[1,"193","2","Broadband Infrastructure Roll-Out in Non-Urban Areas","Digital connectivity will also be expanded through broadband infrastructure roll-out in non-urban areas, bringing connectivity and choice to even more regions and households.",""],[1,"200","2","Free-to-Air Digital Terrestrial Television Rollout","Free-to-Air Digital Terrestrial Television (DTT), offering digital television and radio services is scheduled to be launched by end of 2015.",""],[1,"206","3","Broadband Infrastructure Expansion Initiative","To achieve this, the reach of broadband infrastructure to 95% of populated areas is targeted, along with its affordability - targeting 1% of gross national income (GNI) per capita for fixed broadband cost.",""],[1,"206","3","High-Speed Broadband 2 Roll-out","Key infrastructure roll-out initiatives such as High-Speed Broadband 2 (HSBB 2), Sub- Urban Broadband (SUBB), and Digital Terrestrial Television (DTT) will be undertaken during this period, along with policies to improve access pricing and consumer protection frameworks.",""],[1,"206","3","Sub-Urban Broadband Roll-out","Key infrastructure roll-out initiatives such as High-Speed Broadband 2 (HSBB 2), Sub- Urban Broadband (SUBB), and Digital Terrestrial Television (DTT) will be undertaken during this period, along with policies to improve access pricing and consumer protection frameworks.",""],[1,"206","3","Digital Terrestrial Television Roll-out","Key infrastructure roll-out initiatives such as High-Speed Broadband 2 (HSBB 2), Sub- Urban Broadband (SUBB), and Digital Terrestrial Television (DTT) will be undertaken during this period, along with policies to improve access pricing and consumer protection frameworks.",""],[1,"218","1","Digital Infrastructure Expansion and Affordability Initiative","Malaysia aspires to ensure that its citizens and economy keep pace with the digital global economy by expanding the successful roll-out of digital technologies such as the High-Speed Broadband (HSBB) and Digital Terrestrial Television (DTT).",""],[1,"218","2","Broadband Infrastructure Expansion and Upgrade","Strategy C1: Expanding and upgrading broadband infrastructure through deploying broadband as an essential service, improving connectivity from international to last-mile connections, and integrating digital infrastructure planning;",""],[1,"218","6","Digital Infrastructure Investment and Connectivity Improvement","Policy measures to encourage investments in digital infrastructure will be undertaken by improving connectivity from international to last-mile connections to households.",""],[1,"218","6","Interagency Coordination for Digital Infrastructure Measures","Greater coordination between relevant government agencies will ensure these measures are integrated and coherent.",""],[1,"218","7","Mandatory Ready-to-Use Communication Infrastructure for New Developments","An amendment in 2011 to the Uniform Building By-Laws (UBBL), 1984 stipulates that communication installations is one of the essential services similar to water and electricity under the certification for completion and compliance of buildings.",""],[1,"218","8","International and Last-Mile Bandwidth Capacity Upgrade","Measures will be undertaken to improve the international to last-mile bandwidth capacity to meet the expected demand of 41 terabytes per second (Tbps) during the Eleventh Plan.",""],[1,"218","8","High-Speed Broadband 2 and Suburban Broadband Deployment","Efforts will also be undertaken to enhance connectivity through deployment of the High-Speed Broadband 2 (HSBB 2) and Suburban Broadband (SUBB) for a more holistic coverage in all state capitals and selected high-impact growth areas as shown in Exhibit 7-11.",""],[1,"220","1","Regulatory Review for International Connectivity and Submarine Cable Landing","A review of the regulatory framework for international connectivity and promotion of a conducive environment to encourage international submarine cables to land in Malaysia will be undertaken.",""],[1,"220","2","Digital Infrastructure Planning and Broadband Deployment Collaboration","Collaboration amongst the Ministry of Communications and Multimedia, Malaysian Communications and Multimedia Commission (MCMC), state governments, and local authorities will be strengthened on the planning and deployment of digital infrastructure.","Ministry of Communications and Multimedia | Malaysian Communications and Multimedia Commission (MCMC) | state governments | local authorities"],[1,"220","3","Access Pricing Framework Improvement","The APF will be improved to facilitate competition and infrastructure sharing among service providers.",""],[1,"252","6","Improvement of Digital Infrastructure in Sabah and Sarawak","In addition, access to digital infrastructure, particularly in Sabah and Sarawak, will be further improved to spur the growth of knowledge-intensive services.",""]],"55":[[1,"154","4","1BestariNet Virtual Learning Environment Strengthening","The MoE will strengthen the use of the 1BestariNet Virtual Learning Environment (VLE) platform in schools.","MoE"],[1,"154","4","Digital Content Development Roadmap","A digital content development roadmap will be formulated to ensure that more resources are developed - from digital textbooks to adaptive learning programmes - to support online learning and supplement the existing 24,000 resources.","MoE"],[1,"154","4","Virtual Lessons and Personalized Learning Delivery","The MoE will use these resources to deliver virtual lessons and offer more personalised learning opportunities to students.","MoE"]],"57":[[1,"287","12","Cloud Computing for Data Consolidation and Sharing","Establishing cloud computing for consolidation and data sharing",""],[1,"290","4","Open Data Expansion and Cross-Agency Data Sharing","This will require proliferating open data among agencies, encouraging cross-agency data sharing, and leveraging big data analytics (BDA);",""],[1,"291","7","National Open Data Initiative","MAMPU will spearhead the National Open Data initiative in collaboration with the Multimedia Development Corporation (MDeC) to enable the innovative use of government data.","MAMPU | Multimedia Development Corporation (MDeC)"],[1,"291","8","Open Data Legislative and Guideline Review","Review legislation and guidelines that hinder implementation of open data;",""],[1,"291","9","Public Sector Open Data Framework","Establish an open data framework for the public sector across federal, state, and local authorities;",""],[1,"291","10","Open Data Implementation Roadmap","Develop an open data implementation roadmap as a guideline to agencies;",""],[1,"291","11","Public Awareness Communication Plan","Implement a communication plan to increase awareness among agencies and the public.",""],[1,"291","13","Government Data Sharing Cloud Platform","The Government will focus on the implementation of data sharing.",""],[1,"292","1","Public Sector Cloud Computing Infrastructure","The public sector cloud computing infrastructure is a dedicated cloud to host government applications and data.",""],[1,"292","3","Data Security and Access Control Strengthening","Strengthened security - incorporate data security with adequate access controls to manage usage of sensitive data;",""],[1,"292","5","Faster Deployment of Agency Applications","Faster deployment - enable agencies to run their applications faster as a result of improved manageability and lower maintenance requirements; and",""],[1,"292","6","Real-Time Document Collaboration Platform","Ease of collaboration - allow real time collaboration where documents are stored in a central location and can be accessed by multiple users.",""],[1,"292","7","Public Sector Big Data Analytics Blueprint","The BDA Blueprint for the public sector will be formulated, which will encompass governance mechanisms, communication plan and capability building.",""],[1,"292","7","Big Data Analytics Implementation Using Existing Government Infrastructure","The implementation of BDA will utilise existing government infrastructure such as 1Gov*Net and GDC.",""],[1,"292","10","Multi-Channel Mobile Service Delivery","Deploying multiple channels of delivery focusing on mobile platforms;",""],[1,"292","11","Cyber Security Protection for Critical Online Transactions","Strengthening cyber security protection in critical online transactions;",""]],"58":[[1,"103","2","Mass Sports Participation and Youth Leadership Development","Finally, emphasis will be placed on mass sports participation, developing high-performance athletes, and building youth leadership capabilities in sports and sports-related activities.",""],[1,"110","4","Sports for All Mass Participation Programme","During the Tenth Plan, \"Sports for All\" was promoted to encourage mass participation in sports, recreational, and fitness activities.",""],[1,"114","3","Mass Sports Participation and Talent Development Programme","Finally, the Government will further promote mass sports participation to achieve healthy minds and bodies, and improve programmes to identify and build world-class sporting talent.",""],[1,"124","2","Mass Sports Participation Promotion Strategy","Strategy F1: Promoting mass sports participation at all levels of society to instil a sports culture.",""],[1,"124","5","Community Sports Participation Expansion","The Government will focus on strategies to make Malaysia a sporting nation with extensive community participation in various sports, fitness, and recreational activities.",""],[1,"124","5","Expansion of Iconic Sports Programmes","Iconic programmes such as FitMalaysia, Sports for All League, Sports for PWD, and futsal championships will be expanded.",""],[1,"124","5","Public Park Community Sports Use","Public parks will be used for recreational and community sporting events.",""],[1,"124","6","Sports Programme and Facility Partnership Strengthening","government, private sector, and NGOs in promoting and implementing sports programmes, as well as providing and maintaining sports facilities will be strengthened.",""],[1,"125","1","Mass Sports Participation Initiative","The Eleventh Plan therefore aims to improve wellbeing through six focus areas: enabling universal access to quality healthcare; providing adequate and quality affordable housing; creating safer living environments; improving road safety and emergency services; fostering social cohesion and national unity; and increasing mass participation in sports.",""]],"59":[[1,"124","3","Youth Leadership in Sports Development Programme","Strategy F2: Developing youth leadership in sports.",""],[1,"124","4","High-Performance Athlete Development Programme","Strategy F3: Developing high-performance athletes for global prominence through specialised training programmes, more rigorous compliance with international standards and the hosting of international sports events.",""],[1,"124","7","Sports Skill Enhancement Programmes","The Government will invest in more skill enhancement programmes to improve the professionalism of youth and leaders in sports and sports associations.",""],[1,"124","7","Comprehensive Sports Leadership Development Programme","Comprehensive sports leadership programmes, particularly in events, integrated sports management and coach education programmes, will be enhanced to develop potential leaders in sports and sports-related activities.",""],[1,"124","8","Talent Identification Programme for Olympic Athlete Development","In preparation for the 2020 Olympic Games, talent identification programmes will be conducted at schools and institutions of higher education to identify potential athletes.",""],[1,"124","8","Comprehensive Athlete Training and Sports Facilities Upgrade","Comprehensive training programmes will also be developed and sports facilities improved.",""],[1,"124","8","Anti-Doping Capacity Strengthening and Awareness Programme","the capability of the Anti-Doping Agency of Malaysia (ADAMAS) will be enhanced to meet international standards and the requirements of the World Anti-Doping Agency in enforcing zero tolerance to doping.",""],[1,"124","8","National Doping Awareness and Education Programme","ADAMAS will also conduct awareness and education programmes on doping among athletes nationwide.",""],[1,"124","8","International Sports Event Hosting Initiative","Malaysia will continue to host international sports events and tournaments to provide a platform to showcase Malaysia's sporting talent.",""]],"60":[[1,"291","3","Green Procurement Implementation","The Government will play a catalytic role to bring transformative changes to spur green growth through the implementation of green procurement.",""],[1,"291","3","Green Growth Enabling Environment Strengthening","efforts will be undertaken to reinforce the enabling environment for green growth by enhancing policy, regulatory, and institutional frameworks; creating sustainable green financing mechanisms; increasing capacity, capability, and skills; improving monitoring and evaluation mechanisms; and enhancing public awareness.",""]],"62":[[1,"165","4","Reuse, Reduce, and Recycle Programme","The Reuse, Reduce, and Recycle (3R) programme was intensified during the Tenth Plan",""],[1,"165","4","National Biomass Strategy 2020","To support waste-to-wealth initiatives, the National Biomass Strategy 2020 was launched in 2013 to assess how Malaysia will develop new industries by utilising agricultural biomass waste for high value products, including those for exports.",""],[1,"170","4","Comprehensive Waste Reuse, Reduce, and Recycle Strategy","Management of waste will shift towards a comprehensive reuse, reduce, and recycle (3R) approach that will reduce development of new landfills.",""],[1,"174","6","Holistic Waste Management Coordination and 3R Promotion","Strategy B5: Managing waste holistically through better coordination, encouraging 3R and using waste as a resource for other industries.",""],[1,"179","1","Integrated Waste Management and Recycling Improvement Initiative","All seven types of waste - solid, agricultural, construction, radioactive, mining, sewage, and scheduled waste - will be managed in a holistic manner based on a life cycle approach.",""],[1,"179","2","Waste Management Coordination Platform","A waste management platform that meets regularly to coordinate matters on sustainable and holistic waste management will be established.",""],[1,"179","3","3R Awareness and Education Programmes","Investments in 3R awareness and education programmes therefore need to continue during the Eleventh Plan to shape better consumption and waste disposal behaviour.",""],[1,"179","3","Household Waste Separation at Source Rollout","Waste separation at source for households will be implemented in selected states starting September 2015 and rolled out to other states subsequently during the Eleventh Plan.",""],[1,"179","4","Waste Recycling and Recovery Investment Initiatives","investing in waste recycling and recovery will also reduce dependency of industries on natural resources, as waste becomes a valuable resource - either converted to energy (e.g. biomass and food waste for power generation) or used as an input for other products.",""]],"63":[[1,"167","4","Biodiversity Policy and Legislation Review and Revision","relevant policy and legislation were reviewed to strengthen conservation and enforcement efforts.",""],[1,"170","2","Climate and Biodiversity Resilience Strengthening","the Eleventh Plan continues to strengthen the nation's resilience to natural disasters",""],[1,"180","1","Biodiversity Conservation and Enforcement Programme","Increasing enforcement against illegal deforestation and poaching and undertaking reforestation in affected areas will help towards this objective.",""],[1,"180","2","Natural Resources Conservation and Biosafety Strategy","Strategy C1: Ensuring natural resources security by conserving terrestrial and marine areas as well as endangered plant and wildlife species, managing natural resources and strengthening biosafety;",""],[1,"180","4","Sustainable Management of Natural Assets","Malaysia's natural assets such as forest and marine areas, plants and wildlife, as well as minerals will be managed sustainably.",""],[1,"180","4","Restocking of Threatened Natural Assets","Where threat of deforestation or extinction exists, special focus will be given to restock these assets.",""],[1,"180","4","Legal Framework for Conservation Support","Legal framework will provide institutional support to conservation efforts and promote rational use of biological resources.",""],[1,"180","5","Designation of Terrestrial and Marine Protected Areas","Important biodiversity areas will be gazetted as terrestrial and marine protected areas.",""],[1,"180","5","Reforestation and Forest Enrichment Programme","Reforestation and forest enrichment efforts will be undertaken in affected areas to improve degraded forests.",""],[1,"180","5","Illegal Deforestation Enforcement Measures","Measures to reduce illegal deforestation activities and forest degradation will be taken through stricter enforcement.",""],[1,"180","5","Marine Parks and Water Quality Improvement Measures","Similarly, relevant measures and strict enforcement will help improve the quality of marine parks as well as water quality throughout Malaysia.",""],[1,"180","5","Environmental Forensics for Site Remediation and Enforcement","Environmental forensics will be implemented to support site investigation, site remediation, and strengthen legal enforcement and resource management.",""],[1,"180","6","Endangered Species Conservation and Recovery Programme","Biodiversity conservation efforts will be increased by protecting, rehabilitating, breeding and restocking selected endangered plant and wildlife species such as the tiger, sambar deer, elephant, gaur, keruing layang, asam batu and slipper orchid in its natural habitat (in-situ) and outside its natural habitat (ex-situ).",""],[1,"180","6","Advanced Reproductive Technology for Endangered Species","New methods and technologies, including advanced reproductive technology, will be used to increase the population of endangered species.",""],[1,"180","6","Wildlife Enforcement and Anti-Poaching Network","1Malaysia Biodiversity Enforcement Operation Network initiatives to curb encroachment into protected areas and poaching of wildlife will be intensified.",""],[1,"188","2","Terrestrial and Marine Biodiversity Conservation Measures","The Government will strengthen efforts to enhance terrestrial and marine biodiversity through conservation measures.",""],[1,"188","2","River and Coastal Area Management Guidelines","Management of rivers and coastal areas will be improved by adoption of water management guidelines as well as continuation of conservation efforts, particularly mangrove forests and related coastal forest species, as shown in Exhibit 6-5.",""],[1,"338","14","Gazettement of Permanent Reserved Forests","Gazettement of Permanent Reserved Forest in Pahang, Perak and Selangor.",""],[1,"339","28","Permanent Reserved Forest Gazettement under the Central Forest Spine Initiative","Gazettement of 23,264 hectares of forest as Permanent Reserved Forest under the Central Forest Spine initiative",""],[1,"339","29","Revision of the National Policy on Biological Diversity","Revision of the National Policy on Biological Diversity 1998 in line with international biodiversity targets",""],[1,"339","29","Marine Park Management Plan Development","Development of management plans for marine parks in Pulau Sibu-Pulau Tinggi, Johor; Pulau Tioman, Pahang; and Pulau Redang, Terengganu",""],[1,"339","31","1Malaysia Biodiversity Enforcement Operation Network","Commencement of the 1Malaysia Biodiversity Enforcement Operation Network involving multiple enforcement agencies",""]],"64":[[1,"180","1","Access and Benefit-Sharing Regulatory Framework","the Eleventh Plan will lay the regulatory framework on access to biological resources and benefits sharing (ABS).",""],[1,"182","1","Natural Resource Inventory Database and Research Programme","Continuous research to identify the potential and value of natural resources, including minerals, will be undertaken.",""],[1,"182","1","Natural Resource Misappropriation Regulatory Framework","A holistic regulatory framework to curb the misappropriation of natural resources will be formulated.",""],[1,"182","1","Access and Benefit-Sharing Bill Finalisation","The Government will finalise the Bill of Access to Biological Resources and Benefits Sharing (ABS Bill) to regulate bioprospecting activities in Malaysia, ensuring that benefits are shared in a fair and equitable manner.",""],[1,"182","3","Strengthening of the Department of Biosafety","The Department of Biosafety, Ministry of Natural Resources and Environment (NRE) will be strengthened to increase its capacity and capability in assessing and evaluating harmful effects from emerging and new technology.","Ministry of Natural Resources and Environment (NRE)"],[1,"182","5","Access to Biological Resources and Benefit-Sharing Bill Finalization","The Ministry of Natural Resources and Environment is finalising the Bill of Access to Biological Resources and Benefits Sharing (ABS Bill) after robust consultation with various stakeholders such as federal and state agencies, NGOs, indigenous and local communities and the private sector;","The Ministry of Natural Resources and Environment"],[1,"182","6","Bioprospecting Regulation and Benefit-Sharing Bill","The objective of the Bill is to regulate bioprospecting activities in Malaysia and ensure that benefits are shared in a fair and equitable manner;",""],[1,"182","7","Access and Benefit-Sharing Legal Framework for Biological Resources","The Bill will provide a transparent framework allowing users to negotiate mutually agreed terms with providers prior to accessing biological resources.",""],[1,"183","3","Access and Benefit-Sharing Regulatory Reform","Sustainable use and benefits sharing of biological genetic resources and associated traditional knowledge will be promoted by regulatory measures such as the ABS Bill.",""]],"65":[[1,"271","12","Waste Management Guidelines and Enforcement","Efficient in waste management through guidelines on resource use and effective enforcement",""],[1,"317","4","Low-Carbon Economy and 6Rs Circular Economy Practices","The nation embraces the prospects of becoming a low carbon economy, which minimises waste.",""]],"66":[[1,"172","6","Revision and Strengthening of Environmental and Sustainability Regulations","Existing regulations such as the Environmental Quality Act, 1974; Solid Waste and Public Cleansing Management Act, 2007; National Policy on Climate Change, 2009; and biodiversity-related policies will be revised and strengthened to further encourage and support sustainable socio-economic development.",""],[1,"172","6","Development of New Sustainability Policy Frameworks","New policy framework, including the sustainable consumption and production (SCP) blueprint, sustainable development blueprint, national mitigation plan, and national policy on geospatial information management will be formulated.",""],[1,"172","6","Disaster Risk Management and Geospatial Information Legislation","Legislation on disaster risk management and geospatial information management will also be formulated to regulate and provide an enabling environment for green growth.",""],[1,"173","6","Environmental Impact Consideration in Development Project Planning and Evaluation","Negative externalities of socio-economic development will be taken into consideration when planning, evaluating, and implementing public and private sector development projects, to achieve the double dividend of higher economic growth and lower environmental impact.",""],[1,"174","1","Sustainable Consumption and Production Framework","The Government will take the lead in establishing the sustainable consumption and production (SCP) approach in prominent sectors in Malaysia including industry, power generation, infrastructure, and transportation.",""],[1,"174","1","SCP Regulatory Framework Development","This requires establishing relevant regulatory framework - standards, certifications and guidelines.",""]],"67":[[1,"27","9","Agricultural Modernisation and Sustainable Farming Programme","Agriculture will be modernised by promoting sustainable practices and adopting modern farming technology to generate high-income.",""],[1,"58","3","Agricultural Sector Modernisation and Productivity Enhancement","Emphasis will be on increasing productivity through the modernisation of the sector, supported by greater innovation and research",""],[1,"78","3","Modern Technology Adoption for Agricultural Productivity","Adoption of modern technology to increase productivity levels will be encouraged, especially in agricultural sector.",""],[1,"81","7","Modern Technology Adoption Support for Rural B40 Self-Employed Households","B40 households in rural areas who are self-employed such as farmers, fishermen, and smallholders will be encouraged to adopt modern technology to increase productivity and income.",""],[1,"81","7","Structured Modular Training in Modern Farming and Good Agricultural Practices","Structured modular programmes focusing on modern farming techniques and good agricultural practices will be intensified.",""],[1,"81","7","Land Amalgamation and Small Business Consolidation Support","Amalgamation of land and merging of small scale business activities will also be encouraged to benefit from economies of scale.",""],[1,"81","7","Streamlining of Agricultural Agency Service Delivery","The role of relevant agencies such as Federal Agricultural Marketing Authority (FAMA), Malaysian Agricultural Research and Development Institute (MARDI), and Fisheries Development Authority of Malaysia (LKIM) will be streamlined to provide relevant services and facilitation to these households.",""],[1,"82","1","Expansion of Large-Scale Plantation Programmes","Large-scale plantation programmes such as Agropolitan, Ladang Masyarakat, Mini Estet Sejahtera (MESEJ), and Rancangan Penempatan Semula (RPS) will be expanded.",""],[1,"82","1","Land Consolidation Through Cooperatives","Small-scale land holders will be encouraged to merge their plots to gain economies of scale and guarantee better income in the long-term through cooperatives.",""],[1,"82","2","Urban Farming in Abandoned Buildings and Unused Spaces","In urban areas, abandoned buildings and unused spaces will be utilised for urban farming through the use of modern techniques such as fertigation, hydroponics, and vertical farming.",""],[1,"82","2","Cooperative-Led Urban Farming Initiative for B40 Areas","Cooperative movements will spearhead this initiative in locations where the B40 households form the majority of the population.",""]],"68":[[1,"188","3","Agriculture Climate Modelling Research and Development","Research and development, especially in agriculture-climate modelling, will be intensified",""],[1,"188","3","Expansion of Good Agricultural Practices Adoption","adoption of good agricultural practices will be extended to 500 new fruit and vegetable plantations, 160 new farms and 65 new aquaculture farms",""],[1,"188","4","Climate-Related Disease Public Awareness Initiative","The objectives of this initiative is to enhance public awareness on climate-related diseases to improve public health.",""],[1,"259","1","Agriculture Sector Transformation and Modernisation","In the Eleventh Plan, the agriculture sector, namely the agro-food and industrial commodity subsectors will be transformed and modernised into a high-income and sustainable sector.",""],[1,"259","1","Agricultural Productivity, Skills, and Supply Chain Support","Efforts will be focused on ensuring food security, improving productivity, increasing skills of farmers, fishermen, and smallholders, enhancing support and delivery services, strengthening the supply chain and ensuring compliance to international market requirements.",""],[1,"259","1","Climate-Resilient Agricultural Practices","The development of the sector will also take into account the impact of climate change on sustainability of agricultural practices.",""],[1,"259","1","Modern Technology Adoption for Commodity Smallholders","Special focus will also be given to the industrial commodities smallholders to further boost productivity through the infusion of modern technologies with the aim of reducing labour dependency as well as to address low commodity prices through income stabilising measures.",""],[1,"259","2","Agricultural ICT and Farming Technology Adoption Programme","Improving productivity and income of farmers, fishermen, and smallholders by accelerating adoption of ICT and farming technology, preserving and optimising agricultural land, and intensifying R&D&C in priority areas;",""],[1,"259","9","ICT and Farming Technology Adoption Acceleration","Accelerating adoption of ICT and farming technology",""],[1,"259","10","Smart Farming Technology and ICT Expansion","The use of smart farming technologies and ICT in plantation, farming, livestock, and fishing activities will be intensified to improve production efficiency and reduce dependency on labour.",""],[1,"259","10","ICT-Based Farm and Plantation Management Systems","ICT-based applications to support farm and plantation management, precision farming, and monitoring and surveillance will be expanded to increase productivity and reduce the cost of production.",""],[1,"259","10","Agricultural Market Information and Advisory Platforms","Mobile phone applications and portals will be used to disseminate real-time information on market demand and prices, early detection and warning alerts on disease outbreaks as well as provide interactive platforms for technical advice.",""],[1,"259","11","Agricultural Land Gazettement and Preservation Incentives","State governments will be encouraged to gazette agricultural land, particularly granary areas and permanent food production parks, to preserve land for farming.",""],[1,"259","11","Farm Infrastructure Grants and Revenue Compensation","In this regard, incentives in the form of infrastructure including farm roads and grants will be provided to compensate for loss of revenue.",""],[1,"259","11","Integrated Farming and Inter-Cropping Intensification","Integrated farming and inter-cropping in farms and plantation areas will be intensified to optimise the use of agricultural land to increase the income of farmers.",""],[1,"259","11","Idle Land Bank Database and Leasing Mechanism","A land bank database for idle land will be established through the cooperation of ministries and state land offices.",""]],"69":[[1,"123","3","Arts and Culture Development and Heritage Promotion Programme","Arts and culture will be developed to promote a shared Malaysian culture and heritage, and offer another platform to embrace diversity and a shared national identity.",""],[1,"123","3","Traditional Heritage Talent Development Support","To promote cultural heritages like mak yong and wayang kulit, support will be given to develop the talent of interested individuals and communities.",""],[1,"123","3","Arts and Culture Research Intensification Initiative","Research in arts and culture will be intensified to ensure the authenticity and continuity of Malaysia's national heritage.",""],[1,"123","3","Community Access to Arts and Cultural Activities Initiative","Access to arts and cultural activities will also be enhanced and promoted through greater community participation.",""]],"71":[[1,"165","8","Energy-Efficient Appliance Rebate Scheme","Rebates offered to qualified customers for · Purchase of five star rated appliances, RM200 for refrigerators and RM100 for air-conditioners",""],[1,"165","9","Chiller Replacement for Energy Efficiency","Replacement of old chillers (>10 years) to energy efficient chillers, RM200 per RT1",""],[1,"169","2","Comprehensive Demand-Side Management Master Plan","Fomulation of a comprehensive demand side management master plan",""],[1,"170","4","Balanced Energy Security Management Measures","In the area of energy security, there will be a shift from a focus on supply-side solutions towards a stronger balance of both supply-side and demand side management measures.",""],[1,"174","4","Demand-Side Management Master Plan","Strategy B3: Enhancing demand side management (DSM) by formulating a comprehensive DSM master plan and expanding DSM measures;",""],[1,"177","4","Demand Side Management Initiative","Demand side management (DSM) marks an important paradigm shift for Malaysia towards efficient management of energy resources.",""],[1,"177","5","Demand-Side Management Programme Expansion","strategy will broaden and extend the successful outcomes from early DSM initiatives during the Tenth Plan such as MEPS and the SAVE programme.",""],[1,"177","6","Long-Term Demand-Side Management Master Plan","The Economic Planning Unit, Prime Minister's Department (EPU) will initiate a study on DSM which covers the entire spectrum of the energy sector.","Economic Planning Unit, Prime Minister's Department (EPU)"],[1,"177","7","Energy Efficiency Improvement Measures in Buildings, Industry and Households","During the Eleventh Plan, measures will be taken to identify potential improvements and appropriate approaches to ensure efficient use of energy in buildings, industries and households.",""],[1,"177","7","Energy Service Provider Competency Enhancement","These measures include increasing competencies of energy service providers, especially Registered Electrical Energy Managers, and promoting the implementation of Energy Performance Contracting for government buildings.",""],[1,"177","7","Energy Performance Contracting for Government Buildings","These measures include increasing competencies of energy service providers, especially Registered Electrical Energy Managers, and promoting the implementation of Energy Performance Contracting for government buildings.",""],[1,"177","7","Energy Labelling Awareness and Standards Promotion","User awareness will be enhanced on energy labelling and the availability of standards such as ISO 50001 for buildings and MEPS for appliances will be promoted.",""],[1,"177","7","Enhanced Time of Use Tariff Scheme","Other specific measures will include introduction of Enhanced Time of Use (EToU) tariff scheme and gradual abolishment of the Special Industrial Tariff for energy intensive industries.",""],[1,"177","7","Special Industrial Tariff Phase-Out","Other specific measures will include introduction of Enhanced Time of Use (EToU) tariff scheme and gradual abolishment of the Special Industrial Tariff for energy intensive industries.",""],[1,"177","7","Smart Grid Deployment","Infrastructure related initiatives such as implementation of smart grids and highly efficient co-generation technologies for combined heat and power system will be promoted.",""],[1,"177","7","High-Efficiency Co-Generation Technology Promotion","Infrastructure related initiatives such as implementation of smart grids and highly efficient co-generation technologies for combined heat and power system will be promoted.",""]],"73":[[1,"227","5","Electricity Subsector Supply Security Management","Strategy E4: Managing supply diversity for security of the electricity subsector through better management of resources, enhancing alternative energy sources, and augmenting rural electrification;",""],[1,"227","6","Electricity Subsector Sustainability and Reliability Improvement Strategy","Strategy E5: Improving the sustainability, efficiency, and reliability of the electricity subsector with a sustainable tariff framework and initiatives to improve efficiency and reliability of electricity supply.",""],[1,"229","3","Electricity Generation Mix Optimization and Fuel Diversification","The electricity subsector will maintain an optimum generation mix, which takes into account economic, social, and environmental factors.",""],[1,"230","1","Power Plant Emission Control and Clean Energy Expansion","The Government will ensure that future power planting up must incorporate more stringent emission control technologies to ensure a progressive reduction of the energy industry's carbon footprint.",""],[1,"230","1","Clean and Green Energy Priority in Power Generation","Usage of clean and green energy sources in power generation will be made a priority and is expected to be increased substantially in the generation mix.",""],[1,"230","2","Renewable Energy Source Development and Expansion","The Government will study new potential RE sources to enhance the generation mix.",""],[1,"230","3","Nuclear Power Exploration and Atomic Energy Regulatory Commission Establishment","The usage of nuclear power as an alternative energy resource will be explored further.",""],[1,"230","4","Net Energy Metering for Solar Electricity","The implementation of net energy metering (NEM), especially for solar-generated electricity, will provide savings on electricity bills to consumers.",""],[1,"230","5","Rural Electrification Programme Expansion","Rural electrification programmes, especially in Sabah and Sarawak, will be enhanced to improve national coverage to 99% by 2020, as shown in Exhibit 7-17.",""],[1,"230","5","Off-grid Electricity Supply for Remote Areas","Electricity supply would be provided through off-grid generation for areas which are too far from the grid.",""],[1,"230","5","Alternative Renewable Off-grid Systems Support","The development of alternative systems such as solar hybrid, mini and pico hydro will be supported by off-grid networks to ensure wider coverage.",""],[1,"230","6","Community-Based Rural Electrification Promotion","Community involvement in providing rural electrification will be promoted.",""],[1,"230","6","Community Partnerships for Sustainable Rural Electrification","The Government will explore collaborations with relevant communities to ensure sustainability of rural electrification systems.",""],[1,"230","6","NGO-Backed Micro-Hybrid Rural Electricity Supply","Partnerships with NGOs will be formed to provide electricity supply for the rural communities using micro hybrid and RE sources.",""],[1,"230","7","Electricity Generation Fuel Mix Optimization","the generation fuel mix needs to be balanced to optimise the cost of supply.",""],[1,"231","8","Electricity Generation, Transmission, and Distribution Expansion","The efficiency and reliability of electricity supply will be further improved through continued investment in generation, transmission, and distribution projects by utility providers.",""]],"74":[[1,"161","2","Feed-in Tariff Mechanism for Renewable Energy Growth","The Renewable Energy Act, 2011 implemented the Feed-in Tariff (FiT) mechanism to accelerate renewable energy (RE) growth in Malaysia",""],[1,"162","4","Renewable Energy Act Enforcement and Feed-in Tariff Mechanism","Renewable Energy Act, 2011 enforced and the Feed-in Tariff mechanism implemented",""],[1,"174","3","Renewable Energy Expansion and Net Energy Metering","Strategy B2: Increasing share of renewables in energy mix by exploring new RE sources, enhancing capacity of RE personnel and implementing net energy metering;",""],[1,"176","4","Renewable Energy Source Promotion and Capacity Expansion","In the Eleventh Plan, focus will be on promoting new RE sources, enhancing capacity of RE personnel and implementing net energy metering to further intensify the development of RE.",""],[1,"176","4","Net Energy Metering Implementation","In the Eleventh Plan, focus will be on promoting new RE sources, enhancing capacity of RE personnel and implementing net energy metering to further intensify the development of RE.",""],[1,"176","5","Renewable Energy Source Exploration and Feasibility Studies","Studies will be conducted to identify new RE sources to diversify the generation mix.",""],[1,"177","2","Renewable Energy Industry Training and Skills Development Programme","The Government will provide training to 1,740 personnel through the Sustainable Energy Development Authority (SEDA), creating experts in the field of biomass, biogas, mini hydro and solar PV.",""],[1,"177","2","Private Sector Renewable Energy Training Promotion","In addition, the private sector will be encouraged to conduct training and increase the number of RE experts.",""],[1,"177","3","Net Energy Metering Instrument","a new instrument termed as net energy metering (NEM) will be implemented in the Eleventh Plan.","KeTTHA | Suruhanjaya Tenaga"],[1,"188","1","Renewable Energy Source Diversification","Dependency on particular sources, especially polluting or non-renewable ones, will be systematically addressed through introduction of renewable sources.",""]],"75":[[1,"193","2","Transport and Logistics Network Expansion","the transport and logistics sector will continue to remain a crucial driver of growth - leveraging new investments in road, rail and air services to boost regional development.",""],[1,"206","2","Seamless Transportation and Mobility Enhancement Initiative","Initiatives will be undertaken to provide a seamless transportation system and enhance mobility of people, targeting a 40% public transport modal share in the GKL/KV region and 20% in other state capitals.",""],[1,"206","2","Rural and Inter-city Connectivity Improvement","Rural, rural-urban and inter-city connectivity will also be strengthened through enhanced bus, rail and air services.",""],[1,"207","1","Affordable and Accessible Transportation Provision","Under the Eleventh Plan, the Government aims to continue to provide sufficient and affordable access to transportation to allow for a safe, efficient, and fast flow of people and goods within Malaysia - especially across rural and urban areas - and internationally.",""],[1,"207","2","Integrated Transport Connectivity and Public Transport Promotion","Enhancing connectivity across transport modes and regions through greater connectivity across regions and modes, promoting public transport in both rural and urban areas, and optimising transport planning;",""],[1,"207","5","National Transport Model and Malaysian Aviation Commission Establishment","Strategy A4: Strengthening regulatory and institutional frameworks for the transport industry through introducing a national transport model and establishing the Malaysian Aviation Commission.",""],[1,"208","7","Urban Public Transport Infrastructure Investment and Intermodal Integration","To increase public transport modal share by commuters, investments in new infrastructure, along with greater intermodal integration will be undertaken to ensure seamless travel.",""],[1,"208","7","Demand-Based Public Transport Mode Development","Suitable public transport modes will be developed based on travel demand.",""],[1,"208","9","KTMB Transformation and Service Improvement Programme","KTMB will continue its transformation exercise to improve overall operations, including organisation structure, route rationalisation, and review of fare and freight charges, to provide a better service to the public.",""],[1,"208","9","Rail Service Reliability and Maintenance Improvement","Service reliability and operational performance will be improved by addressing engineering issues, rolling stock management, and infrastructure maintenance.",""],[1,"208","10","Bus Network and Express Bus Service Restructuring","Bus networks will complement rail networks to provide efficient last-mile connectivity.",""],[1,"208","11","Stage Bus Services Transformation Programme Extension to Rural Areas","In this regard, the Stage Bus Services Transformation (SBST) Programme will be extended to rural areas and provide greater coverage.",""],[1,"209","2","Rural Air Services Connectivity and Safety Improvement","The Government will continue to enhance connectivity and safety of rural air services (RAS) by improving short take-off and landing airstrips (STOLports).",""],[1,"209","2","Mukah Airport Construction","The construction of a new airport in Mukah will be completed in 2018",""],[1,"209","2","Lawas STOLport Relocation","the relocation of Lawas STOLport in Sarawak to a suitable site will be carried out",""],[1,"209","3","Rural Air Services Route Rationalisation","These routes will be rationalised to ensure that support on rural air services is targeted towards the right areas.",""],[1,"209","4","Transit-Oriented Development Promotion and Expansion","The transit-oriented development (TOD) concept will be promoted to optimise land use and public transport infrastructure planning.",""],[1,"209","6","Stage Bus Services Transformation Programme","The SBST Programme is an ambitious effort to completely transform the stage bus business model towards financial self-sustainability and increased levels of service for commuters.",""],[1,"209","8","Gross Cost Service Delivery Contract Model","Gross cost service delivery contract model where operators are paid per kilometre of service provided",""],[1,"210","2","Integrated Road and Rail Network Planning","Planning for development of road and rail networks will be integrated, to promote a multimodal transport system.",""],[1,"210","3","Stakeholder-Transport Planner Coordination Mechanism","engagement between stakeholders and transport planners will be established to avoid fragmented planning.",""],[1,"210","3","Freight Modal Shift from Road to Rail","Efforts will be undertaken to promote the modal shift from road to rail in transporting cargo between hinterland and ports.",""],[1,"211","1","Public Transport Safety, Efficiency, and Comfort Improvement","Strategies to expand Malaysia's transport network and enhance intermodal integration must be further complemented by efforts to improve the system's safety and efficiency as well as user's level of comfort.",""],[1,"212","3","National Transport Model for Integrated Transport Policy Formulation","A national transport model will be introduced to strengthen inter- agency collaboration in formulating integrated transport policies.",""]],"76":[[1,"178","3","Low Carbon Mobility and Public Transport Promotion","By encouraging the use of public transport, dual objectives of reducing congestion and minimising environmental pollution can be achieved.",""],[1,"178","4","Electric Vehicle Adoption Promotion for Public Transport","The Government will work with relevant private agencies to increase adoption of EEVs, especially for public transport like buses and taxis.",""],[1,"178","5","Urban Public Transport Investment Programme","Public transport investments in cities - including Mass Rapid Transit (MRT) systems in Greater Kuala Lumpur/Klang Valley (GKL/KV) and bus systems in other state capitals - will be made in line with declared targets to achieve 40% public transport modal share in GKL/KV and 20% in other cities.",""],[1,"178","5","Vehicle Fuel Emissions Reduction Measures","The Government will also work towards increasing bio-diesel blending requirements of up to 15% in automotive fuel and implementing the EURO 5 emission standards during the Eleventh Plan.",""],[1,"178","5","Compressed Natural Gas Promotion","The use of CNG will also be promoted.",""],[1,"207","6","Public Transport Connectivity Investment Programme","Investments will therefore be made in rural, rural-urban, urban, and intercity transport modes.",""]],"77":[[1,"27","6","Transport Infrastructure Productivity and Service Improvement","New investments in road, rail, and air services will be balanced with efforts to improve the productivity, efficiency, and service levels of such infrastructure.",""],[1,"27","6","Logistics Efficiency and Trade Facilitation Enhancement","Efficiency of the logistics sector and trade facilitation will be enhanced, making Malaysia the preferred logistics gateway to Asia.",""],[1,"33","12","Transit-Oriented Development","Transit-oriented development to increase use of public transportation and reduce reliance on personal vehicles",""],[1,"43","13","Large-Scale Public Investment Projects","Public investment is expected to grow at 4% per annum in real terms during the Tenth Plan, spurred by the implementation of large-scale projects, such as the Klang Valley Mass Rapid Transit (KVMRT) Line 1 from Sungai Buloh to Kajang, Electrified Double-Track Railway Ipoh- Padang Besar, Light Rail Transit (LRT) extension from Kelana Jaya and Sri Petaling to Putra Heights, KLIA2 Terminal, Central Spine Road from Kuala Lipis to Bentong, as well as the Regasification Terminal (RGT-1) in Melaka.",""],[1,"53","12","Public Investment and Major Infrastructure Project Roll-out","Some of the major public sector projects that will be undertaken, include the Pengerang Integrated Petroleum Complex (PIPC) in Johor; Pan-Borneo Highway; KVMRT Line 2 and the roll-out of the High Speed Broadband project phase 2.",""],[1,"53","12","Project Sequencing for Sustainable Economic Growth","The Government will take steps to sequence project implementation to ensure sustainable economic growth.",""],[1,"58","2","Major Infrastructure and Development Projects","Other subsectors such as civil engineering and non-residential will remain robust in line with the development of major projects such as the Tun Razak Exchange, KL118 Tower, Refinery and Petrochemical Integrated Development (RAPID), and the Pan-Borneo Highway.",""],[1,"77","2","Paved Roads Construction","paved roads will be constructed",""],[1,"91","4","Rural-Urban Connectivity and Mobility Improvement","Improving rural-urban linkages by improving connectivity and mobility as well as using ICT to strengthen the role of UTCs, RTCs and mini RTCs;",""],[1,"233","1","Transport Infrastructure Investment Programme","In the Eleventh Plan, investment in roads, rail, ports, and air services will be balanced with efforts to improve productivity, efficiency, and service level of such infrastructure.",""],[1,"233","1","Logistics Services Improvement and Trade Facilitation Reform","To enhance national competitiveness and lower the cost of doing business, the logistics services will be improved and trade facilitation mechanisms will be strengthened.",""],[1,"252","7","National Logistics Task Force","the National Logistics Task Force will be set up to lead the implementation of the LTFMP.",""],[1,"258","4","Integrated Logistics Supply Chain Development","A more integrated logistics supply chain will be developed to drive growth and increase competitive advantage.",""]],"78":[[1,"211","4","Kuala Lumpur Air Traffic Control Centre Construction","A new Kuala Lumpur Air Traffic Control Centre will be built at KLIA to replace the National Control Centre at Subang, Selangor to improve aircraft movement capacity.",""],[1,"211","5","Air Navigation Services Upgrade","be upgraded to improve efficiency of air navigation services.",""],[1,"211","5","Langkawi International Airport Upgrade","The Langkawi International Airport, Kedah and the Sultan Ismail Petra Airport, Kelantan will be upgraded to cater for the expected increase in passengers.",""],[1,"212","2","Institutional and Regulatory Framework Strengthening for Transport Sectors","Greater attention will be given to strengthen the institutional and regulatory framework for public transport, port, and civil aviation.",""],[1,"212","4","Malaysian Aviation Commission Regulatory and Planning Functions","The responsibilities of the commission include economic regulation and consumer protection as shown in Exhibit 7-9.",""],[1,"212","4","Aviation Capacity and Competition Management through Licensing and Route Allocation","It will also undertake policy and planning functions to manage capacity and competition via licensing, route allocation, and streamlining airports according to its hierarchy.",""],[1,"212","4","Department of Civil Aviation Technical, Safety, and Security Functions","The Department of Civil Aviation (DCA) will continue to serve as the technical, safety, and security authority.",""],[1,"212","4","Assessment of DCA Corporatisation","The possibility of corporatising DCA will be assessed during the Eleventh Plan.",""],[1,"213","2","Airline Licensing and Certification Regulation","Issue, renew, and revoke airline licenses for airlines with approval of technical certification from DCA (AOC)",""],[1,"213","4","Ground Handling License Renewal, Issuance, and Revocation","Ground handling Issue, renew, and revoke ground handling licenses for self-handling (new) and third party licenses",""],[1,"213","6","Transparent Traffic Rights Allocation and Revocation Reform","Allocate traffic rights through a transparent process and revoke traffic rights that are underutilised",""],[1,"213","7","Airline Consumer Protection Standards","Establish and enforce minimum standards for consumer protection across all airlines",""],[1,"213","9","Non-Discriminatory Carrier Selection and Route Support Mechanism","Conducts non- discriminatory process to select carriers to serve and allocate financial support for those routes",""],[1,"213","12","Airport Operator Licensing and Aerodrome Technical Approval","Issue, renew, and revoke airport operator licenses for airport operators with approval of technical license from DCA (aerodrome license)",""],[1,"213","13","Airport Charges Regulation","Regulates airport charges, in line with the terms defined in the current and future Operating Agreement (OA) between the airport operator and the Government",""]],"79":[[1,"254","1","Islamic Finance Market Development and Product Innovation","The strong position of Malaysia as a global Islamic finance marketplace will continue to be reinforced.",""],[1,"254","1","Islamic Financial Market Diversification and International Promotion","Efforts will continue to enhance the diversity of industry players, increase vibrancy in the Islamic financial markets, and promote Malaysia as the referral centre for Islamic financial transactions.",""],[1,"254","6","Islamic Finance Market Development","Reinforce Malaysia's position as a global Islamic finance marketplace through innovative Islamic financial products and services",""]],"80":[[1,"25","4","Urban Competitiveness Development Initiative","develop cities as a source of competitiveness",""],[1,"33","2","Major City Transformation Programme","By 2020, four major cities3 in Malaysia will have undergone a step- change in their economic growth, importance as talent hubs, and liveability.",""],[1,"33","3","City Competitiveness Master Plans","City Competitiveness Master Plans will be developed for four major cities as a start, based on key principles that increase liveability and stimulate economic growth.",""]],"81":[[1,"236","1","Regional Economic Corridor Development","Regional economic corridors will be further developed to ensure balanced development.",""],[1,"236","1","Strategic Investment in Selected Cities","there will be greater investment in selected cities to enhance their global competitiveness and gain from economic agglomeration.",""],[1,"237","1","Innovation Intensification and Competitive Cities and Corridors Initiative","The Eleventh Plan will embark on game-changing strategies to spur economic growth such as intensifying innovation activities and developing competitive cities and regional economic corridors.",""],[1,"246","4","Regional Economic Corridors Investment Promotion","Regional economic corridors continued to contribute towards sector growth and overall economic development.",""],[1,"248","2","City Competitiveness Master Plans","Developing city competitiveness master plans for four first-tier cities",""],[1,"250","14","Innovation and Competitive Cities Game Changers","Two of these seven focus areas have been identified as game changers in the Eleventh Plan - namely Innovation and Competitive Cities.",""]],"82":[[1,"222","2","Smart Living in Cities Initiative","Efforts will be undertaken by the Ministry of Communications and Multimedia to ensure smart living in cities.","Ministry of Communications and Multimedia"],[1,"222","3","Digital Urban Services and Open Data Initiative","will be placed on addressing major pain points related to urban services such as providing better transportation as well as utilities and waste management through the adoption of digital infrastucture and applications.",""],[1,"222","4","Smart Cities Prioritization Framework","During the Eleventh Plan, a framework will be developed to prioritise areas of focus in the development of smart cities.",""],[1,"222","4","Smart Communities Development Initiative","A fundamental initiative to realise the migration to smart cities will be the development of smart communities.",""]],"83":[[1,"184","3","Community Disaster Awareness Programme","Strengthening disaster risk management by establishing DRM policy and institutional framework, improving disaster detection and response capacity, incorporating DRM into development plans and creating community awareness;",""],[1,"184","6","Comprehensive Disaster Risk Management Framework","Therefore, there is an urgent need for a more comprehensive DRM framework to be put in place.",""],[1,"184","6","Strengthened Disaster Risk Management","In this regard, the Government will strengthen DRM to arrest and reduce the impact of natural disasters on people and infrastructure.",""],[1,"184","6","Faster Disaster Response to Affected Communities","It will also ensure effective and faster response time to communities affected by natural disasters when they occur.",""],[1,"185","2","Disaster Detection and Early Warning System Upgrade","Capacity in disaster detection and early warning will be improved by upgrading detection technology and forecasting systems.",""],[1,"185","2","Disaster Risk Area Mapping Initiative","Mapping of disaster prone and high risk areas is essential to enhance disaster detection efforts.",""],[1,"185","2","Disaster Preparedness and Response Capacity Building","Capabilities of all parties involved in disaster preparedness, response and recovery including capacity to conduct forecasting analysis will be strengthened to improve response time and effectiveness of DRM.",""],[1,"185","4","Community Disaster Preparedness and Response Capacity Building","Efforts will therefore be taken to enhance awareness, build capacity and empower them to take initial response measures in a disaster.",""],[1,"185","4","Large-scale Disaster Drills in Risk-prone Areas","For example, drills in risk prone areas, done on a large scale and involving all sectors can help communities to deal with a natural disaster scenario.",""],[1,"185","4","Disaster Communication and Coordination Platforms","Communication strategies and platforms among disaster-related agencies as well as between the Government and the people will be established to enable better coordination and faster response time.",""]],"85":[[1,"293","10","Strategic Partnership Formation for Collective Engagement","Forming strategic partnerships with NGOs, political associations and CBOs for collective engagement on initiatives undertaken and act as agents of change.",""]],"86":[[1,"79","3","Price Control Regulation Monitoring and Enforcement","strengthening the monitoring and enforcement of price control regulations",""],[1,"83","8","Price Control Regulation Monitoring and Enforcement","Efforts will continuously be taken to strengthen the monitoring and enforcement of price control regulations to curtail unreasonable price increases, especially for basic necessities.",""],[1,"83","8","Consumer Price Reporting and Complaint System","Consumers will play a greater role by reporting unethical pricing practices and stockpiling by retailers through the Skuad Pengguna, consumer associations and the eAduan system.",""],[1,"83","8","National Price Monitoring System","Price monitoring will ensure stable and adequate supply of goods and services and curb excessive market speculation, thus improving market efficiency and purchasing power.",""],[1,"83","8","1Harga 1Malaysia Subsidised Goods Price Standardisation","The 1Harga 1Malaysia programme will be continued to standardise the prices of subsidised goods between Sabah, Sarawak, and Peninsular Malaysia.",""],[1,"83","8","Kedai Rakyat 1Malaysia and Coop1Malaysia Expansion","The coverage of Kedai Rakyat 1Malaysia (KR1M) and Coop1Malaysia stores will also be expanded throughout the nation to ensure widespread access to reasonably priced goods thus reducing the burden of increasing cost of living.",""]],"87":[[1,"208","8","Klang Valley Mass Rapid Transit System","The Klang Valley Mass Rapid Transit (KVMRT) system will become operational during the Eleventh Plan.",""],[1,"208","8","Light Rail Transit Line 3 Construction","Additionally, construction on a Light Rail Transit (LRT) Line 3 connecting Bandar Utama to Klang, running over 36 km and serving 25 stations will start in 2016 with expected completion in 2020.",""]],"88":[[1,"129","1","Education Quality Improvement for Student Outcomes","The Government will focus on four areas: improving the efficiency of the labour market to accelerate economic growth, transforming TVET to meet industry demand, strengthening lifelong learning for skills enhancement, and improving the quality of the education system for better student outcomes and institutional excellence.",""],[1,"135","7","Private Preschool Grants and Fee Assistance","This included providing grants and fee assistance for private preschool operators, which helped increase enrolment for children aged 4+ to 5+ from 72.4% in 2010 to 90.7% in 2014.",""],[1,"136","2","Education Transformation Waves","The education transformation is sequenced in three waves.",""],[1,"136","7","Bilingual Proficiency and Additional Language Learning Initiative","Ensure every child is proficient in Bahasa Melayu and English language and is encouraged to learn an additional language",""],[1,"136","13","Localised Education Solution Customisation","Empower JPNs, PPDs, and schools to customise solutions based on need",""],[1,"137","3","Secondary School Standard Curriculum Reform","The forthcoming Standard Curriculum for Secondary School places a similar emphasis on the teaching and learning of HOTS.",""],[1,"137","3","iThink Creative Thinking Skills Programme","To support these changes, the MoE rolled out programmes such as iThink to train students and teachers in the use of creative thinking tools.","MoE"],[1,"142","7","Education Quality Enhancement Initiative","Above all, the quality of education will be raised to develop talent with both the knowledge and skills, and ethics and morality, to thrive in a globally competitive and ever- changing world.",""],[1,"152","1","Integrated Education Quality Improvement Strategy","This aim will be realised through an integrated approach that includes improving the quality of teachers and academic staff, earned autonomy for IHEs and schools, and a more efficient use of public resources.",""],[1,"152","2","Early Childhood Care and Education Quality Improvement","Enhancing access and quality to improve student outcomes through a range of measures such as better quality early childhood care and education (ECCE), professional development of teachers and school leaders, and the provision of different schooling models to meet the needs of specific student groups;",""],[1,"152","2","Teacher and School Leader Professional Development","Enhancing access and quality to improve student outcomes through a range of measures such as better quality early childhood care and education (ECCE), professional development of teachers and school leaders, and the provision of different schooling models to meet the needs of specific student groups;",""],[1,"152","2","Differentiated Schooling Models for Specific Student Groups","Enhancing access and quality to improve student outcomes through a range of measures such as better quality early childhood care and education (ECCE), professional development of teachers and school leaders, and the provision of different schooling models to meet the needs of specific student groups;",""],[1,"152","3","Strengthening State and District Education Support Offices","empowering Jabatan Pendidikan Negeri (JPN) and Pejabat Pendidikan Daerah (PPD) to provide more instructional support to schools",""],[1,"152","3","Community and Private Sector Partnership for Education Transformation","engaging the community and private sector as partners in the education transformation journey",""]],"89":[[1,"154","1","Specialised Training and Qualification Standards for Early Childhood Educators","The Government will improve the quality of teachers and caregivers through specialised training programmes, as well as require all teachers working in public preschools to have a minimum diploma level qualification.",""],[1,"154","1","Childcare Centre Affordability and Accessibility Measures","Measures to ensure the affordability of and accessibility to childcare centres will be explored by Jabatan Kebajikan Masyarakat (JKM) as the lead agency for ECCE.","Jabatan Kebajikan Masyarakat (JKM)"],[1,"154","1","Workplace Childcare Centre Expansion Initiative","This includes collaborating with other private and public organisations to promote the establishment of more childcare centres at the workplace.",""],[1,"154","1","Preschool Performance Monitoring Expansion","The Government will also expand performance monitoring mechanisms to all preschools, and identify gifted and talented children through the PERMATA programme to enable their potential to be nurtured as early as possible.",""]],"90":[[1,"282","2","Public Service Delivery Efficiency Improvement and Benchmarking","As part of ongoing improvement efforts, Malaysia continued to benchmark and monitor its rankings in various global indices such as the World Competitiveness Yearbook (WCY) by the International Institute for Management Development (IMD), the e-Government Development Index (EGDI) by the United Nations (UN) and the Corruption Perception Index by Transparency International (TI).",""],[1,"285","2","Government Transformation Programme Performance Management Framework","The GTP introduced a new framework across ministries for managing performance and delivery of public services.",""],[1,"285","3","Government Transformation Programme Implementation and Accountability System","A key feature of the GTP is the high degree of precision and accountability in implementation.",""],[1,"285","3","Cross-Ministry Delivery Coordination Teams","The GTP involved extensive collaboration across ministries, including cross- agency teams of public servants to develop, detail, and deliver solutions to the rakyat.",""],[1,"285","3","Delivery Task Force Review and Refinement Meetings","Regular Delivery Task Force (DTF) meetings for each NKRA are convened regularly with relevant ministers and senior public servants to approve plans, monitor progress, and refine implementation strategies as required.",""],[1,"285","3","GTP Annual Reporting and Performance Review","The GTP Annual Report is published and serves as a measure of achievements against targets set and promises made to the rakyat.",""],[1,"285","3","Annual Ministry and Agency Performance Reporting","Each year, implementing agencies and ministries report on what has been accomplished, along with a transparent account on the challenges faced in meeting these targets.",""],[1,"293","13","Outcome-Based Budgeting Implementation","Outcome-based budgeting (OBB), which integrates both development and operating budgets, will be implemented to ensure Government expenditure is aligned with national priorities and benefits the target groups.",""],[1,"293","13","Programme Performance Measurement and Accountability System","Performance of programmes at the national and ministry levels will be measured based on quantity, quality, cost and timeliness.",""],[1,"293","13","Ministry Accountability for Programme Outcomes","Ministries will be held accountable for the performance of programme outcomes, which will form part of their key performance indicators (KPIs).",""],[1,"293","13","OBB Capacity Building Programme","Capacity building will be enhanced for the effective implementation the OBB.",""],[1,"298","4","Outcome-Based Monitoring and Resource Allocation","Improving monitoring and evaluation focused on outcomes through cascading an outcome-based approach (OBA) in results monitoring and resource allocation.",""],[1,"299","14","Outcome-Based Approach Monitoring and Evaluation Strengthening","The monitoring and evaluation process will be strengthened through the OBA.",""]],"92":[[1,"25","4","Green Growth Transition","the Government will embark on green growth to shift the paradigm of sustainability from a narrow focus on natural assets, to include consumption and production processes in all sectors and households",""],[1,"27","3","Green Growth Strategy","Malaysia's green growth strategy will lead to better quality of growth, strengthened food, water and energy security, lower environmental risks and ecological scarcities, and ultimately better wellbeing and quality of life.",""],[1,"33","13","Efficient Waste Management Guidelines and Enforcement","Efficient waste management through guidelines on resource use and effective enforcement",""]],"93":[[1,"22","10","Government Transformation Programme","This transformation agenda is supported by the Economic Transformation Programme, which focuses on the 12 economic areas that are most critical to the nation's continued growth, and the Government Transformation Programme, which focuses on transforming areas of public service that are of greatest concern to the rakyat.",""],[1,"22","10","MyNDS Implementation Strengthening Initiative","The Government has also introduced MyNDS to strengthen implementation approach.",""],[1,"34","1","Public Service Transformation Programme","the Government is committed to transforming the public service by becoming more citizen-centric and enhancing the productivity, efficiency, and effectiveness of service delivery.",""],[1,"34","2","Public Service Delivery Improvement","Enhancing service delivery with citizens at the centre by eliminating unnecessary bureaucratic processes, expanding the outreach of its services, and increasing accountability;",""],[1,"34","3","Public Sector Institutional Rationalisation","Rationalising public sector institutions for greater productivity and performance by reducing overlapping roles and functions among agencies, right sizing the public service, and introducing an exit policy for underperformers;",""],[1,"34","4","Public Service Talent Management and Training Reform","Strengthening talent management for the public service of the future by providing a more conducive working environment including flexible work arrangements, empowering ministries and agencies, and upgrading public sector training;",""],[1,"34","5","Project Management Enhancement Initiative","Enhancing project management for better and faster results by improving the process of project selection and resource allocation, establishing dedicated project implementation teams, and creating a pool of professional project management personnel;",""],[1,"34","6","Local Government Service Quality and Capacity Strengthening","Capitalising on local government for quality services at the local level through greater engagement with local community and NGOs, expanding the outreach and quality of service, and further empowering local authorities in terms of capacity and capability.",""],[1,"48","2","Public Sector Productivity Enhancement and Regulatory Reform","Enhancing public sector productivity and accelerating regulatory reforms",""],[1,"52","8","Public Sector Productivity Enhancement Reform","Enhancing public sector productivity by introducing productivity enhancement key performance indicators (KPIs), accelerating regulatory reforms and rationalising government institutions",""],[1,"60","1","Fiscal Consolidation and Revenue Administration Reform","The Government is committed towards meeting its fiscal consolidation target of a balanced budget by 2020 by continuing and expanding upon the structural reforms initiated during the Tenth Plan.",""],[1,"60","1","Public Expenditure Discipline and Prudence Measures","The main strategy to enhance fiscal flexibility under the Eleventh Plan is to strengthen the efficiency of revenue collection and to undertake more disciplined and prudent use of Government funds.",""],[1,"60","1","Tax System Efficiency Enhancement","The efficiency and effectiveness of the existing taxation system will be further enhanced, following from the implementation of the GST in 2015.",""],[1,"60","2","Goods and Services Tax Introduction","The introduction of the GST will bring in an estimated average of RM31.4 billion revenue per year over the next five years compared to an average of RM15.5 billion collected through the sales tax and services tax during the Tenth Plan, which will strengthen the fiscal position.",""],[1,"60","2","Review of Dividends from Government-Linked Companies","This will be further improved by among others, reviewing dividends received from Government-linked companies and undertaking greater joint audit efforts by the Inland Revenue Board and the Royal Malaysian Customs Department.",""],[1,"60","2","Joint Tax Audit Strengthening","This will be further improved by among others, reviewing dividends received from Government-linked companies and undertaking greater joint audit efforts by the Inland Revenue Board and the Royal Malaysian Customs Department.","Inland Revenue Board | Royal Malaysian Customs Department"],[1,"60","3","Subsidy Rationalisation and Public Spending Efficiency Reform","Prudent spending practice will be enhanced by among others, further rationalising subsidies, adopting accrual accounting at all government agencies and ministries as well as introducing the Creativity Index to evaluate the socio-economic impact of programmes and projects.",""],[1,"60","3","Public Service Rationalisation","The rationalisation of the public service during the Plan period will also contribute towards more moderate operating expenditure.",""],[1,"60","4","Development Expenditure Prioritization for Non-Physical Programmes","As such, development allocation will continue to prioritise non-physical programmes in the Eleventh Plan.",""],[1,"84","5","Social Safety Net Monitoring and Evaluation Mechanism","This will include the implementation of a systematic monitoring and evaluation mechanism which provides for greater accountability.",""],[1,"85","3","B40 Household Upward Mobility Coordination Mechanism","A mechanism will be established to streamline, rationalise, and coordinate various efforts by agencies to elevate B40 households towards a middle-class society.",""],[1,"85","3","Bottom-Up Programme Planning and Monitoring Approach","To ensure programmes and projects are in line with national policies and strategies, a bottom-up approach will be adopted to encourage participation and commitment of all stakeholders, from problem identification to monitoring and evaluation of programmes.",""],[1,"85","3","District-Level Focus Group Committees Empowerment","Focus group committees at district levels will be empowered to ensure development programmes meet their needs.",""],[1,"89","1","Gender-Disaggregated Data Collection Improvement","the collection of gender disaggregated data by various ministries and agencies will be improved to support planning, monitoring and evaluation of programmes.",""],[1,"90","7","SMOKU Planning, Monitoring, and Evaluation Upgrade","SMOKU will be improved to support planning, monitoring and evaluation of existing programmes.",""],[1,"91","6","Regional Development Authority Delivery System Review","Strategy C5: Streamlining the delivery system by reviewing the role of Regional Development Authorities (RDAs) and establishing Sistem Profil Kampung Peringkat Nasional.",""],[1,"91","6","National Village Profile System","Strategy C5: Streamlining the delivery system by reviewing the role of Regional Development Authorities (RDAs) and establishing Sistem Profil Kampung Peringkat Nasional.",""],[1,"91","7","Integrated Rural Basic Infrastructure Database","An integrated rural basic infrastructure database will be developed to facilitate stock-taking and planning of rural basic infrastructure as well as to ensure effective delivery of priority infrastructure to meet the communities' needs.",""]],"94":[[1,"8","5","Productivity and Innovation Strategies and Programmes","The Eleventh Plan will make the difference - it contains specific strategies and programmes bounded on outcomes to unlock productivity and transform innovation to wealth.",""],[1,"24","5","Productivity Enhancement Measures","measures will be undertaken to unlock the potential of productivity to ensure sustainable and inclusive growth.",""],[1,"25","4","Productivity Enhancement for Sectoral Growth","they aim to unlock productivity for accelerated sectoral growth",""],[1,"25","4","Innovation Promotion for New Revenue Sources","unleash innovation to generate new sources of revenue",""],[1,"27","9","Economic Sector Upgrading and Modernisation Strategy","All economic sectors will migrate into more knowledge-intensive and high value-added activities.",""],[1,"27","9","Modern Services Development Initiative","In the services sector, there will be a shift towards modern services, which include Islamic finance, ecotourism, ICT, the creative industry, the halal industry, and oil and gas.",""],[1,"27","9","Manufacturing Diversification and Complexity Upgrade","The manufacturing sector will shift towards more diverse and complex products in three catalytic subsectors, namely chemicals, electrical and electronics, and machinery and equipment.",""],[1,"27","9","Productivity, Innovation, Talent, and Internationalisation Support","Growth across all economic sectors will be supported by productivity improvements, innovation, better talent, and greater internationalisation.",""],[1,"28","1","Productivity Enhancement Strategy","it will place greater emphasis on increasing productivity to achieve a more sustainable, inclusive, and high rate of economic growth",""],[1,"28","8","Productivity-Linked Incentives and Regulatory Reform","At the national level, productivity-linked incentives will be introduced and regulatory reforms will be accelerated.",""],[1,"28","8","Industry-Specific Productivity Initiatives","At the industry level, industry champions will spearhead industry-specific productivity initiatives, while at the enterprise level, incentives and upskilling programmes will be provided.",""],[1,"28","8","Enterprise Incentives and Upskilling Programme","At the industry level, industry champions will spearhead industry-specific productivity initiatives, while at the enterprise level, incentives and upskilling programmes will be provided.",""],[1,"32","2","Enhanced Innovation Ecosystem Collaboration","In the enhanced innovation ecosystem, there will be greater collaboration and integration across industry, academia, and communities.",""],[1,"32","2","Industry-Aligned Research and Innovation Partnership","Research will be closely aligned with industry demand, and the private sector will be active partners in the research, development, commercialisation, and innovation (R&D&C&I) process by contributing funds, expertise, and other resources.",""],[1,"32","4","Enterprise-Level Innovation and R&D Collaboration Initiatives","At the enterprise level, initiatives will enhance demand- driven research, improve collaboration between researchers and industries, and encourage private investment in R&D&C&I.",""],[1,"32","9","Industry-Research Partnership Programme","Better partnerships between industry and researchers, with industry helping to shape research to ensure relevance to business, and contribute ideas, infrastructure, tools, and expertise",""],[1,"39","1","Productivity Improvement and Multi-Factor Productivity Enhancement Programme","Productivity improvements through enhanced capital efficiency and the contribution of Multi-Factor Productivity (MFP) will also be a key driver of the nation's economic growth within the Eleventh Plan.",""],[1,"48","2","Nationwide Productivity Agenda and Implementation Plan","Nation-wide productivity agenda and implementation plan",""],[1,"48","2","Cross-Industry Productivity Promotion","Ensuring productivity is championed across industries",""],[1,"48","2","Enterprise Productivity Assessment and Target Setting","Enterprise-level productivity assessments and targets",""],[1,"52","2","Productivity Enhancement Initiatives","Higher productivity growth will be achieved through comprehensive initiatives at all levels and championed by industry players.",""],[1,"52","2","Innovation Ecosystem Enhancement","The innovation ecosystem will be enhanced to elevate productivity through new or improved processes and technologies.",""],[1,"52","7","Malaysia Productivity Blueprint and National Productivity Implementation Mechanism","Establishing a nation-wide productivity agenda and implementation plan by formulating a five-year Malaysia Productivity Blueprint, strengthening the governance and institutional mechanism for implementation of productivity strategies and establishing a dedicated national productivity portal",""],[1,"52","10","Productivity Champions and Industry-Level Productivity Programmes","Ensuring productivity is championed across industries by appointing productivity champions and customising industry-level productivity programmes",""],[1,"52","11","Enterprise-Level Productivity Assessment and Target-Setting Initiative","Setting up enterprise-level productivity assessments and targets by promoting productivity performance targets, introducing firm- level interventions, promoting health check mechanisms and fostering a productivity-based culture",""],[1,"54","2","Public Investment and Productivity Enhancement","investment and undertake public investment during the Eleventh Plan, it will place greater emphasis on increasing productivity to achieve a more sustainable, inclusive, and high rate of economic growth.",""],[1,"55","1","Targeted Productivity Improvement Actions","Malaysia's approach to productivity will shift from primarily Government- driven initiatives at the national level to targeted actions across the public sector, industry players, and individual enterprises, with champions identified to role model change and ensure buy-in across stakeholders.",""],[1,"55","1","Sector-Specific Productivity Initiatives","Broad-based initiatives will be developed and tailored for each sector",""],[1,"55","2","Productivity-Linked Incentives and Regulatory Reform Package","At the national level, productivity-linked incentives will be introduced and regulatory reforms will be accelerated.",""],[1,"55","2","Industry-Specific Productivity Initiatives","At the industry level, industry champions will spearhead industry-specific productivity initiatives, while at the enterprise level, incentives and up-skilling programmes will be provided.",""],[1,"55","2","Enterprise Incentives and Upskilling Programme","At the industry level, industry champions will spearhead industry-specific productivity initiatives, while at the enterprise level, incentives and up-skilling programmes will be provided.",""],[1,"55","27","Enterprise Advisory Services for Productivity Improvement","Advisory services for enterprises to improve productivity",""],[1,"57","7","Industrial Research and Development Investment","They invest over RM10 million each year into research and development to improve the industrial efficiency of its manufacturing processes.",""],[1,"57","7","Manufacturing Process Innovation Upgrading","They have introduced innovations such as double former production lines, mechanical stripping systems, glove stacking devices, and dipping simulators.",""]],"95":[[1,"22","10","Economic Transformation Programme","This transformation agenda is supported by the Economic Transformation Programme, which focuses on the 12 economic areas that are most critical to the nation's continued growth, and the Government Transformation Programme, which focuses on transforming areas of public service that are of greatest concern to the rakyat.",""],[1,"23","1","People Economy Priority and Inclusive Growth Strategy","The people economy will be given priority, reinforcing the Government's commitment to bring further development to the people by enriching their lives, providing people dignity, and uplifting their potential to partake in the prosperity that is generated.",""],[1,"23","1","Inclusive National Growth Target Framework","national growth targets will include not only GDP growth and per capita income, but also household income and the Malaysian Wellbeing Index to assess the impact of economic growth on people's wellbeing.",""],[1,"24","6","Blue Ocean Strategy-Based National Strategy Formulation","The Eleventh Malaysia Plan used Blue Ocean Strategy (BOS) tools and frameworks, as part of the National Blue Ocean Strategy (NBOS), to formulate national strategies that are high impact, low cost and able to be rapidly implemented.",""],[1,"24","6","Strategy Canvas for National Planning","One key BOS tool used in the formulation of the Eleventh Plan was the strategy canvas - a diagnostic and action framework for visualising strategies.",""],[1,"39","1","Economic Resilience Strengthening and Structural Reform Programme","During the Eleventh Malaysia Plan, 2016-2020, the Government will continue to strengthen Malaysia's economic resilience to withstand future economic challenges.",""],[1,"51","15","Macroeconomic Stability and Economic Resilience Strategy","During the Eleventh Plan, strategies will continue to ensure a conducive and competitive economic environment with stable prices, and supportive levels of interest rates and foreign exchange rates.",""]],"96":[[1,"23","4","Universal Access to Infrastructure, Public Amenities, Housing, Health, Education, and Support Services","Every household will have access to efficient infrastructure and public amenities, quality healthcare and education, quality and affordable housing, and comprehensive support services.",""]],"97":[[1,"25","4","TVET Development for a Higher-Skilled Workforce","harness TVET for the transition to a higher-skilled workforce",""],[1,"26","9","Industry-Led TVET Programme Shift","Technical and Vocational Education and Training (TVET) will shift towards industry-led programmes to produce the skilled talent to meet industry needs.",""],[1,"26","9","Continuous Workforce Upskilling Initiative","The existing workforce will have many opportunities to continuously enrich and develop themselves, so as to stay relevant in the changing economy.",""],[1,"26","9","Education Quality Enhancement for Talent Development","Above all, the quality of education will be raised to develop talent with both the knowledge and skills, and ethics and morality, to thrive in a globally competitive and dynamic environment.",""],[1,"30","4","Industry-TVET Provider Collaboration Across the Value Chain","Industry and TVET providers collaborate across the entire value chain from student recruitment, through to curriculum design, delivery, and job placement;",""],[1,"30","6","System Harmonisation and Streamlining for Stakeholder Coordination","Achieving these aspirations will require harmonising and streamlining how the system currently operates to reduce fragmentation across the various public and private stakeholders.",""],[1,"30","6","Industry-Led Graduate Supply Interventions and Programmes","Furthermore, efforts will be made to encourage industry-led interventions and programmes as they are the stakeholders best placed to ensure that the supply of graduates meet their requirements.",""],[1,"30","12","Industry-Led Curriculum Design and Delivery for TVET","Design and delivery of curriculum led by industry, in partnership with TVET institutions and Government",""],[1,"30","13","Specialized Centres of Excellence in Niche Areas","Institutions to specialise in and create Centres of Excellence in niche areas of expertise",""],[1,"48","2","Collaborative Re-skilling and Research Initiative","Greater collaboration in re-skilling and research",""],[1,"48","5","Talent Gap and Skills Mismatch Reduction Measures","Addressing the talent gap and mismatch",""],[1,"52","2","Industrial Automation and Skills Upgrading","Industrial productivity will be raised through greater adoption of automation and upgrading of skills.",""],[1,"52","9","Upskilling, Reskilling, and Industry-Academia Collaboration Programme","Encouraging up-skilling and re-skilling as well as research through increased industry-academia collaboration, more targeted skills training programmes and increased support for industrial and social innovation activities",""],[1,"53","5","Labour Market Data Warehouse and Clearance Mechanism Reform","Addressing the talent gap and mismatch by establishing a labour market data warehouse, improving the labour market clearance mechanism as well as re-skilling and multi-skilling programmes",""],[1,"53","5","Re-skilling and Multi-skilling Programmes","Addressing the talent gap and mismatch by establishing a labour market data warehouse, improving the labour market clearance mechanism as well as re-skilling and multi-skilling programmes",""],[1,"68","19","Industry-Specific Skills Centres","Establishing industry-specific skills centres based on targeted geographical areas",""],[1,"73","10","Creative Content Skills Development Programme","University College Sabah Foundation (UCSF) together with Sabah Economic Development and Investment Authority (SEDIA) has conducted programmes in creative content skill development under Sabah Animation Creative Content Centre (SAC3) with enrolment of 600 participants in certificate, diploma, and degree level",""],[1,"73","14","Bumiputera Education Support Programmes","Yayasan Peneraju Pendidikan Bumiputera (YPPB) delivered education programmes, including support for professional qualifications such as the Association of Chartered Certified Accountants (ACCA) and Welding Apprentice Programme",""]],"98":[[1,"56","3","TNB Supply Connection Streamlining and Digital Transformation Programme","As part of its ongoing transformation programme, TNB focused on streamlining the end-to-end process of supply connection to reduce the number of steps required for application, improve communications with contractors, introduce electronic document management systems, and manage resources more effectively.",""]],"99":[[1,"56","5","Lean Hospital Process Improvement","To address this, PdSH adopted \"lean\" principles and tools such as value stream mapping, particularly to help reduce waiting times for the discharge of post- natal self-paying patients.",""],[1,"56","6","Lean Hospital Efficiency Improvement","The \"lean\" methodology can be applied effectively in hospitals to eliminate waste, streamline processes, reduce cycle times, improve the quality of care, enhance satisfaction, and reduce delays for patients.",""]],"100":[[1,"57","4","Municipal Business Process Re-engineering and E-Licence System","The Kuantan Municipal Council or Majlis Perbandaran Kuantan (MPK) embarked on business process re-engineering to improve service delivery for customers.",""],[1,"57","5","Tax Administration Digital Service Delivery Improvements","IRBM has embarked on several service delivery improvement initiatives by leveraging on ICT innovations, such as e-Filing for electronic submission of tax returns, e-Payment for online payment of taxes, as well as electronic systems for monthly tax deductions and taxpayer registration.","Inland Revenue Board of Malaysia (IRBM)"]],"101":[[1,"58","7","Train 9 LNG Production Expansion","The production of LNG will increase to 29.3 mtpa with the operation of Train 9 in PETRONAS LNG Complex in Bintulu, Sarawak beginning 2016.",""],[1,"58","7","Enhanced and Improved Oil Recovery Adoption","The production of crude oil will be supported by anticipated oil discoveries, and marginal fields as well as revival of mature fields made possible with the adoption of new technologies, such as enhanced oil recovery and improved oil recovery, subject to economic viability.",""]],"102":[[1,"25","4","B40 Household Income and Wellbeing Support","the Government will raise the income and wellbeing of the B40 households",""],[1,"26","5","Equitable Opportunity and B40 Support Measures","The Government is committed to ensuring equitable opportunities for all segments of society, in particular the B40 households.",""],[1,"26","5","Household Income Growth and B40 Upward Mobility Initiative","All households will witness an increase in income, and the B40 households will be elevated towards a middle-class society.",""],[1,"29","4","B40 Income and Wealth Ownership Support Strategy","The Government will implement strategies to raise the income and wealth ownership of the B40 households, address the increasing cost of living, and strengthen delivery mechanisms for supporting B40 households.",""],[1,"64","1","Equitable Access to Economic Growth Opportunities","Moving forward, the focus will be on ensuring more equitable access to economic growth opportunities while increasing wellbeing and quality of life across all segments.",""],[1,"64","1","Shift from Non-productive Aid to Sustainable Wealth Creation","Non-productive aid programmes will be reduced in favour of more sustainable wealth creation initiatives.",""],[1,"65","1","B40 Household Income Uplift Programme","Strategies aim to increase the overall B40 household income towards improving the quality of life and wellbeing of the rakyat.",""],[1,"65","1","Conditional and Outcome-Based Targeted Support","The focus will be on addressing the needs of identified target groups, prioritising conditional and outcome-based support, whether economic or social.",""],[1,"65","1","Productivity-Linked Assistance and Subsidy Reform","Assistance and subsidies not linked to productivity will be reduced in favour of programmes focused on creating improved wealth ownership and increasing education and skill levels.",""],[1,"65","1","B40 Household Upgrading Programme","Specific strategies include uplifting the B40 households towards a middle-class society;",""],[1,"65","1","Rural Transformation Programme","Specific strategies include ... transforming rural areas to uplift wellbeing of rural communities;",""],[1,"79","1","B40 Household Economic Upliftment and Inclusion Programme","During the Eleventh Plan, focus will be given to lifting the economic opportunities and participation of B40 households",""],[1,"79","2","Integrated Entrepreneurship and Social Enterprise Support","enhancing integrated entrepreneurship support; developing community- and social-based enterprises; incentivising investment in majority B40 households areas; and increasing wealth ownership through investment programmes;",""],[1,"79","4","B40 Household Programme Delivery Streamlining","Enhancing the delivery system of B40 households programmes by streamlining support to B40 households and complementing the Poverty Line Income (PLI) measurement with the Multidimensional Poverty Index (MPI).",""],[1,"79","5","Income Growth Support for Aspirational B40 Households","measures will be taken to spur the income growth of the aspirational group within the B40 households.",""],[1,"79","6","SME Capacity Support for B40 Households","SMEs owned by B40 households, especially the aspirational group will be provided with better opportunities to improve their capacity through financing options and business facilitation.",""],[1,"80","3","B40 Household Income and Wealth Support Strategy","The Government will implement strategies to raise the income and wealth ownership of the B40 households, address the increasing cost of living, and strengthen delivery mechanisms for supporting B40 households.",""],[1,"80","6","Wealth Ownership Investment Programmes","Raise Wealth ownership through investment programmes",""],[1,"80","15","Investment Incentives for Majority B40 Household Areas","Incentivise investment in majority B40 households areas",""],[1,"80","18","B40 Household Support Streamlining","Streamline support to B40 households",""],[1,"81","3","B40 Household Micro-Enterprise Support","Assisting B40 households with individual micro- enterprises",""],[1,"81","4","Community- and Social-Based Enterprise Support for B40 Households","Fostering community- and social-based enterprises among the B40 households, in addition to individual enterprises",""],[1,"81","4","Asset Building and Financial Resilience Support for B40 Households","B40 households are able to save and build wealth including through non-financial asset ownership, making them more resilient to economic shocks",""],[1,"83","6","Expansion of Unit Trust Schemes for B40 Households","Unit trust schemes such as the Amanah Saham Wawasan (ASW), Amanah Saham 1Malaysia (AS1M), and Amanah Saham Gemilang will be further expanded to increase equity ownership among the B40 households.",""],[1,"83","6","Awareness Campaign on Unit Trust Scheme Benefits","Awareness programmes on the benefits of such schemes will be intensified to increase the participation of B40 households in these schemes.",""],[1,"83","7","Cooperative Participation in REITs","Cooperatives will be encouraged to participate in real estate investment trusts (REITs) to increase asset ownership among B40 households.",""],[1,"83","7","Commercial Property Development by Cooperatives","The cooperatives will also undertake commercial property development in strategic locations and build affordable residential units for B40 households in urban areas.",""]],"103":[[1,"26","5","Bumiputera Economic Empowerment Initiative","The status of the Bumiputera economic community will be further enhanced.",""],[1,"65","1","Bumiputera Economic Opportunity Enhancement Programme","Specific strategies include ... enhancing Bumiputera economic opportunities.",""]],"104":[[1,"69","2","Social Safety Net Initiatives","Social safety net (SSN) initiatives were implemented to address vulnerability issues and protect the livelihoods of B40 households from economic shocks.",""],[1,"78","3","Targeted Support for Needy and Vulnerable Households","Every effort will be made to support the needy and vulnerable segments of society.",""],[1,"78","3","Conditional and Outcome-Based Social and Economic Assistance","Key shifts that will be made during this period include prioritising conditional and outcome- based support, whether economic or social.",""],[1,"78","3","Productivity-Linked Social Assistance Reform","Assistance and subsidies not linked to productivity will be reduced in favour of programmes focused on creating improved wealth ownership and increasing education and skill levels.",""],[1,"79","3","Integrated Social Safety Net","introducing an integrated and comprehensive social safety net",""],[1,"84","5","Integrated Social Safety Net Reform","Existing SSN programmes will be transformed to be more integrated and comprehensive with a clear exit policy.",""],[1,"84","5","Standardised Beneficiary Targeting System","A single standardised targeting mechanism will be developed to identify eligible beneficiaries based on the enhanced eKasih database.",""],[1,"84","6","Review of Unconditional Social Welfare Programmes","Unconditional social welfare programmes will be reviewed to include clear productivity linked targets and exit policy.",""],[1,"90","1","Integrated Social Protection for Elderly Poor","Social protection for the elderly poor will be streamlined and integrated to ensure better quality of life.",""],[1,"90","1","Continued Basic Needs Assistance","The provision of assistance will be continued based on basic needs.",""],[1,"90","1","Voluntary Savings and Retirement Scheme Participation","The low-income group, particularly in the informal sector, will be encouraged to participate in voluntary savings and retirement schemes to ensure economic protection in their old age.",""]],"105":[[1,"79","3","Financial and Debt Management Programmes","enhancing financial and debt management programmes",""],[1,"84","7","Financial Literacy and Debt Advisory Services","financial education and debt advisory services will be intensified to assist households to improve their financial management, and responsible practices, including proper use of consumer credit and debt restructuring.",""],[1,"84","8","Consumer Credit Regulation and Household Debt Data Sharing Framework","integrated and enhanced legislation will be put in place to manage consumer credit activities for both banks and non-bank lenders.",""],[1,"84","8","Household Indebtedness Data Collection and Sharing System","the collection, management and sharing of data relating to household indebtedness across national authorities and Government agencies will be enhanced to promote effective analysis and development.",""]],"106":[[1,"82","3","Modern Technology Adoption Support for Small-Scale B40 Entrepreneurs","Small-scale B40 entrepreneurs involved in industries such as printing, food manufacturing, as well as vehicle repair and maintenance will be encouraged to use modern technology to increase productivity and lower cost of production, thus increasing income.",""],[1,"82","4","eRezeki Programme Expansion for B40 Households","the eRezeki programme for B40 households will be expanded to enable the use of ICT to generate additional income.",""],[1,"82","5","eRezeki Pre-Matching Training Programme","training will be provided before matching participants of the eRezeki programme with relevant jobs such as data entry, price monitoring, and document translation.",""],[1,"82","6","Digital Business Support Expansion for Micro-Enterprises","Business support through digital platforms for micro-enterprises will be expanded to enhance outreach and market access.",""],[1,"82","6","Micro-Enterprise E-Payment Platform Expansion","To further expand the e-payment platform for micro-enterprises, affordable terminals and readers that are integrated with e-commerce solutions, will be provided.",""],[1,"82","6","Online Business-Matching Services in Telecentres","online business-matching services to local entrepreneurs will be introduced in telecentres.",""],[1,"82","7","SME Development Coordination for B40 Households","SME Corp will coordinate the development of the SMEs owned by B40 households.",""],[1,"82","7","Integrated Entrepreneurship Support for Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises","Collaboration among agencies providing entrepreneurship support programmes to micro-, small- and medium-scale entrepreneurs in urban and rural areas such as SME Corp, TEKUN Nasional and AIM will be strengthened to provide integrated assistance and reduce overlapping activities.",""],[1,"82","7","Micro-enterprise Linkage to Banking and Financial Institutions","Micro- enterprises will also be linked to banking and financial institutions for easier access to funding.",""],[1,"82","8","Smart Partnerships with R&D Institutions for SME Development","Initiatives will include establishing smart partnerships with research and development (R&D) institutions to assist the SMEs to improve product quality, enhance compliance to standards and increase market access.",""],[1,"82","8","Integrated Entrepreneurship Development Packages","SME Corp will introduce integrated entrepreneurship development packages from start-up to market product placement activities.",""],[1,"82","8","Entrepreneur Training Programmes at UTC and RTC Facilities","Urban Transformation Centre (UTC) and Rural Transformation Centre (RTC) facilities will be utilised to facilitate entrepreneur training programmes.",""]],"107":[[1,"82","1","Acceleration of Communal and Individual Land Ownership Grants","The process of granting communal and individual land ownership to Orang Asli in Peninsular Malaysia and those living in the rural and remote areas in Sabah and Sarawak will be expedited to enable land utilisation by these households.",""],[1,"82","1","Review of Orang Asli Land Disposal and Ownership Policy","The Dasar Pelupusan dan Pemilikan Tanah Orang Asli (DPPTOA) and administrative procedures in granting NCR land ownership for those living in the rural and remote areas in Sabah and Sarawak will be reviewed.",""]],"108":[[1,"88","3","Youth Development Programmes","Youth development programmes will foster dynamic leadership and develop multiple capabilities among youth through education and training, entrepreneurship, sports and volunteerism.",""],[1,"88","3","Youth Values and Leadership Formation Programme","Positive values including spiritual, patriotism, responsibility, care, resilience and positive mindsets will be inculcated to mould the potential young generation to become credible future leaders.",""],[1,"88","3","Youth Social Integration and Unity Programmes","More structured programmes will also be implemented to enhance social integration and promote unity among youth.",""],[1,"88","6","Back to Community Voluntary Programme","Youth from universities will be encouraged to participate in \"Back to Community\" voluntary programmes implemented in partnership with NGOs, universities, and companies.",""],[1,"88","6","Expansion of iM4U and RELA Youth Squad Programmes","Programmes by iM4U and RELA Youth Squad will be expanded to enable more youth from universities to participate and contribute more effectively.",""]],"109":[[1,"88","7","Women Talent Harnessing and Economic Participation Measures","A number of measures will be taken to harness women talent at all levels, and create more opportunities for women to participate in the economy, and increase the female labour participation rate to 59%, by 2020.",""],[1,"88","8","Work-Life Balance and Flexible Work Arrangements","Providing a more conducive working environment will help to promote gender diversity and increase female participation in the labour force with measures such as promoting work-life balance, flexible working arrangements and work from home concept in both the public and private sectors.",""],[1,"88","8","Expansion of Early Childhood Care and Education Access","In addition, accessibility to quality early childcare and childhood education (ECCE) for childcare services will be expanded.",""],[1,"89","1","Women’s Leadership and Entrepreneurship Advancement","Efforts will be intensified to increase the number of women in decision- making positions.",""],[1,"89","1","Back-to-Work Programme for Women","\"Back to work\" programmes to encourage qualified women who have been out of the workforce due to family or other commitments, will also be expanded through collaboration with the private sectors.",""],[1,"89","1","TalentCorp Women Workforce Return Initiatives","Initiatives led by TalentCorp will be continued to increase the number of talented women returning to the workforce.",""]],"110":[[1,"29","4","Multidimensional Poverty Index Introduction","The Government will also introduce the Multidimensional Poverty Index (MPI) to ensure that vulnerability and quality of life is measured in addition to income.",""],[1,"80","3","Multidimensional Poverty Index Introduction","The Government will also introduce the Multidimensional Poverty Index (MPI) to ensure that vulnerability and quality of life is measured in addition to income.",""],[1,"85","4","Multidimensional Poverty Index Adoption","The MPI, a relative poverty measurement approach practised in developed nations, will be adopted to complement the absolute income-based measurement of the PLI.",""]],"111":[[1,"92","8","RDA Role Review and Capacity Strengthening","The role of RDAs will be reviewed to drive socio-economic development of their respective areas.",""],[1,"92","8","Regional Infrastructure and Social Amenities Provision","The RDAs will collaborate with the regional economic corridor authorities to provide sufficient infrastructure and social amenities as well as attract private investments to generate economic activities and create jobs for the local community.",""],[1,"92","8","Socio-Economic Development Programme Support","RDAs will also support relevant agencies in implementing socio-economic development programmes and projects.",""],[1,"92","8","RDA Revenue-Generating Project Capacity Building","The capacity of RDAs will be strengthened to implement revenue generating projects to encourage self-financing.",""],[1,"92","9","National Village Profile Database System","A comprehensive and integrated database system, Sistem Profil Kampung Peringkat Nasional (SPKPN) will be established to provide comprehensive profile of villages which have Jawatankuasa Kemajuan dan Keselamatan Kampung (JKKK).",""]],"112":[[1,"94","1","Regional Corridor Inclusiveness Initiatives","A number of initiatives to promote inclusiveness will also be implemented across the regional economic corridors, mainly focused on income-generating activities and skills training for local communities.",""],[1,"94","1","Iskandar Malaysia Creative Industry Talent Development Programme","the Iskandar Malaysia Creative Industry Talent Development Programme will be enhanced to train more locals",""],[1,"94","1","Entrepreneurship and Skills Development Programmes in ECER","entrepreneurship and skills development programmes will broaden the ability of locals to participate in and benefit from economic development in ECER.",""],[1,"94","1","Agriculture Vocational School Enterprise Training Programme Expansion","In NCER, programmes such as the Agriculture Vocational School Enterprise Training Programme will be expanded.",""],[1,"94","1","Creative Content Development Programmes for Youth in SDC","High impact programmes in creative content development will be developed for youth in SDC with a target of 850 enrolments.",""],[1,"94","1","Tourism and Agriculture Productivity Support Programmes in SCORE","Within SCORE, programmes will be developed to support tourism development and increase agriculture productivity.",""],[1,"94","2","Border Economic Transformation Programme","the Border Economic Transformation Programme (BETP) will enhance outcomes from regional economic development by bringing inclusive development and prosperity to the border regions of Malaysia.",""],[1,"94","2","Border Region Economic Growth Projects and Income-Generating Opportunities","A range of large-scale economic growth projects and local income-generating opportunities will be developed including the development of Lembah Chuping and Perlis Inland Port in Perlis, rubber-based downstream processing in Rubber City in Kedah, the construction of Plaza IMT-GT, a retail plaza, in Bukit Bunga as well as the redevelopment of Kampung Laut in Tumpat, Kelantan.",""]],"113":[[1,"114","4","Integrated Multi-Stakeholder Collaboration Mechanism","intensify the use of interventions that bring together all stakeholders - public, private sectors and NGOs - in an integrated and collaborative manner",""],[1,"115","3","Lean Management in Public Hospitals","Measures include the introduction of lean management practices in public hospitals to release latent capacity, and better enforcement of health regulations to improve transparency and health outcomes;",""],[1,"115","3","Health Regulations Enforcement and Transparency Improvement","Measures include the introduction of lean management practices in public hospitals to release latent capacity, and better enforcement of health regulations to improve transparency and health outcomes;",""],[1,"116","1","Health Legislation Review and Enforcement Strengthening","The Government will review and formulate health legislations and intensify enforcement through strengthened coordination between government agencies and the private sector.",""],[1,"116","1","Consolidation of Health-Related Enforcement Units","the Government will consolidate health-related enforcement units in areas such as pharmaceutical, disease control, food safety, hygiene, and cleanliness, as well as medical practice and professionalism.",""],[1,"116","2","Healthcare Lean Management Reform","Healthcare services will adopt lean management practices to streamline work processes and procedures in order to enhance effectiveness and efficiency.",""],[1,"116","2","Hospital Cluster Resource-Sharing Model","The Government will also implement the hospital cluster concept in selected locations, where hospitals within the same geographical location will work as one unit, sharing resources such as assets, amenities, and human resource.",""],[1,"116","3","eHealth Strategy Implementation","The Government will implement the eHealth strategy, which incorporates existing Information and Communications Technology (ICT) systems into one, system-wide model to enhance health data management, and support research, development and commercialisation (R&D&C) initiatives.",""],[1,"116","3","Private Sector Health Service Delivery Partnership","The Government will also work with the private sector to increase information sharing and strengthen the role of the private sector in service delivery.",""],[1,"116","3","Quadruple Helix Innovation Partnership Promotion","To drive innovation through R&D&C activities, partnerships across the quadruple helix of government, industry, universities, and research institutions will be promoted.",""]],"114":[[1,"107","10","Communicable Disease Health Promotion Expansion","health promotion programmes for communicable diseases were expanded, including the Communication for Behavioural Impact Programme (COMBI), which primarily aims to mitigate the risk of dengue.",""],[1,"112","5","Health Awareness Collaboration with Private Sector and NGOs","Intensifying collaboration with private sector and NGOs to increase health awareness",""],[1,"115","5","Private Sector and NGO Health Awareness Collaboration","Strategy A4: Intensifying collaboration with private sector and NGOs to increase health awareness.",""],[1,"116","6","Communicable and Non-communicable Disease Prevention Measures","Measures will be undertaken to reduce communicable diseases (CD) and non-communicable diseases (NCD), which includes the provision of preventive healthcare services and the promotion of a healthy lifestyle.",""],[1,"116","6","Private Sector Health CSR and Research Collaboration","The private sector will be encouraged to undertake corporate social responsibility programmes (CSR), and to collaborate with the Government in research and development.",""],[1,"116","6","NGO Health Advocacy and Screening Support","NGOs will be encouraged to provide health advocacy activities, health screening, and early health interventions, as well as to work with the private sector in carrying out health-related CSR programmes.",""],[1,"116","6","Community Health Promotion through Public Parks and Recreation","Community participation in health promotion programmes, such as the use of public parks and recreational areas to promote healthy lifestyles will be encouraged.",""],[1,"116","7","Community Health Promotion Training Programme","Intervention programmes where the community will be trained to promote health, such as KOSPEN, will continue to address lifestyle related diseases.",""],[1,"116","7","Community Aedes and Tuberculosis Control Initiative","In addition, Komuniti Bebas Aedes & Tuberculosis (COMBAT), will be enhanced to control CDs through community initiatives such as gotong royong to promote a healthy environment to reduce disease transmission.",""]],"115":[[1,"103","2","Crime Prevention and Law Enforcement Strengthening","Crime prevention efforts will focus on intensifying collaboration across public and private sector stakeholders, building the capabilities of law enforcement personnel, tightening regulations and strengthening enforcement.",""],[1,"109","2","Reducing Crime National Key Result Area","To achieve these aims, the Government undertook comprehensive efforts such as omnipresence in hotspots, special police operations, and greater community participation in voluntary neighbourhood watch activities.","Polis DiRaja Malaysia (PDRM)"],[1,"114","3","Community Policing and Law Enforcement Capacity Strengthening","To create safer living environments, the Government will increase community policing and omnipresence, enable cross-agency collaborations, and build the capabilities of law enforcement personnel.",""],[1,"119","2","Crime Prevention and Community Policing Programme","Strategy C1: Enhancing crime prevention by enforcement agencies, private players, and the public to elevate perception of feeling safe.",""],[1,"119","3","Crime Prevention and Enforcement Strengthening Initiative","Strategy C2: Tightening regulations and strengthening enforcement to stem crime.",""],[1,"119","4","Crime Awareness Prevention Programmes through Schools and Social Media","Strategy C3: Promoting crime awareness for effective prevention through schools and social media.",""],[1,"119","6","Crime Prevention Intensification Programme","Crime prevention will be intensified through omnipresence, the Safe City Programme, and volunteerism programmes.",""],[1,"119","6","Integrated Police Response System Deployment","Police response time to distress calls will be improved from 12 minutes to eight minutes, particularly in urban and major cities, through the deployment of an integrated information system known as the Command, Control, Communications, Computers and Integration (C4i) system.",""],[1,"120","1","Community Policing Participation under SRS and PVR","public participation in community policing will be encouraged under SRS and PVR",""],[1,"120","1","Strengthening of JPJKK Community Crime Prevention Role","The role of Jabatan Pencegahan Jenayah dan Keselamatan Komuniti (JPJKK) will be strengthened to enhance engagement between the police and public in crime prevention efforts","Jabatan Pencegahan Jenayah dan Keselamatan Komuniti (JPJKK)"],[1,"120","1","Private Sector CCTV Installation in Crime Hotspots","The private sector will also be encouraged to install CCTV cameras in hotspots that connect to PDRM control centres through an open network platform","PDRM"],[1,"120","2","Crime Prevention Law and Regulation Review","Existing laws and regulations will be reviewed to improve crime prevention effectiveness.",""],[1,"120","2","Crime Prevention Through Environmental Design Integration","Crime Prevention through Environmental Design (CPTED) elements will be incorporated in the development of new residential and commercial areas.",""],[1,"120","2","Household Theft Deterrence Measures Promotion","Theft deterrent measures in homes, such as CCTV cameras and security alarm systems will be encouraged as part of public self-policing efforts.",""],[1,"120","5","Targeted Social Media Awareness Campaigns for Youth","The Government will undertake targeted social media campaigns aimed at high-risk groups, particularly the youth.",""],[1,"125","1","Safer Living Environment Initiative","The Eleventh Plan therefore aims to improve wellbeing through six focus areas: enabling universal access to quality healthcare; providing adequate and quality affordable housing; creating safer living environments; improving road safety and emergency services; fostering social cohesion and national unity; and increasing mass participation in sports.",""]],"116":[[1,"119","7","Enforcement Personnel Capacity and Capability Building Programme","The capacity and capabilities of enforcement personnel will be enhanced by providing the appropriate tools and capability building programmes.",""],[1,"119","7","International Policing Training and Exchange Collaboration","collaborations with international policing bodies could be leveraged to enhance the knowledge and skills of enforcement personnel through specialised training and exchange programmes.",""],[1,"119","7","Enforcement Integrity Awareness and Oversight Programme","The integrity of enforcement personnel will be bolstered through awareness programmes conducted by the Malaysian Institute of Integrity, and greater oversight by both the Malaysia Anti-Corruption Commission and the Enforcement Agencies Integrity Commission.",""],[1,"119","8","Inter-Agency Task Forces and Integrated Databases","Inter-agency collaboration will be facilitated through the establishment of task forces and integrated databases among the relevant agencies.",""],[1,"119","8","Cross-Border Crime Joint Operations and Enhanced Patrolling","Increased joint operations and enhanced patrolling to combat cross-border crime will ensure faster responses and optimisation of manpower and resources.",""],[1,"119","8","Bilateral and Multilateral Cooperation Against Trafficking and Smuggling","The Government will leverage on bilateral and multilateral relations to mitigate crimes such as human trafficking and smuggling.",""]],"117":[[1,"120","3","Foreign Worker Management Improvement","The management of foreign workers will be improved by enhancing the role of one-stop centre and through greater collaboration between the Immigration Department of Malaysia and local authorities to ensure effective enforcement.","Immigration Department of Malaysia | local authorities"],[1,"120","3","Student Visa Screening and Enforcement","to avoid student visa abuse, stricter screening procedures in countries of origin and stringent enforcement of regulations will be undertaken to ensure educational institutions with foreign students comply with immigration procedures.",""],[1,"120","4","Advanced Passenger Screening and Biometric Border Control System","Unlawful entry at immigration checkpoints will be curbed with the introduction of the Advanced Passenger Screening System (APSS), biometric, and facial recognition systems.",""],[1,"120","4","Joint Border Enforcement Operations","Efforts to stem increasing cross-border crime will be bolstered through joint operations of border enforcement agencies, such as the Malaysian Maritime Enforcement Agency, Anti-Smuggling Unit, and ATM.",""],[1,"120","4","Integrated Border Detection and Surveillance Enhancement","Integrated detection, monitoring, and surveillance capabilities will be enhanced including the introduction of sea-basing platforms to deter border intrusions.",""],[1,"143","4","Foreign Worker Management Reform","Strategy A3: Improving management of foreign workers by reducing the nation's reliance on low-skilled foreign workers and streamlining recruitment as well as immigration processes.",""],[1,"145","5","Comprehensive Foreign Worker Immigration and Employment Policy","A comprehensive immigration and employment policy for foreign workers will be formulated, taking into account the requirements of industry and the welfare of foreign workers.",""],[1,"145","6","Foreign Worker Levy Reform","The levy system will also be improved to better regulate the entry of low-skilled foreign workers.",""],[1,"145","7","Foreign Worker Recruitment Streamlining","The Government will streamline the recruitment of foreign workers by placing it under a single administration.","MoHR"],[1,"145","8","Strict Liability for Employers of Foreign Workers","The Government will introduce the strict liability concept whereby employers of foreign workers are fully responsible for their recruitment process and welfare.",""],[1,"145","8","Management and Enforcement Measures on Illegal Foreign Workers","the Government will address the issue of illegal foreign workers through better management and effective enforcement initiatives.",""]],"118":[[1,"109","8","Inmate Rehabilitation and Parole Programme","Inmate rehabilitation was undertaken through various methods, such as face- to-face family meetings, self-development programmes, and early release for rehabilitated inmates through the parole system.","Jabatan Penjara Malaysia"],[1,"109","8","Community Rehabilitation Programme","the Community Rehabilitation Programme (CRP) was implemented to provide inmates with the necessary technical skills to secure jobs upon reintegration into society so as to reduce recidivism and to reduce prison congestion.",""],[1,"112","12","Rehabilitation, Treatment, and Aftercare for Ex-Inmates and Drug Addicts","Enhancing rehabilitation, treatment, and aftercare to reduce recidivism among ex-inmates and relapse among drug addicts",""],[1,"119","5","Rehabilitation, Treatment, and Aftercare Strengthening Programme","A range of self-development programmes and community-based services will be strengthened to enable the successful reintegration of ex-inmates and drug addicts into society, and reduce recidivism and relapse.",""],[1,"120","6","Inmate and Drug Addict Rehabilitation and Aftercare Enhancement","Rehabilitation, treatment and aftercare of inmates and drug addicts will be enhanced to achieve the targeted recidivist rate of 5% and relapse rate of 35% by 2020.",""],[1,"120","6","Self-Development, Skills and Entrepreneurship Training for Ex-Inmates","To reduce the recidivist rate, the Government will strengthen self-development programmes that provide skills and entrepreneurship training, as well as provide more transit houses for ex-inmates.",""],[1,"120","6","Transit Houses for Ex-Inmates","To reduce the recidivist rate, the Government will strengthen self-development programmes that provide skills and entrepreneurship training, as well as provide more transit houses for ex-inmates.",""],[1,"120","6","Collaborative CRP for Drug Addicts","The CRP will be introduced for drug addicts through collaboration between the National Anti-Drugs Agency and related agencies.","National Anti-Drugs Agency"],[1,"120","6","NGO Support Services for Rehabilitation and Reintegration","In addition, NGOs will be encouraged to provide support services for rehabilitation, treatment, and reintegration such as job placement and aftercare programmes.",""]],"119":[[1,"103","2","Road Safety and Emergency Services Enhancement","A new focus area on enhancing road safety and emergency services will also be introduced.",""],[1,"114","3","Road Safety Awareness and Emergency Services Improvement","Strategies to improve road safety awareness and the effectiveness of emergency services will also be introduced.",""],[1,"116","4","Pre-hospital Care and Emergency Services Improvement","Initiatives will also focus on improving pre-hospital care such as ambulance services, as well as accident and emergency services.",""],[1,"116","4","Ambulance Service and Emergency Response Coordination","Collaboration among agencies that provide ambulance services, private healthcare providers, and NGOs will be strengthened to improve response time and better utilise resources.",""],[1,"121","1","Road Safety Improvement and Emergency Services Upgrade","The Government aspires to reduce the incidences of road accidents and improve the delivery of emergency services to be on par with international standards.",""],[1,"121","2","Road Safety Enforcement and Awareness Campaigns","Improving road safety to reduce accidents through more effective enforcement mechanisms and awareness campaigns;",""],[1,"121","4","Automated Road Enforcement and Penalty Review","This will be achieved through the wider implementation of the Automated Enforcement System (AES) and the review of KEJARA System or Sistem Kesalahan Jalan Raya, which imposes heavier penalties on errant drivers.",""],[1,"121","4","Road Safety Awareness Campaigns","At the same time, awareness campaigns will be further improved through the use of social media.",""],[1,"121","5","Cross-Agency Emergency Services Coordination","the Government will facilitate greater cross-agency collaboration.",""],[1,"121","5","First Responder Capacity Building Programme","the capability of first responders, rescuers, and dispatchers will be enhanced through specialised training and frequent emergency drills.",""],[1,"125","1","Road Safety and Emergency Services Improvement","The Eleventh Plan therefore aims to improve wellbeing through six focus areas: enabling universal access to quality healthcare; providing adequate and quality affordable housing; creating safer living environments; improving road safety and emergency services; fostering social cohesion and national unity; and increasing mass participation in sports.",""]],"120":[[1,"129","1","Labour Market Efficiency Improvement","The Government will focus on four areas: improving the efficiency of the labour market to accelerate economic growth, transforming TVET to meet industry demand, strengthening lifelong learning for skills enhancement, and improving the quality of the education system for better student outcomes and institutional excellence.",""],[1,"134","1","Regular Review of Labour Laws","Employment Act, 1955, Industrial Relations Act, 1967 and Trade Unions Act, 1959 were reviewed on a regular basis to keep pace with the dynamics of the labour market.",""],[1,"142","7","Labour Productivity Improvement Policy","Labour market policies will focus on improving labour productivity.",""],[1,"143","1","Labour Market Efficiency Improvement Strategy","the Government aims to improve the efficiency and operations of the labour market.",""],[1,"143","2","Productivity Linked Wage System Adoption","Key measures include the wider adoption of the Productivity Linked Wage System (PLWS), the shift from low- to high-skilled jobs, and the reduction of existing wage gaps;",""],[1,"143","3","Labour Market Operations Enhancement Strategy","Measures include regulatory reform, more integrated information to enhance decision making, closer integration with industry, and targeted programmes for youth and women;",""],[1,"143","6","Performance-Related Pay Scheme Expansion","The Government will further encourage the implementation of performance-related pay schemes through wider industry implementation of the PLWS.",""],[1,"143","7","Value Chain Upgrading and High-Value Investment Attraction","Existing industries will be encouraged to move up the value chain by investing in high value added activities that require skilled workers.",""],[1,"143","8","Minimum Wage Compliance and Revision Measures","Compensation of employees is expected to increase following greater compliance with minimum wage requirements, upward revisions in minimum wages linked to improved productivity, and enhanced recognition of prior learning (RPL).",""],[1,"144","2","Wage Index for Fair and Transparent Compensation","Introducing wage index as a guide for fair and transparent compensation",""],[1,"144","3","National Wage Index Development","The Government will establish a National Wage Index (NWI) that will serve as a guide and benchmark for employers in determining the right wage level for employees that is in accordance with their qualifications, skills, and productivity.","MoHR"],[1,"145","4","Labour Law Amendment Reform","The MoHR will amend labour-related legislation such as the Employment Act, 1955, Trade Unions Act, 1959, and the Industrial Relations Act, 1967.","MoHR"],[1,"145","5","Automation and Economic Upgrading Initiative","Greater automation especially in labour-intensive activities, as well as migration to knowledge-intensive activities will be encouraged in all sectors of the economy, particularly in the agriculture, manufacturing, and construction sectors, which currently employ more than 30% of foreign workers.",""]],"121":[[1,"142","7","Outcome Target Monitoring System","These targets will constantly be tracked and monitored to evaluate their progress.",""],[1,"142","8","National Human Capital Development Council","the Government will establish a high-powered National Human Capital Development Council (NHCDC).",""],[1,"144","5","Labour Market Information Database Enhancement","The LMIDW will be updated to include more demand-based information such as job openings, employment projections, and salaries to provide better insights into the demands of industry.",""],[1,"144","5","Labour Market Analytics Functionality Upgrade","The functionality and user friendliness of LMIDW will also be enhanced.",""],[1,"144","7","Industry Skills Committee Establishment","An Industry Skills Committee (ISC) will be established to serve as a platform for coordinated engagement of industry players, so as to gather information on the requirements of industry.","Ministry of International Trade and Industry (MITI)"],[1,"144","7","Industry Working Groups for Human Capital Requirements","To support the ISC, Industry Working Groups (IWG) will be established to identify specific human capital requirements beginning with 11 economic sectors.",""],[1,"144","7","Critical Skills Gap Committee Establishment","The Critical Skills Gap Committee under the joint purview of Talent Corporation and ILMIA will also be established to assist the ISC in identifying critical skills gaps, particularly in strategic sectors, for future human capital planning.",""]],"122":[[1,"143","6","Workforce Upskilling and Reskilling Programme","In addition, continuous upskilling and reskilling of the existing workforce will contribute to productivity growth.",""],[1,"145","2","Youth Training and Upskilling Programme","The Government will continue to ensure all youth have access to training opportunities before joining the labour market.",""],[1,"145","2","Youth Labour Market Upskilling Initiative","Youth in the labour market will also be given opportunities for upskilling, to equip them with better skills, and enable them to command higher salaries.",""],[1,"145","2","Youth Employment Preparation and Job Placement Programmes","Efforts to prepare youth for employment and secure job placements will be intensified through programmes such as SKK1M, NDTS and 1Malaysia Skills Training and Enhancement for the Rakyat (1MASTER).",""],[1,"145","3","Family-Friendly Employment Strategies","Female participation in the labour market will be further increased through more family-friendly employment strategies.",""],[1,"145","3","1Malaysia Support for Housewives and Flexiworklife Programmes","the Government will widen access to jobs through the 1Malaysia Support for Housewives and Flexiworklife programmes.",""],[1,"145","3","Women Entrepreneurship Promotion Programmes","Women will also be encouraged to become entrepreneurs through programmes such as Azam Niaga, Women Entrepreneurial Incubator, and 1Nita.",""],[1,"151","1","Industry-Based Employee Upskilling Programmes","Enhancing industry-based programmes to upskill employees",""],[1,"151","2","Industry-Based Upskilling Programmes","Industry-based upskilling programmes will be strengthened to upgrade the skills of existing employees.",""],[1,"151","2","Industry-Based Training in Construction and Automotive Industries","the CIDB and the Malaysian Automotive Institute (MAI) will initiate industry-based training in the construction and automotive industries.",""],[1,"151","2","Malaysian Meister Programme","The Malaysian Meister Programme (MMP), which is adapted from the German-Meister Programme, will be introduced to provide skills enhancement training for experienced employees.",""]],"123":[[1,"134","9","Partnership-Based Vocational College Curriculum Delivery","The vocational college curriculum is also offered in partnership with other public TVET institutions including Institut Latihan Perindustrian (ILP), under MoHR.","MoHR"],[1,"146","13","Industry Partnership Curriculum Reform","The ISC, in collaboration with industry players, will identify relevant competencies for each sector and sub-sector.",""],[1,"146","13","Work-Based Learning and Apprenticeship Expansion","This could include apprenticeships, internships, and work-based learning programmes.",""],[1,"146","13","Problem-Project-Production Learning Module Integration","\"Problem, Project, Production\" learning modules which engage students in authentic, \"real world\" tasks intended to simulate actual workplace situations, will also be embedded in the curriculum to better prepare students for the working environment.",""],[1,"147","1","Mainstreaming of the National Dual Training System","A concerted effort will be made to mainstream the NDTS to produce skilled TVET graduates demanded by industry.",""],[1,"147","1","Expansion of the 1MASTER NDTS Programme","The 1MASTER NDTS programme will be further expanded to support specific economic development areas and industry needs.",""],[1,"147","1","Special NDTS for Out-of-School Youth","A special NDTS for youth who have dropped out of the education system will also be expanded to provide training and certification that will enable them to secure better job opportunities.",""],[1,"147","1","Expansion of NDTS Institutional Participation","The NDTS will be expanded to involve more public and private institutions, and will also encourage increased participation from industry.",""],[1,"149","4","Industry-Led Curriculum and Centre of Excellence Development","Design and delivery of curriculum led by industry, in partnership with TVET institutions and Government Institutions to specialise in and create Centre of Excellence in niche areas of expertise","Government Institutions"]],"124":[[1,"143","8","Malaysia Board of Technologists Establishment","The recognition of technologists6 as professionals through the establishment of the Malaysia Board of Technologists (MBOT) will also improve wages of TVET graduates.",""],[1,"144","1","Technologist Profession Regulation and Development Body","body to regulate, promote, and develop the technologist profession in Malaysia.",""],[1,"148","12","Create Malaysia Board of Technologists","Create Malaysia Board of Technologist (MBOT)",""],[1,"149","12","Professional Ethics and Development Programme for Technologists","MBOT will determine and govern the ethics and conduct of the profession as well as provide guidance and professional development programmes for career advancement.",""]],"125":[[1,"155","2","Devolution of Decision-Making to State and District Education Offices","The Government will empower the Jabatan Pendidikan Negeri (JPN) or State Education Department and Pejabat Pendidikan Daerah_ (PPD) or District Education Office by devolving greater decision making rights to them.",""],[1,"155","3","School-Level PTA Community Engagement and Resource Mobilization","The Parent-Teacher Association (PTA) will drive school-level engagements with the community, private sector, non-governmental organisations, and other education providers, particularly with regard to securing additional expertise and funds.",""],[1,"155","3","Trust School Expansion Programme","The Trust School concept, a public-private partnership model, will be expanded to at least 90 schools by 2020.",""],[1,"155","3","Best Practice Identification for School Improvement","Based on the performance of these Trust Schools, the MoE will also identify best practices that can be used to improve teaching and learning in other schools.","MoE"]],"126":[[1,"155","4","Integrated School Dropout Reduction and Retention Programme","the MoE will collaborate with other relevant agencies and communities to implement an integrated approach to reduce dropout rates from preschool to upper secondary so as to ensure 100% enrolment by 2020","MoE"],[1,"155","4","Child Tracing and School Re-Engagement Initiative","Collaborative efforts will be established with local authorities and community leaders to trace children who have never attended school or who have dropped out",""],[1,"155","4","At-Risk Student Retention Programme","Students who are at risk of dropping out will be identified and intervention programmes to retain them in schools will be implemented",""]],"127":[[1,"157","1","Labour Market Efficiency Improvement","under the Eleventh Plan, the Government will improve the efficiency of the labour market to accelerate economic growth",""],[1,"157","1","Industry-Led TVET Expansion","enable industry-led TVET to meet industry demands",""],[1,"157","1","Lifelong Learning and Upskilling Expansion","expand lifelong learning for continuous upskilling",""],[1,"157","1","Education Quality Improvement Initiative","improve the quality of the education system for better student outcomes",""]],"128":[[1,"160","1","Green Growth Development Trajectory","The intention is to shift from the conventional and costly 'grow first, clean-up later' path to a more greener trajectory - Green Growth - which will ensure that socio- economic development is pursued more sustainably, beginning at the planning stage, and continuing throughout the implementation and evaluation stages.",""],[1,"161","3","Green Growth Enabling Environment Strengthening","To pursue green growth, the enabling environment will be strengthened - particularly in terms of policy and regulatory framework, human capital, green technology investment, and financial instruments.",""],[1,"170","3","Green Growth Strategy Framework","the Government will introduce a transformative green growth strategy framework.",""],[1,"172","1","Green Growth Policy and Institutional Framework","For this change to take place smoothly, the Government will provide the relevant policy and institutional framework for green growth.",""],[1,"172","1","Green Growth Capacity Building, Monitoring, and Evaluation Measures","Concurrently, measures and instruments to build capacity, monitor, and evaluate programmes to support green growth efforts will be put in place.",""],[1,"172","2","Governance Strengthening for Transformation","Strategy A1: Strengthening governance to drive transformation by enhancing regulatory and institutional framework, coordination, capacity as well as monitoring and evaluation mechanisms;",""],[1,"172","3","Shared Responsibility Awareness and Knowledge Sharing Programme","Enhancing awareness to create shared responsibility through comprehensive communication, education, and awareness programmes and platforms for knowledge sharing;",""],[1,"172","4","Sustainable Financing Mechanisms Expansion","Strategy A3: Establishing sustainable financing mechanisms by expanding existing and identifying new economic instruments.",""],[1,"173","1","Comprehensive Monitoring and Evaluation Mechanisms for Green Growth Initiatives","Comprehensive monitoring and evaluation mechanisms will be established to track and assess the effectiveness of green growth initiatives, as well as to facilitate planning and decision-making process, so as to enable continuous improvements in undertaken efforts.",""],[1,"173","1","National One-Stop Data Access Centre","a one-stop centre will be established to provide access and linkage to all data in the nation, including data that are housed in relevant agencies.",""],[1,"173","1","National Green Economy Indicator Development","new indicators such as the green economy indicators, resource indicators and inventory, and SCP indicators will be developed to complement existing ones, making them more meaningful in reflecting the current situation.",""],[1,"173","2","Communication, Education and Public Awareness Programmes","Communication, education and public awareness (CEPA) programmes engaging all levels of society will be enhanced to increase awareness about the environment, climate change adaptation and mitigation, conserving natural resources, and the role of green growth in raising productivity.",""],[1,"173","3","CEPA Programme Coordination and Integration","The Government will improve the effectiveness of CEPA programmes by coordinating and integrating public awareness messages communicated by different public sector agencies and on different themes - including demand side management, transport, energy consumption, recycling, biodiversity conservation, climate change, disaster risk management, and environmental pollution.",""],[1,"173","4","CEPA Programme Stakeholder Engagement","Besides Government-led initiatives, involvement of the private sector, NGOs, academia, and the rakyat in CEPA programmes will also be encouraged.",""],[1,"173","5","Green Growth Collaboration Platforms","Platforms will be created for sharing of best practices and collaboration on green growth related projects.",""],[1,"173","8","Green Financing Instruments Development","Economic instruments such as green tax, carbon tax, and REDD+ (reducing emissions from deforestation and forest degradation) will be utilised where appropriate to develop green financing systems.",""]],"129":[[1,"172","5","Green Industry Transition and Indigenous Green Technology Development","The policy, regulatory and institutional framework will be strengthened to encourage industries to shift to greening their products and services by adopting green technologies as well as accelerating innovation and development of indigenous green technology.",""],[1,"172","8","Green Growth Capacity and Skills Development Programme","The transition to green growth will be supported by developing the required capacities, capabilities, and skills at all levels.","relevant ministries and agencies at the federal, state and local levels | the private sector | academia"]],"130":[[1,"174","2","Government Green Procurement","Strategy B1: Creating green markets through Government green procurement, adoption of green buildings criteria and strengthening green certification;",""],[1,"174","2","Green Buildings Criteria Adoption","Strategy B1: Creating green markets through Government green procurement, adoption of green buildings criteria and strengthening green certification;",""],[1,"174","2","Green Certification Strengthening","Strategy B1: Creating green markets through Government green procurement, adoption of green buildings criteria and strengthening green certification;",""],[1,"174","7","Government Green Procurement and Green Market Promotion","The Ministry of Energy, Green Technology and Water (Kementerian Tenaga, Teknologi Hijau dan Air, KeTTHA) supported by relevant ministries and agencies will promote the development of a domestic market for green products and services.","The Ministry of Energy, Green Technology and Water (Kementerian Tenaga, Teknologi Hijau dan Air, KeTTHA)"],[1,"174","7","Green Buildings and Industrial Greening Initiative","Measures to be undertaken include implementing Government green procurement, promoting the development of green buildings and greening of industries to spur green growth.",""],[1,"174","7","Green Product and Service Supply Chain Development Support","A Government driven push will encourage local industries, especially small and medium enterprises, to develop green products and services, eventually leading to further greening of the supply chain.",""],[1,"174","8","Mandatory Government Green Procurement","Government green procurement (GGP) will be made mandatory for all government ministries and agencies.",""],[1,"174","8","Green Product Certification Support through Eco-Labelling","GGP will complement the existing eco-labelling scheme in the country for green products certification.",""],[1,"174","8","Private Sector Green Procurement Promotion","Concurrently, the private sector will also be encouraged to emulate Government efforts in green procurement.",""],[1,"174","9","Green Government Buildings and Retrofit Programme","New government buildings will adopt green features and designs, and use green building materials as per the Skim Penarafan Hijau Jabatan Kerja Raya Malaysia.",""],[1,"174","9","Private Building Green Certification Promotion","Industry players will also be encouraged to obtain green certification for private buildings such as GreenPASS and the",""],[1,"175","8","Sustainable Consumption and Production Project","Malaysia is undertaking the SCP project under the SWITCH-Asia Programme Policy Support Component for a period of four years, from February 2012 until January 2016.",""],[1,"175","10","Government Green Procurement Guidelines and Pilot Procurement Programme","Malaysia has developed GGP guidelines and as a pilot project that started in July 2013, five selected ministries have procured green products and services worth RM352 million as of April 2015.",""],[1,"175","11","SCP Integration in Formal Education Curriculum","Integrating SCP in the formal syllabi to instil sustainable behaviour among students.","Ministry of Education"],[1,"175","12","SCP Portal Development","SCP portal (www.scpmalaysia.gov.my): Developed to enhance awareness, knowledge and capacity of all levels towards green growth.",""],[1,"176","1","Green Building Index","Green Building Index.",""],[1,"176","2","Green Industry Rating and Standards System","Green rating systems and standards, aligned with international best practices, will be introduced to promote the greening of industries.",""],[1,"176","2","MyHijau Mark Green Product Labelling Expansion","the MyHijau Mark programme, a uniform labelling established by the Government for green products and services, will be expanded for key product areas such as household products, electronic and electrical appliances.",""],[1,"176","2","Industrial Self-Regulation for Pollution Mitigation","the Department of Environment (DOE) will expand self- regulation among industries to mitigate pollution at source, and cover new aspects such as noise and soil pollution, in addition to hazardous waste, water and air pollution.","Department of Environment (DOE)"]],"131":[[1,"180","1","Community Biodiversity Livelihood Training Programme","Communities that live on the fringes of protected areas and depend on natural resources will be trained to take on new opportunities to improve their quality of life.",""],[1,"180","3","Alternative Livelihoods for Indigenous and Local Communities","Strategy C2: Enhancing alternative livelihood for indigenous and local communities by involving them in biodiversity conservation and empowering them for alternative economic opportunities.",""],[1,"183","1","Alternative Livelihood Support for Indigenous and Local Communities","Indigenous and local communities (ILCs) living on the fringes of protected terrestrial and marine areas and largely dependent on natural resources for their livelihood will be provided with alternative economic opportunities to reduce this dependency and avoid illegal extraction of natural resources from these areas.",""],[1,"183","2","Community and Civil Society Participation in Protected Area Management","Active efforts to promote community and civil society participation, especially ILCs, in the planning and management processes of protected areas will be undertaken, including initiatives to proactively engage ILCs in conservation programmes.",""],[1,"183","3","ILC Capacity-Building Training Programmes","Capabilities of ILCs will be enhanced through participation in training programmes such as language courses, nature guides and entrepreneurship, as well as basic medical and emergency response to prepare them for alternative income generation.",""]],"132":[[1,"192","1","Infrastructure Network Expansion and Efficiency Improvement","As Malaysia moves closer to its vision of becoming an advanced economy and inclusive nation by 2020, the focus will not only be on further expanding the physical reach of these networks to all communities, but to improve the efficiency, productivity, and affordability of these services, and enhancing user experience.",""],[1,"192","1","Infrastructure Licensing and Regulatory Streamlining Reform","The Government will address issues of streamlining licences and regulations, and strengthen institutional frameworks to improve integrated planning and regulatory oversight of the industry.",""],[1,"192","1","Major Infrastructure Investment Pipeline","These efforts will lay the right \"software\" for infrastructure as new significant investments - from mass rapid transit system, high-speed broadband, expanded sewerage networks to new oil refining capacity - are rolled out in the next five years.",""],[1,"193","2","Fuel and Electricity Supply Security Strengthening","efforts to further strengthen the security of Malaysia's fuel and electricity supplies will be undertaken.",""],[1,"206","1","Infrastructure Network Performance and Affordability Improvement","In the Eleventh Plan, focus will not only be on expanding the physical capacity and reach of infrastructure networks, but improving their performance, productivity, and affordability.",""],[1,"206","4","New Power Generation Capacity Expansion","In energy sector, 7,626 MW new generation capacity will be installed in Peninsular Malaysia, along with 300,000 bpd refining capacity at PIPC, providing security to Malaysia's energy needs.",""]],"133":[[1,"207","3","Transport Operations Safety and Infrastructure Upgrade Strategy","Strategy A2: Improving safety, efficiency, and service levels of transport operations by shifting to preventive maintenance, improving road and rail safety, and upgrading air navigation and airport infrastructure;",""],[1,"207","7","Rural and Rural-Urban Highway Connectivity Development","The Eleventh Plan will therefore focus on rural and rural-urban connectivity.",""],[1,"207","7","Pan Borneo Highway Development","The Pan Borneo Highway will promote better connectivity in Sabah and Sarawak.",""],[1,"207","7","Central Spine Road and East Coast Highway Development","Further development of the Central Spine Road, Kota Bharu- Kuala Krai Highway, and the Lebuh Raya Pantai Timur will improve connectivity in Peninsular Malaysia and catalyse growth in the east coast region.",""],[1,"207","7","West Coast Expressway Completion","The completion of the West Coast Expressway in 2019 will also provide better access to the west coast of Perak and Selangor.",""],[1,"207","7","Comprehensive Road Planning Needs Analysis","A comprehensive needs analysis will be adopted in road planning to ensure effective decision-making on whether to upgrade existing roads or construct new ones.",""],[1,"208","10","Rural Road Connectivity Improvement","Rural roads linking the main road networks will continue to be given focus.",""],[1,"211","2","Preventive Road Maintenance Programme","Road maintenance programmes will focus on preventive maintenance by adopting a life-cycle costing approach.",""],[1,"211","2","Advanced Materials and Innovative Technology for Road Infrastructure","Utilisation of advanced materials and innovative technology in road construction and maintenance will be intensified to ensure durability of road infrastructure.",""],[1,"211","2","Rail Asset Refurbishment and Track Replacement Programme","Maintenance of rail assets will focus on refurbishment of rolling stocks and replacement of tracks and sleepers.",""],[1,"211","3","Road and Rail Safety Improvement Programme","Road and rail safety will be improved during the Eleventh Plan.",""]],"134":[[1,"207","4","National Port Capacity and Accessibility Expansion","Strategy A3: Expanding port capacity, access, and operations through the National Port Policy, a port community system, and improving port accessibility and capacity;",""],[1,"211","6","Port Capacity Expansion and Congestion Reduction","attention will be given to expanding capacity of ports and address issues in congestion.",""],[1,"211","7","National Port Policy Implementation","The National Port Policy will be implemented to foster systematic development and growth of ports and jetties by introducing comprehensive strategy and policy measures.",""],[1,"211","7","Secondary Port Network Strengthening","Major hub ports will be strengthened by networks of secondary ports to improve competitiveness of the national logistics chain.",""],[1,"211","7","Port Land Use Planning Integration","In addition, port development will take into account land use planning to ensure the sustainable growth of major ports.",""],[1,"211","8","Port Community System Establishment","All port authorities will be required to establish their port community system (PCS), an open electronic system that enables intelligent and secure information exchange between public and private stakeholders.",""],[1,"211","8","Single Communications Platform for Ports","A single communications platform will promote information sharing among ports and private stakeholders such as logistics firms and customs agents.",""],[1,"212","1","Port Channel Deepening Works","Accessibility to major ports will be improved to cater for bigger vessels through channel deepening works.",""],[1,"212","1","Port Capacity Expansion Programme","In addition, port operators will undertake capacity expansion, which includes building additional berths and wharfs.",""],[1,"216","3","Port Klang Last-Mile Connectivity Improvement","The last-mile connectivity to Port Klang, Selangor via road and rail will be improved to cope with the rise in container volume.",""],[1,"216","3","Westports-Northport Rail Link Upgrade","Priority will be given to upgrading the rail link between Westports and Northport to reduce congestion and encourage rail freight.",""],[1,"216","3","Port Klang Road Capacity Upgrades","Critical stretches along Jalan Pelabuhan Utara and Pulau Indah Highway will be upgraded to ease congestion and enable the seamless movement of goods.",""],[1,"216","3","Port Klang Traffic Information Systems","the usage of traffic information systems will be promoted for better traffic management within Port Klang.",""],[1,"216","4","Padang Besar Terminal Upgrade","The Padang Besar Terminal in Perlis will be upgraded to capture the potential growth in cargo volume",""]],"135":[[1,"193","2","Integrated Logistics and Trade Facilitation","The Government will work with the private sector to create an integrated logistics, which coupled with an efficient trade facilitation will further boost Malaysia's trade.",""],[1,"206","2","Logistics Industry Strengthening","The logistics industry will therefore be strengthened.",""],[1,"214","2","National Logistics Task Force Institutional and Regulatory Strengthening","Strategy B1: Strengthening the institutional and regulatory framework through the National Logistics Task Force (NLTF) and regulating other functions such as off-dock depots, warehousing activities, and commercial vehicle registrations;",""],[1,"214","3","Trade Facilitation Mechanisms Enhancement","Strategy B2: Enhancing trade facilitation mechanisms through collaboration to reduce cargo clearance time and greater paperless trading;",""],[1,"214","4","Freight Infrastructure Efficiency and Capacity Improvement","Strategy B3: Building freight infrastructure efficiency and capacity by improving last-mile connectivity at Port Klang and expanding air and rail freight infrastructure;",""],[1,"214","5","E-commerce Virtual Selling Platforms and Logistics Infrastructure Development","Deploying technology in the logistics chain through development of virtual selling platforms and supporting logistics infrastructure for e-commerce;",""],[1,"214","6","Logistics Service Provider Training and Accreditation Programme","Strengthening the capabilities of logistics service providers through training and accreditation programmes.",""],[1,"214","7","National Logistics and Trade Facilitation Master Plan Implementation","the NLTF will implement the National Logistics and Trade Facilitation Master Plan, providing strategic direction for the development of the logistics industry and further improving its productivity and competitiveness.",""],[1,"214","8","Off-Dock Depot Regulation and Management System","The Land Public Transport Commission (SPAD) will be given the mandate and capacity to ensure the orderly development of off-dock depots.",""],[1,"214","9","National Warehouse Planning and Inventory System","The planning and development of warehousing activities will be placed under the purview of MOT.","MOT | Ministry of Urban Wellbeing, Housing and Local Government (KPKT)"],[1,"215","1","Commercial Vehicle Registration Simplification","Efforts will be focused on simplifying the commercial vehicle registration process.",""],[1,"215","1","Landing Permit Processing Time Reduction","processing time for application of landing permits for non-scheduled flights will be shortened.",""],[1,"215","2","Heavy Vehicle Axle Load and Prime Mover Interchangeability Review","In order to optimise vehicle utilisation and enhance road freight efficiency, the axle load for heavy vehicles and the interchangeability of prime movers for different trailers will be reviewed.",""],[1,"216","1","Cargo Clearance Process Streamlining Initiative","Collaboration between the Royal Department of Customs and permit issuing agencies will be strengthened to shorten cargo clearance processing time without compromising security.","Royal Department of Customs | permit issuing agencies"],[1,"216","2","Paperless Trading through u-Customs","Paperless trading will be driven through u-Customs to encourage industry players and permit issuing agencies to gradually reduce the usage of hardcopy documents.",""],[1,"216","2","Trade Document Security Enhancement","The security of the trade documents will be enhanced with better features and standards to ensure only genuine documents are used.",""],[1,"216","5","Kota Kinabalu Airport Cargo Handling Upgrade","The cargo handling facilities and freighter service at Kota Kinabalu International Airport will be upgraded based on demand to support the export of agricultural produce, particularly aquacultural products.",""],[1,"216","5","KLIA Cargo Facilities Review","the need for cargo facilities such as cool ports and staging areas to consolidate and facilitate cargo movement at KLIA will be reviewed.",""],[1,"216","5","Former Low-Cost Carrier Terminal Cargo Hub Conversion","the former low-cost carrier terminal will be transformed into a regional cargo hub.",""],[1,"217","1","Virtual Selling Platforms for Logistics Services","Virtual selling platforms will be promoted to match logistics supply and demand.",""],[1,"217","2","E-commerce Fulfilment Centre Development","Supporting logistics facilities for e-commerce featuring fulfilment centres will be developed at strategic locations to increase the efficiency and productivity of online retailers.",""],[1,"217","2","SME Online Market Access Support","In addition, SMEs will be encouraged to go online and gain access to a wider market through fulfilment centres.",""],[1,"217","3","Urban Logistics Services Initiative","The development of urban logistics services will be given priority to encourage efficient distribution of goods purchased online in the urban areas.",""],[1,"217","4","Logistics Industry Skills Enhancement Programme","Skills of professionals in the logistics industry will be enhanced through on-the-job training programmes.",""],[1,"217","4","Logistics Short-Term Courses and Certification Initiative","universities and training institutes will be encouraged to offer logistics-related short-term courses or certification programmes to improve competency.",""],[1,"217","4","Industry-Led Logistics Training Collaboration","Efforts will be undertaken to enhance industry-led training through greater collaboration between training institutions and industry experts.",""],[1,"217","5","Logistics Service Provider Accreditation System","An accreditation system for logistics service providers will be introduced to certify companies that comply with regulations and adopt best practices such as green logistics and information, communications and technology (ICT) applications.",""]],"136":[[1,"206","3","Broadband Access Pricing and Consumer Protection Reform","Key infrastructure roll-out initiatives such as High-Speed Broadband 2 (HSBB 2), Sub- Urban Broadband (SUBB), and Digital Terrestrial Television (DTT) will be undertaken during this period, along with policies to improve access pricing and consumer protection frameworks.",""],[1,"218","3","Improved Access Pricing Framework","Strategy C2: Increasing affordability and protection for consumers through an improved Access Pricing Framework (APF) and setting standards for consumer protection;",""],[1,"218","3","Consumer Protection Standards","Strategy C2: Increasing affordability and protection for consumers through an improved Access Pricing Framework (APF) and setting standards for consumer protection;",""]],"137":[[1,"221","1","Strengthening the Communications and Multimedia Self-Regulatory Framework","The self-regulatory framework under the Communications and Multimedia Act 1998 will be strengthened to enhance consumer protection.",""],[1,"221","1","Strengthening Monitoring and Compliance for Service Providers","In addition, the monitoring and compliance framework will also be strengthened to impose stiffer penalties on service providers for non- compliance.",""],[1,"221","2","Telco Star Rating System","a Star Rating System for telcos will be introduced to assist consumers in making informed choices about service providers.",""],[1,"221","3","General Consumer Code Review and Service Provider Guidance","The General Consumer Code (GCC) will be reviewed to provide model procedures for service providers on reasonably meeting consumer requirements, handling consumer complaints, protecting consumer information and promoting a high level of consumer confidence in service delivery from the industry.",""]],"138":[[1,"218","4","Second Phase of Digital Terrestrial Television Implementation","Migrating to DTT by implementing the second phase of DTT and introducing value-added services;",""],[1,"221","5","Digital Terrestrial Television Phase Two Roll-out","The second phase of the Digital Terrestrial Television (DTT) service will be implemented in 2016-2017, covering 46 areas nationwide including 24 areas in Sabah and Sarawak.",""],[1,"221","6","Digital Terrestrial Television Value-Added Services Development","In addition to providing TV and radio services, DTT opens the room for new value added services through televisions, as well as spurs the development of content and applications, which contributes to the growth of the content and software solutions industry.",""]],"139":[[1,"224","4","Sewage Treatment Plant Rationalisation and Upgrading","and by rationalising and upgrading sewage treatment plants",""],[1,"224","8","Sewerage Service Tariff Setting Mechanism","A new tariff setting mechanism will also be implemented for sewerage service to cover operational cost.",""],[1,"225","3","Rural Sewerage Service Expansion","Connected sewerage services will be extended to rural areas through solutions tailored for population agglomerations of less than 5,000 people.",""],[1,"225","5","Sewage Treatment Plant Rationalisation and Upgrading Programme","In the Eleventh Plan, 3,000 small and inefficient sewage treatment plants will be rationalised through the construction of regional and centralised plants with larger capacities and efficient technologies.",""],[1,"225","5","Sewage Treatment Plant Upgrading with Mechanical and Electrical Components","In areas where such plants are not feasible, existing treatment plants will be upgraded with new mechanical and electrical components to ensure effluent levels are compliant with standards.",""],[1,"225","5","Alternative Financing for Sewage Infrastructure","Alternative financing methods based on privatisation concepts will be further promoted as a new source of capital.",""],[1,"226","2","National Sewerage Master Plan Development","The National Water Services Commission (SPAN) will develop the National Sewerage Master Plan to provide integrated and holistic long- term policy directions and strategic shifts for the sewerage services industry.","The National Water Services Commission (SPAN)"],[1,"226","3","Waste-to-Wealth Initiatives for Sewerage Service Operators","Waste to wealth initiatives will be actively promoted for sewerage service operators.",""],[1,"226","4","National Sewerage Master Plan Guidelines","Guidelines will be introduced under the National Sewerage Master Plan to lay necessary requirements to support these initiatives.",""],[1,"226","4","Service Operator SOP Strengthening","service operators will be encouraged to strengthen their standard operating procedures.",""]],"140":[[1,"227","1","Energy Security and Subsector Infrastructure Improvement Strategy","Malaysia is committed to ensuring energy security for the nation while improving infrastructure and service delivery for the oil, gas and electricity subsectors.",""],[1,"227","1","Energy Subsidy Rationalisation and Market-Based Pricing Reform","Underpinning these efforts are continuing policies to rationalise energy subsidies and move towards a market- based energy pricing so that energy resources are utilised optimally.",""],[1,"227","2","Energy Sector Stakeholder Coordination and Collaboration Strategy","Strategy E1: Strengthening stakeholder coordination and collaboration in the energy sector through greater institutional collaboration on energy planning and engaging end-users on efficient energy consumption;",""],[1,"227","7","Energy Sector Stakeholder Coordination and Collaboration Strategy","Strategy E1 Strengthening stakeholder coordination and collaboration in the energy sector Fostering greater institutional collaboration on energy planning",""],[1,"227","8","Energy Sector Inter-Agency Governance Framework","A comprehensive governance, that allows for more structured inter- agency collaboration in the area of planning and management for the energy sector, will be instituted.",""],[1,"227","8","High-Level Energy Policy Coordination Focal Point","A high-level focal point in the Government will be established to oversee and streamline all energy related policy decisions and execution.",""],[1,"227","8","National Petroleum Advisory Council Energy Planning Mandate","National Petroleum Advisory Council will oversee comprehensive planning and management of the energy sector and streamline the interests of all parties.",""],[1,"227","9","Energy Resource Communication and Public Awareness Plan","A comprehensive and effective communication plan on the sustainable use of energy resources is required to improve public awareness and understanding, and to manage public perception of the subsidy rationalisation programme.",""],[1,"227","9","Energy Efficiency Public Awareness Programme","This includes communications and public awareness programmes to build buy-in for the development of coal and nuclear power plants required for security of supply, and for consumers to use energy efficiently in homes, schools, and at workplaces.",""],[1,"227","9","Energy Communication Coordination Task Force","A task force comprising of representatives of the Government, the private sector, and non-government organisations (NGOs) will be formed to ensure coordinated implementation of the plan.",""],[1,"228","4","Market-Based Energy Pricing Reform","Sustained efforts to institute market-based energy pricing will be carried out to reduce the amount of energy subsidies.",""],[1,"228","5","Gas Supply Pricing Structure Review","review the pricing structure for gas supply will be continued during the Eleventh Plan to gradually align current piped gas prices towards market prices.",""],[1,"228","5","Incentive-Based Gas Regulation","In addition, Incentive Based Regulation (IBR) for gas will be introduced to ensure efficient resource allocation, usage and sustainable financial performance.",""],[1,"228","5","Managed Float Fuel Price Regulation","The price for RON 95 petrol, RON 97 petrol and diesel will continue to be regulated using the managed float system to stem leakages.",""],[1,"228","5","CNG Price Review and Retail Infrastructure Expansion","Compressed natural gas (CNG) prices will also be reviewed accordingly to gradually remove subsidies and encourage expansion of CNG retail infrastructure.",""],[1,"229","1","Gas Market Competition and Subsidy Reform","fair competition will be encouraged and a vibrant gas supply market will be created while local industries will be weaned off subsidies.",""]],"141":[[1,"228","1","Gas Supply Security Infrastructure Expansion","Gas supply security would be ensured through the construction of pipelines from the Malaysia-Thailand Joint Development Area to Kerteh, Terengganu; construction of the RGT-2 in Pengerang, Johor; and the commissioning of two floating LNG units offshore Sabah and Sarawak with a capacity of 2.7 mtpa.",""],[1,"228","1","Emergency Gas Supply Buffer and Swing Field Provision","In addition, to ensure undisrupted supply during emergencies, a swing field offshore east of Peninsular Malaysia will provide an additional 100-200 mmscfd of natural gas.",""],[1,"228","1","Gas Storage Capacity Buffer for Peninsular Malaysia","These additional volumes, together with a 15% buffer of storage capacity from RGT-1 in Sungai Udang, Melaka, will cater for gas demand in Peninsular Malaysia.",""],[1,"228","2","Sabah Gas Supply Reliability and Connectivity Upgrades","Reliability of gas supply in Sabah will be improved with additional pipeline connections from offshore fields to demand centres in FT Labuan, as well as Kota Kinabalu and Kimanis in Sabah.",""],[1,"228","2","Alternative Gas Pipeline Bypass Links","Platforms will be connected through multiple links to provide alternative bypass options and provide capacity to users in the event of platform shutdowns.",""],[1,"228","2","Sabah-Sarawak Gas Pipeline Connection to FT Labuan","Improved connectivity for FT Labuan will be realised through the establishment of a pipeline connection between the Sabah-Sarawak Gas Pipeline and FT Labuan.",""],[1,"228","2","Advanced Technology for Stranded Gas Monetisation","In addition, advanced technology will be deployed in mature and marginal fields to monetise stranded gas.",""],[1,"228","3","Virtual Pipeline Natural Gas Distribution","Distribution of natural gas to scattered and uneconomic demand areas in Peninsular Malaysia and Sabah will be served through virtual pipelines, which is a method of distributing natural gas from city gate to consumers using trucks.",""],[1,"228","3","Alternative Natural Gas Distribution Methods Exploration","Safe and economic alternative distribution methods for natural gas will also be explored.",""]],"142":[[1,"230","7","Electricity Tariff Subsidy Rationalisation","subsidy rationalisation for electricity tariffs will continue to be implemented.",""],[1,"231","7","Incentive-Based Regulation for Utility Efficiency","The implementation of IBR will be continued to ensure utility companies provide efficient services.",""],[1,"231","7","Electricity Tariff Separation and Automatic Adjustment Mechanism","The separation of generation, transmission, and distribution tariffs with automatic adjustments to take into account changes in fuel prices will increase transparency and efficiency of electricity supply as illustrated in Box 7-3.",""],[1,"231","7","Competitive Bidding for Power Plant Expansion","New additions of power plants and extensions of existing power plants will continue to be selected through competitive bidding for greater transparency.",""],[1,"232","3","Electricity Tariff Regulation under the IBR Model","Under this new model, the Energy Commission, approves the electricity tariff based on a 3-year operations and investment plan submitted by the power utility company.",""],[1,"232","3","Electricity Utility Unbundling","unit of Generation, Transmission, Distribution, Single Buyer and System Operator is unbundled from an accounting standpoint.",""],[1,"232","3","Utility Efficiency Incentive Mechanism","The IBR model further incentivises efficiency gains by the utility, the benefits of which can be passed through to the consumer.",""],[1,"232","7","Imbalance Cost Pass-Through Mechanism","Enables periodic pass-through of fuel-related and other generation specific costs through the Imbalance Cost Pass-Through mechanism, while providing a fair return to the utility;",""]],"143":[[1,"236","1","Enterprise and Societal Innovation Promotion","Efforts to promote innovation will be undertaken at the enterprise and societal levels.",""],[1,"237","1","Productivity Enhancement and Economic Growth Strategy","A more cohesive and comprehensive approach to raise productivity will be implemented across national, industry, and enterprise levels.",""],[1,"240","2","Economic Transformation Programme","The Government embarked on the Economic Transformation Programme to further fuel economic growth and productivity, including further liberalisation of the services sector.",""],[1,"250","1","Knowledge-Intensive Growth and Innovation Investment","Accelerating the momentum of economic growth by expanding knowledge-intensive activities and producing complex products, increasing productivity and innovation, and investing in cities and regional economic corridors.",""],[1,"250","2","Economic Growth Acceleration and Diversification Strategy","During the Eleventh Plan, the focus is on accelerating the momentum of economic growth to place the economy on a strong foundation for sustained expansion and to withstand economic shocks.",""],[1,"250","2","High-Income Economy Transition Measures","Achieving this target will entail further broadening of the economic base, venturing into knowledge-intensive and complex economic activities to generate high-paying jobs, improving overall efficiency and capacity through increased productivity and innovation, and introducing new sources of growth.",""],[1,"251","1","Services Sector Blueprint Implementation","In the Eleventh Plan, the development of the services sector will be guided by the Services Sector Blueprint, which aims to unlock the potential of the sector and transform it to become more knowledge- intensive and innovation-led.",""]],"144":[[1,"251","3","Integrated Governance Reform Coordination","Strategy A2: Implementing comprehensive and integrated governance reforms by strengthening coordination and",""],[1,"251","6","Investment Incentives Management Reform","Strategy A4: Enhancing the management of investment incentives with a more effective, transparent, and performance- based incentives programme;",""],[1,"252","7","Strengthened Inter-Ministerial Coordination and Collaboration","coordination and collaboration between ministries, agencies, and other relevant stakeholders will be strengthened to improve their effectiveness and efficiency.",""],[1,"252","7","Special Committee on the Services Sector Oversight Mechanism","The Special Committee on the Services Sector will oversee the implementation of the services sector development strategies and action plans, particularly the Services Sector Blueprint, the Logistics and Trade Facilitation Master Plan (LTFMP), and the Construction Industry Transformation Programme (CITP).",""],[1,"252","8","Comprehensive Governance Reform for the Services Sector","Comprehensive and integrated governance reforms will be pursued to ensure a thriving and competitive environment for the services sector.",""],[1,"252","8","National Policy on the Development and Implementation of Regulations","The National Policy on the Development and Implementation of Regulations (NPDIR) to modernise the current regulatory regime will be fully implemented to include states and local governments.",""],[1,"252","8","Strengthening of Regulatory Coordinator Capacity","The capacity of regulatory coordinators in ministries and agencies will be strengthened to ensure adherence to the NPDIR.",""],[1,"252","8","Regulatory Alignment with Trade Commitments","The regulatory reform will also be aligned to Malaysia's commitments in existing free trade agreements and unilateral liberalisation initiatives.",""],[1,"252","8","Regulatory Portal Development","A regulatory portal will be established to improve access to and transparency of regulations.",""],[1,"253","2","Performance-Based Investment Incentive Reform","The current investment incentive programme will be replaced with a more effective, transparent, and performance-based incentive programme to attract quality investment and boost productivity.",""],[1,"253","2","Incentive Coordination and Collaboration Office","The Incentive Coordination and Collaboration Office (ICCO) will be established under the Malaysian Investment Development Authority (MIDA) to act as a coordinator for all investment incentives.","Malaysian Investment Development Authority (MIDA)"],[1,"253","2","Investment Incentive Impact Assessment and Monitoring","In addition, ICCO will undertake an impact assessment on the incentives provided, besides assisting in high-level monitoring from a demand perspective.",""],[1,"264","5","Business Formation Simplification and Formalisation Reform","Enhancing ease of doing business by simplifying the process of formation and formalising of businesses as well as increasing ease of access to financing;",""],[1,"265","1","Business Registration and Licensing System Integration","The on-going integration of Malaysia Corporate Identity Number (MyCoID) and Business Licensing Electronic Support System (BLESS) will simplify the process of formation and formalising of businesses.",""]],"145":[[1,"252","5","Demand-Driven, Private Sector-Led R&D&C Mechanism","(R&D&C) that is mainly supply-driven today will be replaced with a mechanism that is demand-driven and private sector-led.",""],[1,"252","6","Expansion of the Research Incentive Scheme for Enterprises","The Research Incentive Scheme for Enterprises will be expanded to enhance technology absorption and allow companies to hire experienced R&D researchers by partially funding the monthly wages of researchers for a specified period.",""],[1,"252","6","Support for R&D Centres and Centres of Excellence in Priority Technologies","This incentive is expected to attract technology leaders to set up R&D centres or centres of excellence (CoE) in prioritised technology focus areas, such as big data analytics, cloud computing, and the Internet of Things (IoT).",""],[1,"258","3","Innovation Finance Access Improvement Measures","Improvements will be undertaken to strengthen the enablers including encouraging financial institutions to better understand innovation processes and risks to improve access to financing, mainly by engaging panels of experts when evaluating business and innovation projects in new areas.",""],[1,"258","3","Performance-Based Incentive Scheme for Productivity and Innovation","Specific and performance-based incentives, with clear key performance indicators and exit policy, will be introduced to raise productivity and spur innovation.",""],[1,"264","3","Technology Commercialisation Platform","continuing the Technology Commercialisation Platform (TCP) and Inclusive Innovation programmes",""],[1,"264","3","Inclusive Innovation Programmes","continuing the Technology Commercialisation Platform (TCP) and Inclusive Innovation programmes",""],[1,"264","9","SME Automation and ICT Adoption Support","SMEs will be encouraged to adopt greater automation in production processes and business services.",""],[1,"264","9","ICT Utilisation Promotion for Business Operations","Greater ICT utilisation will be promoted, mainly in business operations, supply chain management, and delivery systems.",""],[1,"264","9","TCP Innovation Facilitation Platform","The TCP links innovation initiatives under one platform and aims to remove market and financing barriers to innovation.",""],[1,"264","9","PlaTCOM TCP Implementation Support","PlaTCOM, established in 2014, will continue to implement the TCP to assist SMEs to innovate and commercialise products and services.",""]],"146":[[1,"252","4","Embed ICT Programme for Services Firms","The utilisation of technology, particularly ICT, will be enhanced among services firms through the Embed ICT programme to reduce dependence on low-skilled foreign workers and to boost productivity.",""],[1,"254","2","ICT Niche Area Promotion and Export Expansion","In the ICT industry, niche areas will be further promoted and export capabilities enhanced to ensure that Malaysia captures a bigger export market for ICT products and services.",""],[1,"254","3","ICT Ecosystem Strengthening Initiative","the ICT ecosystem will be strengthened, including the capacity of start-ups, talent, infrastructure, R&D&C, and governance.",""],[1,"254","4","Local Digital Content Quality and Export Promotion Initiative","The quality of local digital content will be improved to further strengthen the export potential of local digital content.",""],[1,"254","4","Digital Content IP Financing and Commercialisation Support","The number of registered digital content IPs will be increased and exploited as collateral for loan financing, product line expansion, and licensing and merchandising.",""],[1,"254","4","Digital Content Industry Capacity and Market Access Initiative","Three main initiatives that will be implemented are attracting anchor companies to serve as industry drivers, building local capacity and capability, and raising global market access through a better understanding of global technology trends towards greater adoption of digital distribution and new business models.",""],[1,"254","8","ICT Export Promotion and Industry Support Ecosystem Strengthening","Improve exports of ICT products and services by developing ICT technology focus areas, infusing ICT in other sectors and strengthening ICT industry support ecosystem",""]],"147":[[1,"254","11","Private Higher Education Quality Assurance and Self-Regulation Incentives","Continue to develop reputable and high-quality private higher education institutions through ratings and quality assessments and self-regulation incentives",""],[1,"255","3","Private Higher Education Quality and Self-Regulation Enhancement","Continued focus will be given to developing reputable and high-quality private higher education institutions.",""],[1,"255","3","Academic Staff Scholarship and Loan Support","Academic staff will be given greater access to scholarships and loans to improve their academic qualifications.",""],[1,"255","3","Targeted Student Financing Mechanism","A targeted financing mechanism will be developed to ensure eligible students receive adequate funding.",""]],"148":[[1,"255","4","Ecotourism Development and Promotion Programme","Ecotourism will be positioned as a premier segment of the tourism industry by leveraging biodiversity assets through extensive protection and conservation, supported by targeted branding and promotion activities.",""],[1,"255","4","High-Yield Ecotourism Value Chain Development","Ecotourism products will be developed along the value chain of high-yield tourism by attracting reputable investors who are competent in the conservation and preservation of nature and wildlife.",""],[1,"255","4","Ecotourism Facilities and Safety Upgrading","Experience-enriching elements, such as tourism facilities, interpretive centres, safety measures, and communications, will be strengthened.",""],[1,"255","4","Community-Based Ecotourism Income Generation Initiative","The development of ecotourism will also offer greater opportunities for local communities to participate in related income-generation activities to raise living standards.",""]],"149":[[1,"257","4","Access to Financing and Performance-Based Incentives Strategy","Strategy B4: Strengthening growth enablers by improving access to financing, prioritising performance-based incentives as well as increasing competitiveness of the logistics supply chain and industrial estates;",""],[1,"257","6","Strategic Diversification of Manufacturing Exports","Strategic diversification of the manufacturing sector will be promoted to strengthen its output base and increase exports.",""],[1,"257","7","Frontier Product Diversification Incentives","Manufacturers will be incentivised to diversify into frontier products which will be included in the promoted list of products under MIDA.",""],[1,"257","7","Expanded SME and Start-up Frontier Industry Funding","The scope of funds under various agencies will be expanded to encourage SMEs and start-ups to venture into frontier industries.",""],[1,"257","7","SME-Large Company Partnership Promotion","Partnerships between SMEs and large companies, including MNCs,",""],[1,"257","8","SME Frontier Product and Export Market Development","will be encouraged to develop the capabilities of SMEs to venture into frontier products and gain access to export markets.",""],[1,"257","8","Collaborative Research Task Force for Chemicals and M&E Subsector","A task force will be established to foster collaborative research in the chemicals and M&E subsectors by emulating the model of the Collaborative Research in Engineering, Science & Technology (CREST) Centre for the E&E subsector.",""],[1,"257","8","Industry-TVET Skills Gap Bridging Initiative","skills gaps in the identified industries producing frontier products will be bridged through closer collaboration between industries and technical and vocational education and training (TVET) institutions.",""],[1,"258","5","Export Market Access and Distribution Support","The Malaysia External Trade Development Corporation (MATRADE) and related agencies will strengthen their capability to assist export-ready companies across all sectors to penetrate a wider export market and strengthen product distribution.",""],[1,"258","5","Mid-Tier Companies Development Programme Intensification","The Mid-Tier Companies Development Programme will be further intensified to accelerate export growth by mid-tier companies (companies with average annual revenues of RM20 million to RM500 million) by providing targeted market intelligence, building export capabilities, and matchmaking mid-tier companies with suitable business partners abroad.",""],[1,"258","5","National Export Council","the newly established National Export Council will address gaps and challenges in the export supply chain.",""],[1,"258","6","Industry Association Partnership Strengthening","The role of industry associations will also be further strengthened to deal with global competition through smart partnerships with industry associations in target export markets.",""],[1,"258","6","Vendor Development Programme","greater collaboration between MNCs and SMEs will continue to be fostered through the Vendor Development Programme and the factory-in-factory concept.",""],[1,"258","6","Factory-in-Factory Collaboration Concept","greater collaboration between MNCs and SMEs will continue to be fostered through the Vendor Development Programme and the factory-in-factory concept.",""],[1,"258","6","Local SME Sourcing Incentives for MNCs","MNCs will also be encouraged to source for inputs locally, particularly from SMEs.",""],[1,"264","6","SME Procurement Policy Review and Export Standards Support","Increasing demand for SME products and services by reviewing policies for procurement from SMEs and encouraging SMEs to obtain international standards and certifications to increase exports;",""],[1,"264","7","Catalyst Programme for High-Performing SME Development","Strategy E5: Creating home-grown champions through the Catalyst Programme to build high performing SMEs into regional and international players;",""],[1,"265","2","SME Procurement Policy Review","Government policy on procurement from competitive SMEs will be reviewed to increase the demand for high-quality local products and services.",""],[1,"265","2","Local SME Supplier Development and Procurement Promotion","Similarly, government-linked companies (GLCs) and MNCs will be encouraged to procure from local SMEs and invest in supplier development programmes.",""],[1,"265","2","SME Consortium Market Access Support","The SMEs will leverage the consortium approach to take advantage of market opportunities for large orders.",""],[1,"265","2","SME Standards and Certification Compliance Support","SMEs will also be encouraged to comply with international market standards and certifications, such as good manufacturing practices (GMP), eco-labelling, and Hazard Analysis & Critical Control Points (HACCP).",""],[1,"265","2","Going Export Programme Scale-Up","To further boost exports, the Going Export (GoEx) Programme will be scaled up to assist SMEs to venture into exports.",""],[1,"265","3","Catalyst Programme for High-Potential SMEs","The Catalyst Programme will help to remove barriers and provide assistance to potential SMEs to become home-grown champions who can compete in regional and international markets.",""]],"150":[[1,"257","9","Industry-Led Training Collaboration Initiative","The emphasis on skills development will be driven by enhancing industry-led training through greater collaboration between industry experts and training institutes to ensure workforce readiness.",""],[1,"259","3","Youth Agropreneur Development and Training Programme","Promoting training and youth agropreneur development through collaboration across agencies and the private sector to modernise farming techniques and nurture agribusiness start-ups;",""],[1,"259","4","Extension Services Streamlining and Advisory Support","Strategy C3: Strengthening institutional support and extension services by streamlining extension services and encouraging advisory services from industry and academia;",""],[1,"260","1","Agricultural Research and Development Programme","Focus will be given to R&D&C, particularly in the development of quality seeds, breeds, fries and animal feeds, integrated pest and disease management, as well as product improvement and development of green products.",""],[1,"260","1","Climate-Resilient Agricultural Research","In addition, research will also focus on addressing climate change issues to ensure crops, livestock, and fisheries are climate resilient.",""],[1,"260","1","Agricultural Research Collaboration and Coordination Mechanism","Collaboration in agricultural research will be spearheaded by a research management agency (RMA) with support from existing agricultural research agencies, such as the Malaysian Agricultural Research and Development Institute (MARDI), Malaysian Palm Oil Board (MPOB), Malaysian Rubber Board (LGM), universities, and private research centres.",""],[1,"260","1","Participatory and Market-Driven Agricultural Research System","This is to ensure that the research is participatory and market-driven to promote the uptake of solutions among industries and farmers.",""],[1,"260","2","Agricultural and Entrepreneurship Skills Upgrading Programme","Focus will be given to enhancing the agricultural and entrepreneurship skills of farmers to modernise the sector.",""],[1,"260","2","Agricultural Training Curriculum Review Mechanism","The National Agricultural Training Council (NATC) and Institute of Malaysian Plantation and Commodities (IMPAC) will collaborate with higher learning institutions and industry players to continuously review existing training curriculums to meet industry demand.",""],[1,"260","2","Farmer, Fishermen, and Smallholder Upskilling Programme","The current skill sets of farmers, fishermen, and smallholders will be assessed and upskilling programmes introduced to assist them in adopting modern technologies and good agricultural practices.",""],[1,"260","3","Entrepreneurship Development Programmes for Agropreneurs","Entrepreneurship development programmes will be improved through collaboration among the NATC, IMPAC, Malaysian Global Innovation & Creativity Centre (MaGIC), and National Institute of Entrepreneurship (INSKEN) to assist and nurture more start-ups, particularly by young agropreneurs, into successful and sustainable agribusinesses.",""],[1,"260","3","Optimization of Agricultural Training Institute Facilities for Entrepreneurial Courses","Existing facilities in agricultural training institutes will be optimised to undertake entrepreneurial courses.",""],[1,"260","3","Young Agropreneurs Programme Promotion and Start-up Support","the young agropreneurs programmme, a collaborative effort between Agrobank, universities, and agricultural training institutes, will be further promoted to attract undergraduates into agribusinesses.",""],[1,"260","4","Agricultural Extension Services Streamlining and One-Stop Advisory System","Extension services provided by various agencies will be reviewed and streamlined based on location, agricultural activities, and relevance of services provided.",""]],"151":[[1,"248","16","Agricultural Cooperative and Association Capacity Building","Building capacity of agricultural cooperatives and associations along the supply chain",""],[1,"259","5","Agricultural Cooperative Capacity Building and Supply Chain Integration","Building capacity of agricultural cooperatives and associations along the supply chain by vertically integrating the supply chain for selected crops, enhancing management skills, and pooling resources for promotion and exports;",""],[1,"259","6","Market Access and Logistics Support Strengthening","Strategy C5: Improving market access and logistics support by strengthening logistics and enhancing access to domestic and international marketplaces;",""],[1,"260","5","Cluster-Based Agro-Food and Industrial Commodity Development","A cluster-based approach that vertically integrates production, quality control, processing, and marketing will be promoted to encourage participation of cooperatives and associations in agro-food and industrial commodities along the supply chain.",""],[1,"260","6","Cooperative and Association Capacity Strengthening Programme","the capacity of cooperatives and associations including fishermen associations in the area of management, finance, investment, and marketing will be strengthened to enable them to undertake new business ventures along the supply chain",""],[1,"260","6","Deep-Sea Vessel Purchase Incentive Scheme","Fishermen associations will be incentivised to assist members in purchasing deep-sea vessels equipped with modern technologies through special schemes",""],[1,"260","6","Smallholder Cooperative Establishment Support","assistance will be provided to smallholders in the establishment of new cooperatives",""],[1,"261","1","Young Agropreneurs Placement in Cooperatives","cooperatives will be enhanced with the placement of young agropreneurs programme participants to infuse entrepreneurship and dynamism.",""],[1,"261","1","Cooperative Market Access and Promotion Support","cooperatives and associations will be encouraged to pool their collective resources and participate in various local and international events to showcase their products and secure contracts.",""],[1,"261","1","Cooperative Product Testing and Marketing Grants and Loans","Assistance in the form of matching grants and soft loans will be provided for product testing, packaging, and promotional activities at cooperative or association-level.",""],[1,"261","2","Agricultural Product Marketing Improvement Programme","Marketing of agricultural products will be improved by linking producers to commercial outlets, establishing more market outlets and increasing market-compliant products.",""],[1,"261","2","Online Agricultural Marketing and Branding Initiative","Online marketing, promotion, and branding will also help stimulate product sales.",""],[1,"261","2","Review of FAMA Contract Farming Marketing Role","Direct involvement of the Federal Agricultural Marketing Authority (FAMA) in the marketing of agricultural produce through contract farming arrangements will be reviewed.","Federal Agricultural Marketing Authority (FAMA)"],[1,"261","2","International Promotion of Agricultural Exports","MATRADE will intensify the promotion of agricultural products in relevant international markets through trade and food exhibitions with the collaboration of agriculture attachés under the Ministry of Agriculture and Agro-Based Industry.","MATRADE | Ministry of Agriculture and Agro-Based Industry"],[1,"261","2","Overseas Promotion of Industrial Commodities","Similarly, promotion for industrial commodities including palm oil, rubber, timber, and timber products will be intensified through the efforts of overseas offices of the MPOB, Malaysian Palm Oil Council, Malaysian Rubber Export Promotion Council and Malaysian Timber Council, under the Ministry of Plantation Industries and Commodities.","MPOB | Malaysian Palm Oil Council | Malaysian Rubber Export Promotion Council | Malaysian Timber Council | Ministry of Plantation Industries and Commodities"],[1,"261","2","Agricultural and Fishery Logistics Support Improvement","The logistics support for collection, distribution and marketing of agricultural produce as well as fishery products will be improved to ensure quality, minimise post-harvest loss, and reduce marketing cost.",""],[1,"261","2","Collection and Distribution Centre Expansion","Additional collection and distribution centres will be established in new and existing production areas, while cold storage and handling facilities will be provided and upgraded in fishery complexes, ports, and airports based on demand to facilitate the export of perishable products.",""],[1,"261","2","Halal and Green Logistics Promotion","The use of halal and green logistics will be emphasised to increase the marketability of agricultural exports.",""]],"152":[[1,"248","19","Performance-Based Incentive and Certification Programmes","Intensifying performance-based incentive and certification programmes",""],[1,"259","7","Agricultural Financing Restructuring and Flexible Payment Mechanism","Scaling up access to agricultural financing by restructuring and providing a more flexible payment mechanism",""],[1,"259","7","Sustainable Financing for Replanting Programmes","increasing sustainability of financing mechanisms for replanting programmes",""],[1,"259","8","Performance-Based Farm Certification and Incentive Programme","Intensifying performance-based incentive and certification programmes by encouraging farmers to get certified, and prioritising certified farms for incentives and support.",""],[1,"261","3","Agrobank Flexible Repayment Financing Reform","Government funding through Agrobank will be restructured from fixed- term financing to flexible repayment based on harvest cycles of agro-food",""],[1,"261","4","Flexible Agro-Food Commodity Loan Repayment and Credit Insurance Scheme","The current practice of loan repayment for paddy based on harvesting cycles will be extended to other agro-food commodities, such as aquaculture and vegetables.",""],[1,"261","5","Replanting Cess Extension and Soft Loan Financing Scheme","The suitability of the current mechanism in financing the replanting of rubber through the collection of cess will be explored for extension to oil palm, cocoa, and pepper.",""],[1,"261","6","Performance-Based Agricultural Incentives","Existing input-driven subsidies will be gradually replaced with performance-based incentives to ensure productivity-led assistance.",""],[1,"261","6","Agricultural Certification Compliance Incentives","Incentives will be provided to encourage compliance of farmers and smallholders to the Malaysian Good Agricultural Practices (MyGAP) certification and other certifications such as the Malaysian Sustainable Palm Oil (MSPO), a sustainable palm oil certification scheme.",""],[1,"261","7","Certified Farm Grant and Soft Loan Support","Certified farms will be given priority for grants or soft loans.",""],[1,"261","7","MyGAP Certification Streamlining","the MyGAP certification will be streamlined according to the Global GAP requirements to increase market access, particularly to the European Union.",""],[1,"261","7","MyGAP Consumer Promotion Campaigns","The benefits of MyGAP certified products will be promoted to consumers through campaigns and awareness programmes.",""],[1,"261","7","Industrial Commodity Quality Certification","For industrial commodities, quality certification of products such as palm oil, cocoa and pepper, and sustainable forest management certification for forest plantation will be encouraged.",""],[1,"261","7","MSPO Promotion for Plantations and Smallholdings","the MSPO will be promoted among plantations and smallholdings to ensure palm oil from Malaysia complies with sustainable practices to enable them gain better market access.",""],[1,"261","7","Malaysian Timber Certification Scheme Promotion","the Malaysian Timber Certification Scheme, an internationally recognised national timber certification scheme, will also be promoted.",""]],"153":[[1,"262","3","SME and Bumiputera Contractor Capacity Building","accelerating capacity and capability building of SMEs and Bumiputera contractors",""],[1,"262","3","Human Capital Quality Improvement Initiative","increasing human capital quality",""],[1,"262","3","Labour Market Matching Improvement","reducing the mismatch between labour demand and supply",""],[1,"262","7","Construction Industry Training Module Collaboration","Key initiatives include fostering greater collaboration between Construction Industry Development Board (CIDB), the respective professional boards, and training institutions to develop industry-relevant training modules.",""],[1,"262","7","Skilled Trade Apprenticeship Programme","A structured skilled trade apprenticeship programme for specific courses such as safety supervisors, crane operators, and rotary drill operators will also be introduced to produce a highly skilled workforce.",""],[1,"262","7","Construction SME Capability Enhancement and Productivity Centre of Excellence","SME capabilities will be enhanced, particularly Bumiputera contractors, with the support of key partners and the establishment of productivity CoE for sharing of best practices.",""],[1,"262","7","Construction Manpower Planning System","Regular manpower planning will be undertaken to reduce the mismatch between labour demand and supply.",""],[1,"262","7","Skilled Foreign Labour Entry and Levy Reform","The proportion of skilled foreign labour will be increased by streamlining entry requirements and introducing a new levy system.",""]],"154":[[1,"262","6","Firm Internationalisation and Export Capacity Support","Increasing internationalisation by building capacity and scale of firms to export and addressing issues through negotiations at government-to-government level as well as utilising the Services Export Fund.",""],[1,"263","3","SME Partnership and Consortium Support for International Projects","The strategies to increase the internationalisation of firms will focus on building capability and scale of firms by encouraging high- performing SMEs to forge partnerships with larger corporations or form multidisciplinary consortia when bidding for international projects.",""],[1,"263","3","Public Procurement Review for Consortium Formation","The public procurement policy will be reviewed to facilitate the formation of such consortia.",""],[1,"263","3","FTA and MRA Utilisation Support for Firms","In addition, firms will be encouraged to leverage FTAs and MRAs, and provide feedback to the Government on challenges faced when venturing abroad to enable issues to be addressed at government-to-government level.",""],[1,"263","3","Strategic Export Facilitation for Construction Firms","The SEF, which covers activities such as tendering, negotiating, and conducting feasibility studies for international projects as well as export promotion activities, will assist construction firms to secure opportunities abroad.",""]],"155":[[1,"267","9","Higher Order Thinking Skills Promotion Strategy","Strategy F7: Promoting higher order thinking skills to develop a dynamic society by scaling up existing programmes such as i-Think and Genovasi, prioritising science and mathematics in education, and expanding career opportunities in science and technology.",""],[1,"268","3","Scale-up of HOTS Programmes","Existing HOTS programmes, including i-Think and Genovasi, will be scaled-up to inculcate the current and future workforce with critical thinking, communications, and leadership skills.",""],[1,"268","3","Priority for Science and Mathematics Education","science and mathematics in education will also be given priority in line with the Malaysia Education Blueprint, 2013-2025",""],[1,"268","3","Expansion of Science and Technology Career Opportunities","Career opportunities in science and technology will be expanded with the Government's emphasis on knowledge-intensive and high value-added industries.",""],[1,"270","3","Talent and Skills Development Initiative","Strategy G2: Strengthening corridors to fuel regional development through a strategic review of corridor development master plans, accelerate investment in regional economic corridors, improve infrastructure, as well as enhance talent and skill development.",""]],"156":[[1,"270","1","Urban and Regional Economic Corridor Investment","Malaysia will invest in developing cities and regional economic corridors that are essential for growth, to maximise impact for local communities, and stimulate broader national development.",""],[1,"270","2","City Competitiveness Master Plans for Four Major Cities","Strategy G1: Developing city competitiveness master plans for four major cities, namely Kuala Lumpur, Johor Bahru, Kuching, and Kota Kinabalu3, along the principles of creating density, expanding transit- oriented development (TOD), strengthening knowledge-based clusters, enhancing liveability, encouraging green-based development and practices, as well as ensuring inclusivity;",""],[1,"270","5","City-Specific Competitiveness Plans","Based on the findings from this study, city-specific competitiveness plans will be developed for four selected cities in the Eleventh Malaysia Plan.",""],[1,"271","1","Four-City Urban Transformation Programme","By 2020, four major cities in Malaysia will have undergone a step- change in their economic growth, importance as talent hubs, and liveability.",""],[1,"271","2","City Competitiveness Master Plans","City Competitiveness Master Plans will be developed for the four major cities as a start, based on key principles that increase liveability and stimulate economic growth.",""],[1,"272","3","City Competitiveness Planning Framework","Specific city competitiveness plans will be drawn up, taking into account the competitive advantages of each city.",""],[1,"272","5","Revision of Malaysian City Planning Guidelines","Existing Malaysian city planning guidelines will be revised progressively to optimise the built environment, enhance connectivity, and integrate infrastructure development.",""],[1,"273","1","Development of Knowledge-Based Clusters","Knowledge-based clusters will be developed to attract investment and talent.",""],[1,"273","2","Urban Planning and Land Use Zoning Improvement","Better city planning mechanisms will be developed, including land use zoning that promotes residential, commercial, and basic social amenities in close proximity to increase walkability.",""],[1,"273","2","Sports, Arts, and Cultural Facilities Promotion","Sports, arts, and cultural facilities will be promoted through greater collaboration between related associations, corporate bodies, and NGOs.",""],[1,"273","2","Public Transport and Urban Services Upgrading","Emphasis will also be given to the quality, capacity, and reliability of public transport, social amenities, and telecommunications networks.",""],[1,"273","2","Local Healthcare and School Facility Development","Healthcare facilities and high-quality schools will be planned for and developed accordingly to meet local demand.",""],[1,"273","2","Urban Cultural and Commercial Attraction Development","Vibrant cultural attractions, food and beverage and retail spaces will be developed to create cities that are attractive to global talent.",""],[1,"273","4","Urban Inclusiveness and Social Connectedness Initiative","Inclusiveness will be one of the main thrusts for the four cities, to ensure that communities have ample opportunities to participate in social, political, and economic activities.",""],[1,"273","4","Urban Homelessness and Poverty Reduction Collaboration","Focus will also be given to address issues related to homelessness and poverty in cities through collaboration among relevant agencies, corporate bodies, NGOs, and local governments.",""],[1,"273","4","Urban Connectivity Improvement","In addition, good connectivity will be a priority to enable the spillovers of economic gains from these cities to the hinterland and suburban areas.",""]],"157":[[1,"271","11","Transit-Oriented Development Initiative","Transit-oriented development to increase use of public transportation and reduce reliance on personal vehicles",""],[1,"272","6","Transit-Oriented Development Adoption","City authorities will adopt TOD as part of the city's competitiveness master plan to provide mobility options to residents, add vibrancy to city spaces, reduce pollution and energy consumption by reducing commute times and increasing the use of public transport or walking, and also revitalise brownfield areas within the city.",""],[1,"273","3","Green City Development Integration","All these cities will place high importance on continuous sustainable growth by enhancing green-based development and optimising low carbon resources.",""],[1,"273","3","Green Buildings and Sustainable Consumption Measures","Environment-friendly practices, such as green buildings, green lifestyles, and sustainable consumption and production, will be embedded within the development plans of these cities.",""],[1,"338","18","Green Building Index Adoption for Construction","Adoption of Green Building Index for construction",""]],"158":[[1,"300","4","Local Economic Development Collaboration Strategy","Strategy E3: Strengthening collaboration for stimulating local economic development by engaging the private sector and improving infrastructure and the business environment;",""],[1,"301","7","Local Economic Development Collaboration","Local authorities and the private sector will collaborate closely together to develop potential economic activities.",""],[1,"301","9","Local Economic Development and Informal Business Relocation Programme","Local authorities will develop the local economy, by providing a conducive environment including better infrastructure and commercial facilities.",""]],"159":[[1,"300","5","Local Authority Public Engagement and Data Sharing Initiative","Strategy E4: Intensifying public engagement and data sharing by local authorities, leveraging new technologies for greater feedback and dissemination of information.",""],[1,"300","9","Community Expectations Survey for Local Authority Performance KPIs","An independent survey will be conducted by the Local Government Department (JKT) to understand community expectations, which will be translated into KPIs to measure the performance of local authorities.","Local Government Department (JKT)"],[1,"300","9","Public Communication Channels for Local Authority KPIs","In addition, various communication channels will be deployed to inform the community of the KPIs to enable better understanding and encourage their active participation.",""],[1,"302","1","Local Authority Public Engagement and Data Sharing Initiative","Strategy E4 Intensifying public engagement and data sharing by local authorities Widening engagement with community and non- governmental organisations",""],[1,"302","2","Expanded Community and NGO Engagement for Local Authorities","Engagement with the community and NGOs will be widened to gain feedback on existing and proposed services by local authorities.",""],[1,"302","2","Multi-Channel Digital and Conventional Citizen Feedback Platform","Conventional and digital platforms will be utilised to provide multiple channels for greater community engagement.",""],[1,"302","2","Residents Representative Committee Support for Wellbeing Issues","The Residents Representative Committee will assist the local authorities in dealing with wellbeing issues.",""]],"160":[[1,"301","2","Multi-Level Coordination for Public Sector Development Projects","Collaboration between local authorities, federal and state governments, and the private sector will be strengthened to ensure that public sector development projects are in accordance with the requirements of the local community and national interests.",""],[1,"301","2","Urban Liveability and Public Services Improvement","Focus will be given to ensure an attractive and vibrant living environment, efficient public transport, quality and affordable housing, as well as efficient public utility services.",""],[1,"302","4","Stricter Environmental and Social Impact Assessment Compliance Enforcement","Local authorities will ensure stricter compliance to the requirements of the Environmental Impact Assessment (EIA) and Social Impact Assessment (SIA) for relevant projects.",""],[1,"302","6","Local Authority Planning Data Collection System","The JKT will introduce a system to enable local authorities to collect data that is required for planning and decision-making.",""]],"161":[[1,"338","15","Peatland Fire Prevention Infrastructure","Construction of 137 check dams, 40 water tube wells and three watch towers in hot spot areas to address peatland fires",""],[1,"339","12","Hazard Map Development for Flood-Prone Areas","Development of 34 hazard maps to facilitate disaster prevention and development planning in major flood-prone areas",""]]}});